topic(["islam","general","d-av-sonstiges-islam-2","c-kannibalismus-verbot"],{"title":"Kannibalismus verbot","k":"Averroes","blurb":"1 post","article":{"claim":"Kannibalismus verbot","tree":{"they":"Kannibalismus verbot","we":"Sunan Abi Dawud 3207 Narrated Aisha, Ummul Mu'minin: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Breaking a dead man's bone is like breaking it when he is alive.","more":{"h":"Sunan Abi Dawud 3207","p":["Sunan Abi Dawud 3207","Narrated Aisha, Ummul Mu'minin:","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Breaking a dead man's bone is like breaking it when he is alive.","Sahi","----------------------------------","Sunan Ibn Majah 1616","It was narrated from ‘Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:","“Breaking the bones of the deceased is like breaking his bones when he is alive.”","Hassan","https://fiqh.islamonline.net/en/cannibalism-islamic-view/\nCannibalism: Islamic View - Fiqh\nCannibalism: Islamic View - Fiqh\nDear scholars, As-Salamu `alaykum. A British newspaper reported that on Thursday, 2 January 2003, Britain's Channel 4 television is to show a Chinese artist eating the flesh of a dead baby. He claims that no religion or law forbids cannibalism. What is the Islamic stance on this issue? Jazakum Allah khayran."],"credit":"Averroes · sonstiges islam 2 › #kannibalismus-verbot","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1275832106949283962/1286151241768108125"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Averroes (sonstiges islam 2 › #kannibalismus-verbot)."}});
