topic(["christianity","church","d-av-kirchenva-ter-recherche","c-hadithe-webseite"],{"title":"Hadithe webseite","k":"Averroes","blurb":"1 post","article":{"claim":"Hadithe webseite","tree":{"they":"Hadithe webseite","we":"Https://islamsyria.com/ رابطة العلماء السوريين رابطة العلماء السوريين يجيب على الفتاوى متخصصون في مختلف العلوم الفقهية https://ketabonline.com/ar جامع الكتب الإسلامية جامع الكتب الإسلامية ابحث في أكبر مكتبة تحتوي على آلا…","more":{"h":"https://islamsyria.com/","p":["https://islamsyria.com/\nرابطة العلماء السوريين\nرابطة العلماء السوريين\nيجيب على الفتاوى متخصصون في مختلف العلوم الفقهية","https://ketabonline.com/ar\nجامع الكتب الإسلامية\nجامع الكتب الإسلامية\nابحث في أكبر مكتبة تحتوي على آلاف الكتب المجانية","https://app.turath.io/\nتراث\nتراث\nلتحميل وقراءة الكتب الإسلامية","https://en.tohed.com/hadith/musnad-ahmad/24864/\nMusnad Ahmad 24864 — Supplement to the Musnad of ‘A’ishah (ma...\nMusnad Ahmad 24864 — Supplement to the Musnad of ‘A’ishah (ma...\nMusnad Ahmad 24864 - Narrated from Hazrat Aisha that whenever the Prophet (peace be upon him) mentioned Hazrat Khadijah, he would praise her greatly. One day, I","dr halid al hayyik https://www.addyaiya.com/content.php?page-id=485&v=01f7743c\nالموقع الرسمي للشيخ الدكتور خالد الح...\nالموقع الرسمي للشيخ الدكتور خالد الح...\nالموقع الرسمي للشيخ الدكتور خالد الحايك","https://hdith.com/encyclopedia/s\nالبحث في الموسوعة الحديثية\nالبحث في الموسوعة الحديثية\nابحث في أحاديث السنة، تراجم الرواة، كتب الحديث، والمواضع.","https://alkulify.blogspot.com/\nمدونة أبي جعفر عبد الله بن فهد الخليفي\nمدونة أبي جعفر عبد الله بن فهد الخليفي"],"credit":"Averroes · Kirchenväter recherche › #hadithe-webseite","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1275832106949283962/1379877660121104506"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Averroes (Kirchenväter recherche › #hadithe-webseite)."}});
topic(["islam","general","d-dr-muslim-questions"],{"title":"Muslim questions","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"6 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Muslim questions","tree":{"they":"Muslim questions","we":"@Dawud as salamu alaykem , if someone gifts you a lottery ticket, and you redeem it, is it still considered gambling","more":{"h":"Muslim questions","p":["@Dawud as salamu alaykem , if someone gifts you a lottery ticket, and you redeem it, is it still considered gambling"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #muslim-questions","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1354163509142884684"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Wa alaykumus salaam It is not considered gambling but the prize is still Haram.","more":{"h":"Wa alaykumus salaam It is not considered gambling but the prize is still Haram.","p":["Wa alaykumus salaam It is not considered gambling but the prize is still Haram.\nif you don’t mind me asking, why would the price be considered haram if its source isn’t from gambling"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #muslim-questions","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1354163509142884684"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"If you don’t mind me asking, why would the price be considered haram if its source isn’t from gambling did bro win the lottery?","more":{"h":"if you don’t mind me asking, why would the price be considered haram if its source isn’t from gambling","p":["if you don’t mind me asking, why would the price be considered haram if its source isn’t from gambling\ndid bro win the lottery?"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #muslim-questions","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1354163509142884684"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Did bro win the lottery? no","more":{"h":"did bro win the lottery?","p":["did bro win the lottery?\nno"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #muslim-questions","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1354163509142884684"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Not at all. In short, because the prize money carries the khubth/filth of the sin (meaning it was 100% acquired through unlawful means), the wealth is considered Haram and filthy.","more":{"h":"Muslim questions","p":["Not at all. In short, because the prize money carries the khubth/filth of the sin (meaning it was 100% acquired through unlawful means), the wealth is considered Haram and filthy. This is separate from a person gambling and winning. Then he has the sin of gambling and the Haram wealth. It would be like Person A steals wealth then gifts it to Person B (knowingly). The wealth is Haram for person B even though he didn't steal it.\nunderstood, what makes the money filthy, though? how is it acquired through unlawful means?","is it because the money is generated from buying the lotto tickets, which itself is a participation in gambling"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #muslim-questions","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1354163509142884684"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Is it because the money is generated from buying the lotto tickets, which itself is a participation in gambling Exactly There's basically three separate things to consider here: the sin involved in acquiring the wealth, …","more":{"h":"Muslim questions","p":["is it because the money is generated from buying the lotto tickets, which itself is a participation in gambling\nExactly","There's basically three separate things to consider here: the sin involved in acquiring the wealth, whether you actually have legal ownership of it and then whether the wealth itself is permissible to use or still carries some khubth (unlawful taint) because of how it was acquired."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #muslim-questions","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1354163509142884684"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#muslim-questions)."}});
topic(["islam","general","d-dr-non-muslim-questions"],{"title":"Non muslim questions","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Non muslim questions","tree":{"they":"Non muslim questions","we":"Not all heroes wear capes May Allah reward you bro just cuz someone concedes doesnt make your argument valid i mean im aware there are ppl who formulate it the way youre making but personally I'd rather avoid tht debate …","more":{"h":"Not all heroes wear capes","p":["Not all heroes wear capes","May Allah reward you","bro just cuz someone concedes doesnt make your argument valid","i mean im aware there are ppl who formulate it the way youre making but personally I'd rather avoid tht debate","Like for theism we dont have any positive reason to believe \"oh my faculties are inaccurate under creationism\". But in evolution its literally positively driven by selection for survival and thus there is an active defeater for genuine access. The asymmetry isnt based on possibility alone.\nkakarots problem","@Delman","here"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #non-muslim-questions","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1330737183010721824"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Bro just cuz someone concedes doesnt make your argument valid Sorry man, I don't understand this point.","more":{"h":"bro just cuz someone concedes doesnt make your argument valid","p":["bro just cuz someone concedes doesnt make your argument valid\nSorry man, I don't understand this point. We're just talking about agreeing on a premise/axiom, not the validity of the argument or whether the premises follows. So i don't see how this relevant","i mean im aware there are ppl who formulate it the way youre making but personally I'd rather avoid tht debate\nYeah that's fine, everyone has their own way and this can be quite complicated, but the whole point of this argument, is you need a theory or framework in which your existence is likely, since right now it's extremely unlucky with all the possibilities, it's 0","and since theism has one in where every possible person is created then it follows that under bayesian reasoning, theism is infinitely or incredibly likely for god to exist since athiesm has no framwork in which your existence is likely (if you reject the notion that all possible worlds actually exist) so in otherwords, the whole point is theism at least has some framework to make your existence '1'. That's all you need your guy to concede which is pretty easy"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #non-muslim-questions","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1330737183010721824"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#non-muslim-questions)."}});
topic(["islam","general","d-dr-tafsir-stuff"],{"title":"Tafsir stuff","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"6 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Tafsir stuff","tree":{"they":"Tafsir stuff","we":"Https://x.com/i/status/2026877820299866192 @winnie4prez @wheresurhayabro Imam ibn Ashur (may Allah have mercy on him) answered this in his tafsīr, he said: \"And the repetition of the name al-Raḥmān in this passage four t…","more":{"h":"https://x.com/i/status/2026877820299866192","p":["https://x.com/i/status/2026877820299866192\n@winnie4prez @wheresurhayabro Imam ibn Ashur (may Allah have mercy on him) answered this in his tafsīr, he said:","\"And the repetition of the name al-Raḥmān in this passage four times alludes to the fact that the attribute al-Raḥmān, firmly established for God, whose true reality the polytheists","1/?","https://x.com/i/status/2026887619385372720\n@winnie4prez @wheresurhayabro @abduallah_amin All of Surah Maryam is aimed very prominently at Christians and Allah only refers to himself as Al-Rahman throughout. One possible reason is that was the prevalent name of Allah used by Arab Christians. Another is it highlights that Allah being merciful doesn't require a son ...","https://x.com/Kashmiri_Fire/status/2046077737618530355?s=20\nFakhr al-Din al-Razi citing the two scholarly views on the namesake of \"Yaḥyā\" being unique - Quran 19:7"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #tafsir-stuff","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1456253843439620190"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Early Tafsir: Abu Ubaydah al-Muthanna al-Tamimi: (d.","more":{"h":"Early Tafsir:","p":["Early Tafsir:","Abu Ubaydah al-Muthanna al-Tamimi: (d. 824)\nhttps://shamela.ws/book/23630/743","Hud ibn Muhakkam al-Hawwari: (d. 850-903)\nhttps://mega.nz/folder/bNpB3IJS#xrzQxq-xr3Gp-DzlCZBR-g","Yahya bin Salam: (d. 815) (Hawwari's tafsir is said to be based upon Yahya bin Salam's tafsir, which only exists partially. B=\nhttps://shamela.ws/book/12851 - partial version (older edition)\nBut there was a recent find iirc: https://x.com/mkry11/status/2033983957130269164","Al Farrah the Grammarian (d. 822)\nhttps://shamela.ws/book/23634","Al-Zajjaj (d. 923)\nhttps://shamela.ws/book/922","Tahreer wat Tanweer - Ibn Ashur\nhttps://shamela.ws/book/9776 \n \nhttps://shamela.ws/book/22371 - Another linguistic tafsir from grammarian (Al-Akhfash al-Awsat died in 215AH) and was specialized in bedouin poetry","https://app.turath.io/book/12810 - Tafsir Mujahid","https://app.turath.io/book/2229 - Tafsir Sufyan bin Uyaynah","https://books.rafed.net/view/4523/page/246?search=%20السماء - Sharif al Radi's Majazat al Quran:","https://shamela.ws/book/3259 - Ibn Qutabayh's Gharibat al Quran:","https://mega.nz/folder/qMpxXaYa#EIWtuRtgoT5piQo5WmTOAA Tafsir of Hakim al-Jashmi al-mutazili","https://quran-tafsir.net/maturidy/sura7-aya172.html al-Maturidi's tafsir\nتفسير يحيى بن سلّام التيمي البصري القيرواني (ت 200هـ)،\nتحقيق هند شلبي، تونس، 2مج\nقال الناشر:\nصدر بفضل الله تعالى ما بقي من تفسير يحيى بن سلام مما لم يصدر من قبل، من سورة البقرة إلى سورة الحجر، ومن...\nFile folder on MEGA\nFile folder on MEGA"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #tafsir-stuff","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1456253843439620190"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Https://blog.fussilat.com/the-authority-of-ibn-abbas-and-other-companions-in-tafsir/ The Authority of Ibn Abbas and Other Companions in Tafsir The Authority of Ibn Abbas and Other Companions in Tafsir https://blog.fussil…","more":{"h":"https://blog.fussilat.com/the-authority-of-ibn-abbas-and-other-companions-in-tafsir/","p":["https://blog.fussilat.com/the-authority-of-ibn-abbas-and-other-companions-in-tafsir/\nThe Authority of Ibn Abbas and Other Companions in Tafsir\nThe Authority of Ibn Abbas and Other Companions in Tafsir","https://blog.fussilat.com/consensus-in-tafsir-and-its-authority/#2-definition-of-consensus-in-usul-al-fiqh\nConsensus in Tafsir and Its Authority\nConsensus in Tafsir and Its Authority","Helped get these realized"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #tafsir-stuff","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1456253843439620190"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Https://archive.org/details/sabuni_infallibility_of_prophets/page/n9/mode/2up Muhammad Ali Al Sabuni Infallibility Of The Prophets Muhammad Ali Al Sabuni Infallibility Of The Prophets Muhammad Ali al-Sabuni - Infallibili…","more":{"h":"https://archive.org/details/sabuniinfallibilityofprophets/page/n9/mode/2up","p":["https://archive.org/details/sabuni_infallibility_of_prophets/page/n9/mode/2up\nMuhammad Ali Al Sabuni Infallibility Of The Prophets\nMuhammad Ali Al Sabuni Infallibility Of The Prophets\nMuhammad Ali al-Sabuni - Infallibility of the Prophets"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #tafsir-stuff","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1456253843439620190"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Book so good he had to share it thrice!","more":{"h":"book so good he had to share it thrice!","p":["book so good he had to share it thrice!"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #tafsir-stuff","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1456253843439620190"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Https://ibrahimsreflections.com/posts/alternative-reading-of-surah-al-tin/ An Alternative Reading of Sūrah al-Tīn An Alternative Reading of Sūrah al-Tīn “By the fig and the olive, and [by] Mount Sinai, and [by] this secu…","more":{"h":"https://ibrahimsreflections.com/posts/alternative-reading-of-surah-al-tin/","p":["https://ibrahimsreflections.com/posts/alternative-reading-of-surah-al-tin/\nAn Alternative Reading of Sūrah al-Tīn\nAn Alternative Reading of Sūrah al-Tīn\n“By the fig and the olive, and [by] Mount Sinai, and [by] this secure city.” (95:1-3)\nSūrah al-Tīn is commonly read as a sūrah about the human body and its old age. However, its actual subject is revelation: where it came down, how Allāh ﷻ made the human being to receive it, what becomes of the one who accepts it and the one who reject..."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #tafsir-stuff","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1456253843439620190"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#tafsir-stuff)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-hadith-general-inquiry-and-news"],{"title":"Hadith general inquiry and news","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Hadith general inquiry and news","tree":{"they":"How likely is it that one chain got it from the other and made a mistake?","we":"How likely is it that they all made a similar mistake?","more":{"h":"How likely is it that one chain got it from the other and made a mistake?","p":["How likely is it that they all made a similar mistake?\nExample 1: A hadith of Abu Hurairah (RA), \"The Muslim with the completest iman is the one with the best manners.\" (see picture for chains)","How likely is it that one chain got it from the other? Not likely because 1) The narrators were reasonably reliable, and 2) Not that far apart in time such that we can say one is very late and likely to have taken it from the earlier one.","Example 2: A hadith of Anas (RA), \"Seeking knowledge is obligatory on every Muslim.\"","This hadith has many weak chains to Anas ibn Malik.","Tarif (weak) > Anas\nZiyad (weak) > Anas.","“A man from Syria” > Qatadah > Anas. Qatadah was a prolific teacher with many students. No one else narrated this from him.","Hafs (matruk) > Kathir > Ibn Sirin > Anas.","Each of these chains could have easily derived from the others. Tarif could have gotten it from Ziyad. The rest could have mistakenly given other chains to the hadith of Ziyad. We have no reason to believe otherwise since they were all weak!","Imam Ahmad said, “This is a fabricated hadith.”","A hadith deemed Sahih or Hasan because of corroboration rather than because of itself is termed Sahih li-Ghayrihi or Hasan li-Ghayrihi.","Many later scholars were more lenient with corroboration because they took it as a strict additive rule (weak + weak = hasan, or hasan + hasan = sahih) instead of thinking critically whether the chains truly raises confidence in the authenticity of the hadith.","A true master of hadith must acknowledge the possibility of narrators getting the hadith from each other, especially when the narrators are weak and could have easily forgotten or fabricated the chain. A chain is only as useful as the narrator who claims it.","The following is an example of reliable narrators with a mursal hadith (i.e. they didn't mention their sources), but the same principle applies to weak narrators when they claim chains:","There is a hadith that the Prophet (SAW) told a group of companions to redo wudhu when they laughed in prayer. At least 4 tabi'oon narrated it (mursal) from the Prophet (SAW).","A naive person would think the hadith must have some basis because of the number of people who narrated it.","Ali ibn al-Madini (Bukhari's teacher) said:","Ibn Mahdi said to me: ‘All of its narrations ultimately revolve around Abu al-Aliyah.’","I said to him, ‘But al-Hasan narrates it from the Prophet ﷺ in mursal form.’","He replied, ‘Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Hafs ibn Sulayman, who said: “I was the one who narrated it to al-Hasan, from Hafsah, from Abu al-Aliyah.”’","I said to him, ‘But Ibrahim also narrates it from the Prophet ﷺ in mursal form.’","He said, ‘Sharik narrated to us from Abu Hashim, who said: “I was the one who narrated it to Ibrahim, from Abu al-Aliyah.”’","I said to him, ‘But al-Zuhri also narrates it from the Prophet ﷺ in mursal form.’","ʿAbd al-Rahman replied, ‘I read this hadith in the book of al-Zuhri’s nephew, narrated from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Hasan.’","The generations of narrators","Older Companions E.g. Ibn Masud (RA)\nYounger Companions E.g. Ibn Umar, Abu Hurairah, Aisha, Anas (RA), etc.\nStudents of Companions: Often close students or relatives of companions.\nE.g. Urwah from his aunt Aisha, Ibrahim from his uncles Alqamah and Aswad from Ibn Masud, Salim from his father Ibn Umar","First Regional Collector Era: Regional Collectors learned from many sources in their cities.\nE.g. Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri learned from Urwah, Salim, and others in Madinah.","E.g. Qatadah in Basra, A'mash in Kufa, etc.","Many scholars who were not regional collectors but specialists as well. E.g. Hisham ibn Urwah from his father Urwah.","Second Regional Collector Era: A second generation of regional collectors who collected from their regions and learned from the first regional collectors.\nE.g. Malik (wrote Muwatta) and Ibn Ishaq (wrote Seerah) in Madinah, Ma'mar (wrote Jami') who learned from Hijaz, Yemen, and Iraq (but was weak in Iraq), Shu'bah in Basrah, Sufyan al-Thawri in Kufa, Ibn Uyainah in Makkah, etc.","Malik, Mamar, and Ibn Uyainah were major students of Zuhri as well."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #hadith-general-inquiry-and-news","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1458934120817098838"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#hadith-general-inquiry-and-news)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-hell-is-mostly-women"],{"title":"Hell is mostly women","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Hell is mostly women","tree":{"they":"Hell is mostly women","we":"The hadith reads: Here, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ gives a statistic of the people of hell, that most of them are women.","more":{"h":"The hadith reads:","p":["The hadith reads:","Here, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ gives a statistic of the people of hell, that most of them are women. He ﷺ then goes on to explain why women are the majority in hell; they were ungrateful for the good done to them, and overlooked much good due to a single case of wrong. It is these qualities that took such women into hell; they did not go to hell simply for being women.","Critics also bring and misinterpret another hadith:","However, al-Munawi commented on this hadith:","We see that this doesn’t suggest women will always be the minority in paradise, but instead, after the Muslims are released from hell, they will be the majority in paradise. al-Munawi also specifies,","“There is no evidence in this tradition that the women of the earth are less than men in Paradise”","Hence, it should not be taken as such."],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #hell-is-mostly-women","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1357493348998447306"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Also see: https://youtu.be/jGJwYT-QixA?si=zfJ6Gkp05JW6Ymxe","more":{"h":"also see: https://youtu.be/jGJwYT-QixA?si=zfJ6Gkp05JW6Ymxe","p":["also see: https://youtu.be/jGJwYT-QixA?si=zfJ6Gkp05JW6Ymxe"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #hell-is-mostly-women","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1357493348998447306"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Https://x.com/TaymiFawaid/status/2086020699378884610 Shaykh al-Islām Ibn Taymiyyah argues that although it’s established in an authentic ḥadīth that women will be the majority in the Fire, there’s also evidence that wome…","more":{"h":"https://x.com/TaymiFawaid/status/2086020699378884610","p":["https://x.com/TaymiFawaid/status/2086020699378884610\nShaykh al-Islām Ibn Taymiyyah argues that although it’s established in an authentic ḥadīth that women will be the majority in the Fire, there’s also evidence that women will be the majority in Paradise, since every man will have two wives from amongst humankind in Paradise. This is simply because t…","https://shamela.ws/book/1711/3887","قَالَ الْقَاضِي ظَاهِرُ هَذَا الْحَدِيثِ أَنَّ النِّسَاءَ أَكْثَرُ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ وَفِي الْحَدِيثِ الْآخَرِ أَنَّهُنَّ أَكْثَرُ أَهْلِ النَّارِ قَالَ فَيَخْرُجُ مِنْ مَجْمُوعِ هَذَا أَنَّ النِّسَاءَ أَكْثَرُ وَلَدِ آدَمَ","Al-Qadi said: \"The apparent meaning of this hadith is that women constitute the majority of the people of Paradise, while another hadith states that they constitute the majority of the people of Hellfire. He said: Therefore, taking both together, it follows that women make up the majority of the children of Adam.\"\nج17 - ص172 - كتاب شرح النووي على مسلم - قو...\nج17 - ص172 - كتاب شرح النووي على مسلم - قو...\nج17 - ص172 - كتاب شرح النووي على مسلم - قوله صلى الله عليه وسلم حفت الجنة بالمكاره وحفت - المكتبة الشاملة"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #hell-is-mostly-women","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1357493348998447306"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#hell-is-mostly-women)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-women-are-deficient-and-testimony"],{"title":"Women are deficient and testimony","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Women are deficient and testimony","tree":{"they":"Women are deficient and testimony","we":"Https://youtu.be/m3_LUBS3RvA?si=vTXAPccGKPmZPTtq @TestifyApologetics Gets DEMOLISHED (Women in Islam) @TestifyApologetics Gets DEMOLISHED (Women in Islam) Watch from 4:00 to 5:30","more":{"h":"https://youtu.be/m3LUBS3RvA?si=vTXAPccGKPmZPTtq","p":["https://youtu.be/m3_LUBS3RvA?si=vTXAPccGKPmZPTtq\n@TestifyApologetics Gets DEMOLISHED (Women in Islam)\n@TestifyApologetics Gets DEMOLISHED (Women in Islam)","Watch from 4:00 to 5:30"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #women-are-deficient-and-testimony","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1357493267897516152"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Https://www.openislam.wiki/posts/womens-testimony-in-islam-why-two-women-half-a-mind-the-complete-scholarly-analysis-from-ibn-taymiyyah-to-mahmoud-shaltut/ Women's Testimony in Islam: Why Two Women ≠ Half a Mind — The C...","more":{"h":"Women are deficient and testimony","p":["https://www.openislam.wiki/posts/womens-testimony-in-islam-why-two-women-half-a-mind-the-complete-scholarly-analysis-from-ibn-taymiyyah-to-mahmoud-shaltut/\nWomen's Testimony in Islam: Why Two Women ≠ Half a Mind — The C...\nWomen's Testimony in Islam: Why Two Women ≠ Half a Mind — The C...\nWomen's Testimony in Islam — Refutations analysis with scholarly evidence and primary sources.","One must first take a step back on the matter of negative depiction of woman and first assess what the status of women in Islam is. This is done by analyzing the various fada'il of women in the religion. When one assesses the reports they will realize Islam has a specific view on the roles of men and women and that there is often great praise of women in the religion.","This is not to say that Islam holds to everything as numerically equal between men and women in all matters. There are places where men are given more and other places where women are given more. Given either more burdens via responsibility or more leniency via rewards and responsibilities. All of this is from God's design of each gender and due to the respective natures of each creation (man/woman)."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #women-are-deficient-and-testimony","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1357493267897516152"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"There is no doubt Allah has created both men and women with honor; both endowed with the necessary rational faculties to understand his signs in the world and to understand the scriptures that he sends.","more":{"h":"Women are deficient and testimony","p":["There is no doubt Allah has created both men and women with honor; both endowed with the necessary rational faculties to understand his signs in the world and to understand the scriptures that he sends. Thus it should be clear that a man and a woman do not differ in this regard, as they both are created with the same baseline intellectual capacity for knowledge.","It is well known by experiential evidence that men and women differ in intellectual ability on an individual basis. For example, one man might be smarter than a woman or another woman smarter than a man. There is no doubt about such, can anyone deny that Aisha RA had more knowledge about the religion than most of the educated men today? Neither is it possible to deny the same differences in intellect in regards to secular education.","So how should we understand the hadith that woman have been created with \"naqs\" in their aql? And how do we understand the ruling on testimony if a woman can be an expert in financial contracts?","To start and regarding the first point, the first thing we need to do is gather all of the reports so that we can see what the intended meaning of the report is. Without doing such the understanding of the transmission will not be clear.","WIP"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #women-are-deficient-and-testimony","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1357493267897516152"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#women-are-deficient-and-testimony)."}});
