topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-quran-contradiction-what-is-man-created-from"],{"title":"Quran contradiction what is man created from","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"5 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Quran contradiction what is man created from","tree":{"they":"Quran contradiction what is man created from","we":"Allah created Adam (peace be upon him) from the earth i.e., from what it contains.","more":{"h":"Quran contradiction what is man created from","p":["Allah created Adam (peace be upon him) from the earth i.e., from what it contains. Allah says (interpretation of the meaning): \n“Thereof (the earth) We created you, and into it We shall return you, and from it We shall bring you out once again”\n[Ta-Ha 20:55]","He created him from the dust of the earth, as He says (interpretation of the meaning): \n“Verily, the likeness of ‘Eesa (Jesus) before Allah is the likeness of Adam. He created him from dust…”\n[Aal ‘Imraan 3:59]","Then the dust was combined with water to form clay, as the Lord of the Worlds says (interpretation of the meaning): \n“He it is Who has created you from clay, and then has decreed a (stated) term (for you to die). And there is with Him another determined term (for you to be resurrected)”\nal-An’aam 6:2","There are also many similar verses. \nThis clay was sticky – or it was said, viscous – as it says in the verse (interpretation of the meaning): \n“Verily, We created them of a sticky clay”\n[al-Saaffaat 37:11]"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-contradiction-what-is-man-created-from","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220729660669963"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Ibn Manzoor said: the words laazib (sticky) comes from the root lazuba which has the meaning of becoming sticky and solid.","more":{"h":"Quran contradiction what is man created from","p":["Ibn Manzoor said: the words laazib (sticky) comes from the root lazuba which has the meaning of becoming sticky and solid.\nLisaan al-‘Arab, 1/738","Then this sticky clay became muntin (stinking). Allah says (interpretation of the meaning): \n“And indeed, We created man from dried (sounding) clay of altered mud [min hama’in masnoon]”","[al-Hijr 15:26]","Al-Raazi said: Al-hama’ means black mud.\n(Mukhtaar al-Sihaah, p. 64).","It says in Lisaan al-‘Arab (1/61):\nAl-hama’ means black, stinking mud. In the Quran it says “min hama’in masnoon.”","And it says in Lisaan al-‘Arab (13/227): \n“Masnoon means muntin (stinking), as in the verse ‘min hamaa’in masnoon.’ Abu ‘Amr said: this means altered and stinking. Abu’l-Haytham said: sunna al-ma’, fa huwa masnoon, i.e., the water changed, so it was altered (masnoon).”"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-contradiction-what-is-man-created-from","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220729660669963"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"When this mud was mixed with sand, it became salsaal (dried clay).","more":{"h":"When this mud was mixed with sand, it became salsaal (dried clay).","p":["When this mud was mixed with sand, it became salsaal (dried clay).","Al-Raazi said: Salsaal is hot mud mixed with sand, so it starts to clank or clatter when it dries. If it is baked with fire it becomes fired clay or earthenware pottery. \nMukhtaar al-Sihaah, 1/154.","It says in Lisaan al-‘Arab (11/382): Al-Salsaal min al-teen (clay made from mud) is that which has not been made into pottery. Any mud or clay that dries is described as salla saleelan (rattling or clattering) … i.e., it makes a noise like new pottery. Thus salsaal is likened to pottery, as in the verse,\n“He created man (Adam) from sounding clay like the clay of pottery”\n[al-Rahmaan 55:14 – interpretation of the meaning]","All of this is confirmed by the hadeeth of Abu Moosa al-Ash’ari who said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ‘Allah created Adam from a handful that He gathered from the entire earth, so the sons of Adam come like the earth. Some of them are red, some are white, some are black and some are in between. Some of them are easy, some of them are difficult, some are evil and some are good.”"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-contradiction-what-is-man-created-from","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220729660669963"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"(Narrated by al-Tirmidhi, 2955; Abu Dawood, 4693.","more":{"h":"Quran contradiction what is man created from","p":["(Narrated by al-Tirmidhi, 2955; Abu Dawood, 4693. Al-Tirmidhi said that this hadeeth is hasan saheeh, and it was classed as saheeh by Ibn Hibbaan, 14/29; al-Haakim, 2/288; and al-Albaani in Saheeh Abi Dawood, 3926).","This is how Adam was created: from the earth – i.e. from its dust – which was then mixed with water to form mud, which then became black, stinking mud. And this dust was created from the earth which is partly sand and when it is mixed it becomes sounding clay like the clay of pottery.","Hence when Allah describes the creation of Adam in the Quran, in each case He describes one of the stages through which his creation passed and through which the mud was formed. So there is no contradiction in the verses of the Quran.","Then after that the sons of Adam started to multiply and they were created through water which is the sperm and fluids which are emitted by men and women, as is well known."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-contradiction-what-is-man-created-from","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220729660669963"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"This is explained by the Quran in the verses (interpretation of the meanings): “And it is He Who has created man from water, and has appointed for him kindred by blood, and kindred by marriage” [al-Furqaan 25:54] “Then H…","more":{"h":"Quran contradiction what is man created from","p":["This is explained by the Quran in the verses (interpretation of the meanings): “And it is He Who has created man from water, and has appointed for him kindred by blood, and kindred by marriage”\n[al-Furqaan 25:54]","“Then He made his offspring from semen of despised water (male and female sexual discharge)” [al-Sajdah 32:8]","Ibn al-Qayyim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: When the perfection, complete power, all-encompassing knowledge, ever-executed will and utmost wisdom of the Lord decreed that His creation should be of materials of different kinds, and that they should vary in their forms and attributes and natures, His wisdom decreed that He should take a handful of dust from the earth, then mix it with water. So it became like black stinking mud. Then the wind was sent upon it and it dried out, until it became clay like pottery. Then it was given shape and limbs and faculties, and each part of it was given a shape suited to its purpose.\nThen he mentioned how people are created by means of intercourse and the emission of semen.\nAl-Tabaayun fi Aqsaam al-Quran, p. 204"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-contradiction-what-is-man-created-from","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220729660669963"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#quran-contradiction-what-is-man-created-from)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","war","d-dr-purge-of-banu-qurayza"],{"title":"Purge of banu qurayza","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Purge of banu qurayza","tree":{"they":"Purge of banu qurayza","we":"Https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSrANNh13/ TikTok · deenrespondsyt TikTok · deenrespondsyt 4230 likes, 108 comments.","more":{"h":"https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSrANNh13/","p":["https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSrANNh13/\nTikTok · deenrespondsyt\nTikTok · deenrespondsyt","4230 likes, 108 comments. “#islam #muslim #quran #hadith ”"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #purge-of-banu-qurayza","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220832228184114"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#purge-of-banu-qurayza)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","marriage","zaynab","d-dr-the-prophets-marriage-with-zaynab"],{"title":"The prophets marriage with zaynab","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"4 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"The prophets marriage with zaynab","tree":{"they":"Prophet muhammad married Zaynab after his adopted son zaid divorced her found in Surah 33:37 because he fell in love with her after seeing her naked.","we":"First let’s start with the weak Hadith that was quoted… Weak Hadith (shortened) Zaynab had dressed in haste when she was told \"the Messenger of God is at the door.\" She jumped up in haste and excited the admiration of th…","more":{"h":"The prophets marriage with zaynab","p":["Argument\nProphet muhammad married Zaynab after his adopted son zaid divorced her found in Surah 33:37 because he fell in love with her after seeing her naked.","Refutation\nFirst let’s start with the weak Hadith that was quoted…","Weak Hadith (shortened)\nZaynab had dressed in haste when she was told \"the Messenger of God is at the door.\" She jumped up in haste and excited the admiration of the Messenger of God, so that he turned away murmuring something that could scarcely be understood. However, he did say overtly: \"Glory be to God the Almighty! Glory be to God, who causes hearts to turn!\"\nAt-Tabari Volume 8 Page 2","The issue is that if you just go to page 1, we find the following..","This hadith is disconnected (meaning it does not even connect to the prophet).\n,","Muhammad b. Yahyä b. Habbän was a tābiʿūn(lived in the second generation of Muslims) which means he never saw the prophet (ﷺ)\n,","3.'Abdalläh b. 'Amir al-Aslami Abú 'Ämir al-Madani is a weak hadith narrator","al-Waqidi was known to fabricate Hadith narrator according to a consensus of scholars\n,"],"imgs":5,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophets-marriage-with-zaynab","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220987358969948"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Thus, this Hadith about Muhammad seeing Zaynab naked is extremely weak and is must be mawdu(fabricated) Marriage reason The marriage of prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) and Zaynab was not due to her being attractive but rather to abolish adoption.","more":{"h":"Thus, this Hadith about Muhammad seeing Zaynab naked is extremely weak and is must be mawdu(fabricated)","p":["Thus, this Hadith about Muhammad seeing Zaynab naked is extremely weak and is must be mawdu(fabricated)","Marriage reason\nThe marriage of prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) and Zaynab was not due to her being attractive but rather to abolish adoption.","Al-Qurtubi states in his commentary:","This was something that was commonly practiced (adoption) and could not be abolished except through a major event. So Allah wanted this law to be demonstrated by His Messengerﷺ in word and deed.","And Al-Qurtubi further goes on to say:","As for the report which says that the Prophet (saw) liked Zaynab the wife of Zayd, and some immoral people even use the word \"fell in love\", this comes from one who is ignorant of the infallibility of the Prophet (saw), who was protected against such things, or from one who has no respect for him.","From this we learn that the main reason prophet Muhammad married Zaynab was not that he found her attractive or fell in love with her and those who believe this has no respect for the prophet as Al-Qurtubi states, but rather to abolish adoption because something so widely accepted in a Arab society cannot be fully condemned unless a major event occurs. In this case, it would be the word of Allah and the action of the prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) marrying Zaynab, the prophets adopted son Zaid’s Ex-Wife."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophets-marriage-with-zaynab","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220987358969948"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Marriage The prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) did not force Zaid to divorce his wife Zaynab but he was having problems in the marriage and prophet Muhammad even told Zaid to be good to Zaynab before they divorced.","more":{"h":"The prophets marriage with zaynab","p":["Marriage\nThe prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) did not force Zaid to divorce his wife Zaynab but he was having problems in the marriage and prophet Muhammad even told Zaid to be good to Zaynab before they divorced.","In Surah 33:37 it say:\nAnd ˹remember, O  Prophet,˺ when you said to the one for whom Allah has done a favour and you ˹too˺ have done a favour, “Keep your wife and fear Allah,” while concealing within yourself what Allah was going to reveal. And ˹so˺ you were considering the people, whereas Allah was more worthy of your consideration. So when Zaid totally lost interest in ˹keeping˺ his wife, We gave her to you in marriage, so that there would be no blame on the believers for marrying the ex-wives of their adopted sons after their divorce. And Allah’s command is totally binding.","From this verse, we learn that prophet Muhammad ﷺ told Zaid to “keep your wife and fear allah” so when Zaid lost interest in his wife, allah married Zaynab to Muhammad ﷺ to abolish adoption. Some Christian’s like to say the reason he lost interest in his wife was because the prophet saw her naked but it cannot be the case because we already explain why that Hadith is mawdu(fabricated) and there is no reason to believe it’s even a little bit authentic. So why did Zaid divorce Zaynab?","Sahih al-Bukhari 7420\nNarrated Anas:\nZaid bin Haritha came to the Prophet (ﷺ) complaining about his wife. The Prophet (ﷺ) kept on saying (to him), \"Be afraid of Allah and keep your wife.\"","Here, we see that Zaid and Zaynab were having issue within the marriage and thus he lost interest and divorced her."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophets-marriage-with-zaynab","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220987358969948"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"“Why go so far to abolish adoption? Isn’t adoption good?” one might ask.","more":{"h":"The prophets marriage with zaynab","p":["“Why go so far to abolish adoption? Isn’t adoption good?” one might ask. This is to protect an orphans lineage. In verse 33:5 Allah says:","Let your adopted children keep their family names. That is more just in the sight of Allah. But if you do not know their fathers, then they are ˹simply˺ your fellow believers and close associates. There is no blame on you for what you do by mistake, but ˹only˺ for what you do intentionally. And Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Here, raising and taking care of a child that is not your, is lawful unless you change their last name to your last name. You are also not allowed to take them as your actual child. For instance, once the boy passed the age of puberty, he cannot see his adopted mother without her hijab or touch her(although some might dispute this, Allah knows best).","Taking care of orphans in Islam is one of the best deeds a persons can do and Allah will grant (the believers) Paradises.","Sahih al-Bukhari 6005\nNarrated Sahl bin Sa`d:\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said, \"I and the person who looks after an orphan and provides for him, will be in Paradise like this,\" putting his index and middle fingers together.","Conclusion\nThe marriage of Muhammad and Zaynab was to abolish adoptions and was not due to lust nor him falling in love with her."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophets-marriage-with-zaynab","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368220987358969948"},"next":[]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#the-prophets-marriage-with-zaynab)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-how-many-days-for-creation"],{"title":"How many days for creation","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"How many days for creation","tree":{"they":"How many days for creation","we":"The claim is that these two accounts of creation, in Quran 7 & 41, contradict each other; one supposes that creation was done in a total of 6 days, while the other seems to say it was done in 8.","more":{"h":"How many days for creation","p":["The claim is that these two accounts of creation, in Quran 7 & 41, contradict each other; one supposes that creation was done in a total of 6 days, while the other seems to say it was done in 8.","This is wrong. The account in Quran 41 shows the Earth itself created in two, and says Allah blessed it and gave it sustenance all in 4 days. This doesn’t mean the Earth took 2 days and everything on it took 4 days; it means that the Earth took 2 and everything on it took 2. In total, this would mean creation took 4 days for the Earth to complete; the planet itself, as well as everything on it.","It is as if one says, “I took 2 years to get my associate's degree, and spent 4 years on my bachelor’s.” In this example, the person in question didn’t spend 6 years to get a bachelor’s and associate’s degree; rather, he spent 2 on one, while simultaneously spending 2 on the other. This is the same way creation took place: The Earth, in total, took 4 days; 2 were spent making the planet itself, which also contributed to the creation of all of Earth, and 2 were spent making everything on the Earth, thus completing the creation of Earth with a total of 4 days.","This is supported by how Allah says, “4 days without distinction - for those who ask. Additionally, commentators have elaborated on the use of the language here.","Al-Qurtubi:","Al-Baghawi:","Al-Zajjaj:"],"imgs":5,"credit":"Deenresponds · #how-many-days-for-creation","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221172566851737"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Under the understanding that creation took 2 days for the Earth itself, 2 days for everything on the Earth, and 2 days for the Heavens, this means that it took, in total, 6 days.","more":{"h":"How many days for creation","p":["Under the understanding that creation took 2 days for the Earth itself, 2 days for everything on the Earth, and 2 days for the Heavens, this means that it took, in total, 6 days. Thus, the account in Quran 41 has been harmonized with Quran 7.","However, one should not assume the “days” here means literal, 24-hour days, which would contradict modern science, as the Quran uses the term “day” relatively: it can refer to periods taking longer than our normal 24 hours. For example, every matter ascends to Allah in a day:","“A day with [our] lord” is also used relatively:","The “Day” of Judgement is also used relatively:","We see that the Quran often uses the term “day”, while not referencing the 24 hours here on Earth. Therefore, there is nothing wrong with interpreting the “days of creation” as 6 “periods” instead of 24-hour periods.","In summary, there isn’t a contradiction in the Quran with the days of creation: the Earth itself took 2 days, everything on the Earth took 2 days, and the Heavens took 2 days; creation took a total of 6 days. Furthermore, the term “days” should be interpreted relatively, in a manner in line with the Quran’s overall usage of the term. Thus, the Quran doesn’t contradict itself, nor modern science."],"imgs":8,"credit":"Deenresponds · #how-many-days-for-creation","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221172566851737"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#how-many-days-for-creation)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-expel-ahlul-kitab-from-arabia"],{"title":"Expel ahlul kitab from arabia","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Expel ahlul kitab from arabia","tree":{"they":"Expel ahlul kitab from arabia","we":"The hadith reads: The claim is that this shows the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ wanted to expel the Jews and Christians from all of Arabia.","more":{"h":"The hadith reads:","p":["The hadith reads:","The claim is that this shows the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ wanted to expel the Jews and Christians from all of Arabia. However, the correct understanding is that he only wanted to keep them away from the region of Hejaz, which encompasses the holy cities of Mecca and Medina, which encompass the holy mosques.","This opinion was shared by an-Nawawi, who commented on this hadith:","An-Nawawi reasons that the hadith above showed the Prophet ﷺ sent them to a place called Tayma, which is still a part of Arabia, but outside of the Hejaz region.","As for why they were to be exiled in the first place, it’s partly because they are considered impure; Christians and Jews do not conduct the ritual cleanings that Muslims due, so they wouldn’t be considered pure enough to be near the Holy Sites:","Another reason is for safety. If the People of the Book stayed within these cities, they would be able to conspire with outside forces against the Muslims from within their holiest sites. To Protect the State, as well as the Holy Cities, it is safer to have them outside of Hejaz.","Finally, keeping Hejaz as a holy space for Muslims, without any outside infleunce or other ideologies being spread, is the best way to ensure uniformity in the Holy Sites, and that only Muslims are allowed therein."],"imgs":5,"credit":"Deenresponds · #expel-ahlul-kitab-from-arabia","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221278141677698"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#expel-ahlul-kitab-from-arabia)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-quran-copies-from-talmud"],{"title":"Quran copies from talmud","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Quran copies from talmud","tree":{"they":"Quran copies from talmud","we":"Solidifying the point that the Talmud isn’t making everything up, and is working with previous sources— oral and possibly written ones.","more":{"h":"Quran copies from talmud","p":["Solidifying the point that the Talmud isn’t making everything up, and is working with previous sources— oral and possibly written ones. This is confirmed in that there are traditions found within the Talmud that can be found in extra-biblical literature. For example, the Talmud details a story of Solomon having demons under his control:","This same sentiment is also found in the “Testimony of Truth,” which is dated to be a 1st century CE (Pre-Talmudic) apocryphal text:","1 Add Reaction","The same is in another non-canonical text called the “Apocalypse of Adam”, another 1st century CE (Pre-Talmudic) apocryphal text:","Thus, the Talmud isn’t just making this information up; it’s preserving it from non-rabbinic, extra-biblical, historical sources; there are some fabrications— either from the authors, their sources, or their sources— but there are also instances of Rabbis quoting sources available to them. Also, these texts can preserve more than past revelation; they can also simply preserve history. Israelite history can be passed down orally until it arrives in apocryphal texts, biblical texts, and rabbinic texts.","The Quran never says that everything in the Talmud is false; that there can be no revelation found in the Talmud. The Quran never says there can be no revelation to Israel other than the Torah and the Gospel; it never says they weren’t given extra tradition."],"imgs":11,"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-copies-from-talmud","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221336115351693"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#quran-copies-from-talmud)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-women-are-like-dogs"],{"title":"Women are like dogs","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Women are like dogs","tree":{"they":"Women are like dogs","we":"So as sheikh ul islam, ibn Taymiyyah(Rahimullah) said Knowing this we can now explain the hadith , just as you would describe a man as well as gorilla and a lion as all being strong, they would all fit under one category…","more":{"h":"So as sheikh ul islam, ibn","p":["So as sheikh ul islam, ibn \nTaymiyyah(Rahimullah) said","Knowing this we can now explain the hadith , just as you would describe a man as well as gorilla and a lion as all being strong, they would all fit under one category because of this one description that they all correlate with eachother, in the same way the thing that correlates a women with a black Dog as well as a donkey is that they are great distractions to the prayer. Al Qurtubi (Rahimullah) said:","But this doesn't mean that the prayer is then invalidated and you have to redo it and the male aswell as a female or whatever might be that might be passing by someone infront of them while they're praying are all sources of distraction and it is ill adviced and they are described as shaytan, the ones who do that in that interrupt thr prayer by walking past however these 3 are specifically pointed out because they are 3 sources of great interruption as I mentioned before with the women's beauty being a fitnah as well as the braining of the donkey causing a huge amount of noise and distraction as well as specifically a black Dog that might be seen to be dangerous"],"imgs":5,"credit":"Deenresponds · #women-are-like-dogs","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221303655370913"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#women-are-like-dogs)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-10-94-prophet-can-doubt"],{"title":"10 94 prophet can doubt","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"10 94 prophet can doubt","tree":{"they":"Christians and Jews of that time?","we":"All Christians and Jews, including those of today?","more":{"h":"Christians and Jews of that time?","p":["all Christians and Jews, including those of today?\n,"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #10-94-prophet-can-doubt","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221384760623326"},"next":[{"they":"a specific group among them?","we":"Nearly all Mufassireen, including Tafseer Ibn Abbas (RA), agree that the Quran refers specifically to the Muslims among the People of the Book—such as Abdullah Ibn Salam (RA) and his followers—not the average Jews or Christians.","more":{"h":"a specific group among them?","p":["Nearly all Mufassireen, including Tafseer Ibn Abbas (RA), agree that the Quran refers specifically to the Muslims among the People of the Book—such as Abdullah Ibn Salam (RA) and his followers—not the average Jews or Christians. It does not instruct the Prophet (ﷺ) to seek guidance from disbelievers among them. It would be illogical for Allah (SWT) to command the Prophet (ﷺ) to consult those who actively opposed Islam.","This group of true believers from among them is also mentioned in the following verses of the Quran:","Quran 3:199: \"And indeed, among the People of the Scripture are those who believe in Allāh and what was revealed to you and what was revealed to them, [being] humbly submissive to Allāh. They do not exchange the verses of Allāh for a small price. Those will have their reward with their Lord. Indeed, Allāh is swift in account.\"","Quran 17:107-109: Say, \"Believe in it or do not believe.\" Indeed, those who were given knowledge before it - when it is recited to them, they fall upon their faces in prostration, And they say, \"Exalted is our Lord! Indeed, the promise of our Lord has been fulfilled.\" And they fall upon their faces weeping, and it [i.e., the Qur’ān] increases them in humble submission.","Quran 46:10: Say, \"Have you considered: if it [i.e., the Qur’ān] was from Allāh, and you disbelieved in it while a witness from the Children of Israel has testified to something similar and believed while you were arrogant...? \"Indeed, Allāh does not guide the wrongdoing people.","Nearly all Mufassireen, including Tafseer Ibn Abbas (RA), agree that the Quran refers specifically to the Muslims among the People of the Book—such as Abdullah Ibn Salam (RA) and his followers—not the average Jews or Christians. It does not instruct the Prophet (ﷺ) to seek guidance from disbelievers among them. It would be illogical for Allah (SWT) to command the Prophet (ﷺ) to consult those who actively opposed Islam.","This group of true believers from among them is also mentioned in the following verses of the Quran:","Quran 3:199: \"And indeed, among the People of the Scripture are those who believe in Allāh and what was revealed to you and what was revealed to them, [being] humbly submissive to Allāh. They do not exchange the verses of Allāh for a small price. Those will have their reward with their Lord. Indeed, Allāh is swift in account.\"","Quran 17:107-109: Say, \"Believe in it or do not believe.\" Indeed, those who were given knowledge before it - when it is recited to them, they fall upon their faces in prostration, And they say, \"Exalted is our Lord! Indeed, the promise of our Lord has been fulfilled.\" And they fall upon their faces weeping, and it [i.e., the Qur’ān] increases them in humble submission.","Quran 46:10: Say, \"Have you considered: if it [i.e., the Qur’ān] was from Allāh, and you disbelieved in it while a witness from the Children of Israel has testified to something similar and believed while you were arrogant...? \"Indeed, Allāh does not guide the wrongdoing people.","Observation:\nThe Quran in the above verses highlights key characteristics of these Muslim Jews and Christians (before the Sharia of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ):","They did not compromisetheir faith for worldly gain. (unlike those mentioned in Quran 2:79 who distorted Allah's words for fleetin gain).\nBefore the Quran was revealed, they had prior knowledge and recognized its truth when it was recited. They humbly prostrated, praised Allah, and acknowledged its divine authenticity.\nThey were humble, not arrogant, and accepted Islam when it was presented to them.\nConclusion:","The claim that the Quran instructs Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) to ask Christians and Jews if in doubt is a misinterpretation. The verse in Quran 10:94 does not specify Christians or Jews but refers to those with knowledge of earlier scriptures. It rhetorically addresses the Prophet (ﷺ), and the intended audience is likely the disbelieving pagans or humanity in general.","The verse does not suggest that the Prophet (ﷺ) should consult those who opposed Islam. Rather, it aligns with interpretations that focus on Muslims among the People of the Book, like Abdullah Ibn Salam (RA), who recognized the truth of Islam before its formal revelation.","This group of believers, who did not distort their faith for worldly gain, accepted Islam humbly and acknowledged the truth of the Quran when it was revealed. From the Islamic perspective, they are considered \"Muslims\" even before accepting the Sharia of Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ).","Muqatil bin soleiman our earliest complete tafsir written (130AH) that is preserved tell us it is concerning going to the likes of Abdullah bin Salam RA\n,"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #10-94-prophet-can-doubt","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221384760623326"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#10-94-prophet-can-doubt)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-abu-dawud-4449-torah-preserved"],{"title":"Abu dawud 4449 torah preserved","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Abu dawud 4449 torah preserved","tree":{"they":"Abu dawud 4449 torah preserved","we":"The Hadith reads: Critics utilize this report to push the agenda of the Islamic “Dilemma”; to say that this Hadith shows the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ confirmed belief in the entire Torah available at his time.","more":{"h":"The Hadith reads:","p":["The Hadith reads:","Critics utilize this report to push the agenda of the Islamic “Dilemma”; to say that this Hadith shows the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ confirmed belief in the entire Torah available at his time. However, this is wrong for multiple reasons.","Fabricator Detected, Hadith Rejected\n,\n,\nIf we examine the chain of narration, we can distinctly see the presence of a person of interest:","This shows the presence of a “Hisham ibn Sa’ad” in this chain. Here’s some information about this narrator (Farid Responds, https://youtu.be/jWWGA_607MI?t=315 ):\nDavid Wood Challenged Me to Refute This Video! (5 Disgusting \"Facts\")\nDavid Wood Challenged Me to Refute This Video! (5 Disgusting \"Facts\")"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #abu-dawud-4449-torah-preserved","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221464624365691"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"We can see that this chain has a distinctly weak narrator.","more":{"h":"Abu dawud 4449 torah preserved","p":["We can see that this chain has a distinctly weak narrator. This alone is reason enough to reject it. Although one may contend that Al-Bani, the esteemed contemporary scholar of Hadith, graded it hasan, meaning good. Al-Bani, however, is not infallible and can make mistakes. Ibn Hazm has said something regarding this hadith in specific:","As for the report in which the Prophet (peace be upon him) took the Torah and said: ‘I believe in thee’, it is a fabricated false report that did not reach us with proper chain of transmission","(Ibn Hazm, Al-Fisal fe al-Milal wa al-Ahwaa wa al-Nihal, Volume 1, p. 237)","The hadith in Abu Dawood is the only one with this wording. We can see that this report isn’t strong; in fact, it’s either weak or fabricated. Therefore, no Muslim has to, or even should, accept this Hadith, let alone the reasoning critics bring with it.","Interpretation\n,\n,\nThere is no doubt that this is an exceptionally weak Hadith. However, even if one were to, hypothetically, accept it, it still wouldn’t necessitate a complete acceptance of the Torah. This is aided by context from the Quran and Sunnah:","This last Hadith is from one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, Abdullah ibn Abbas. Here are some reports that strengthen the authority of his opinion:","Thus, considering the strength of the report as well as outside context, Abu Dawood 4449 is either a fabrication, or does not mean that Islam confirms the entirety of the Bible.","see ⁠✧│islamic-dilemma for more"],"imgs":4,"credit":"Deenresponds · #abu-dawud-4449-torah-preserved","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221464624365691"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#abu-dawud-4449-torah-preserved)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-judge-by-the-gospel-5-47"],{"title":"Judge by the gospel 5 47","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Judge by the gospel 5 47","tree":{"they":"Judge by the gospel 5 47","we":"The verse reads: The claim is that this is the Quran affirming the New Testament.","more":{"h":"The verse reads:","p":["The verse reads:","The claim is that this is the Quran affirming the New Testament. This is wrong, as it is a commandment to obey the general truths found in the Gospel. This is supported by the wording; the verse does not say, “Let the people of the Gospel judge by it”, it, instead, says, “Let the people of the Gospel judge by what Allah has revealed in it”. This indicates that not all of it is what Allah has revealed.","This interpretation of general affirmation is supported by the earliest Tafsir of this verse, from Muqatil bin Suleiman:","This shows Muqatil Bin Suleiman interpreting this verse as commanding the abiding of general good things in the Gospel, such as pardoning the killer, not to abide by everything therein.","What this verse also does not mean is that the Quran confirms all of the Bible, as there are many verses claiming textual corruption:","There is also a clear hadith from Ibn Abbas, a cousin and great companion of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, detailing how the other scriptures haven’t been perfectly preserved:","The Quran does command an affirmation of the general truths of the other scriptures. In terms of the Gospel, the Quran defines it as a scripture given to Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام:","This means that biographies written about Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام wouldn’t fit this definition. However, this just means that the New Testament wasn’t the scripture given to Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام; it can still contain truths from said scripture. It is these truths that the Quran refers to when it gives a general affirmation in verses like 5:47 above."],"imgs":5,"credit":"Deenresponds · #judge-by-the-gospel-5-47","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221512032849920"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#judge-by-the-gospel-5-47)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-razi-preservation-of-torah"],{"title":"Razi preservation of torah","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Razi preservation of torah","tree":{"they":"Razi preservation of torah","we":"The claim is that Razi believed that the Torah was preserved.","more":{"h":"The claim is that Razi believed that the Torah was preserved.","p":["The claim is that Razi believed that the Torah was preserved.","Razi\n,\n,\nIn terms of Razi, he believed the original Torah was distorted by a king in Babylon during a time when mass transmission wasn’t applicable, unlike that of the Prophet ﷺ.","(Al-Arba'een fi Usul ad-Deen, vol. 2, pp. 77)","see ⁠✧│bukhari-preservation-of-torah for more"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #razi-preservation-of-torah","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221551836794930"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#razi-preservation-of-torah)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-bukhari-preservation-of-torah"],{"title":"Bukhari preservation of torah","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Bukhari preservation of torah","tree":{"they":"Bukhari preservation of torah","we":"(Tafsir ibn Kathir Quran 3:78) Ibn Hajar also attributes the statement to Ibn Abbas instead of Bukhari when he declared it didn’t come with a proper chain of narration: The argument is still weak, even if one were to gra…","more":{"h":"Bukhari preservation of torah","p":["(Tafsir ibn Kathir Quran 3:78)","Ibn Hajar also attributes the statement to Ibn Abbas instead of Bukhari when he declared it didn’t come with a proper chain of narration:","The argument is still weak, even if one were to grant the authenticity of this statement. Firstly, Bukhari titles the chapter where he places this hadith as speaking about the Preserved Tablet.","Although, not everything in the narration is relevant to the Preserved Tablet. Now, notice how Ibn Abbas says the meaning of this distortion is that “they remove”:","This means Ibn Abbas does believe people can remove from the books in this life.\nHe would be contradicting himself if he went on to say they can't remove from the very thing they just removed from. This indicates that he's saying, in this life, the people remove words from their original places, but they can't do so with Allah's books with him.\nThey can only misplace the contents of the preserved tablet in this lif,e but can never change it as it's forever preserved with Allah.","This interpretation is justified, as at-Tabari used similar language when specifically speaking about the Preserved Tablet:","(Tafsir at-Tabari Quran 6:115)","Ibn Kathir does the same thing when citing a similar quote from Wahb bin Munnabih, but he still believes it’s referring to the Preserved Tablet:","(Tafsir Ibn Kathir Quran 3:78)","Preceding this, Ibn Kathir also cites a similar quote from Ibn Abbas above, and yet he still believes it's open to be referring specifically to the preserved tablet."],"imgs":7,"credit":"Deenresponds · #bukhari-preservation-of-torah","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221594211844178"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The last reason to support this interpretation is the Quranic Principle, where we use the clear statements to inform our understanding of the more ambiguous ones.","more":{"h":"Bukhari preservation of torah","p":["The last reason to support this interpretation is the Quranic Principle, where we use the clear statements to inform our understanding of the more ambiguous ones. We take the clear statements to be the foundation and try to harmonise the ambiguous ones with them.","And, as we know, there's a famous clear hadith from Ibn Abbas telling us that the people of the book distorted and corrupted their books by adding to them. So if Bukhari had this clear hadith of distortion, he would’ve used it to inform his understanding of the ambiguous:","In summary, Razi didn’t believe in the preservation of the torah. And the Quote attributed to Bukhari is actually from Ibn Abbas and is inauthentic. But even if we grant its authenticity, Bukhari most likely interpreted it as the Preserved Tablet."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #bukhari-preservation-of-torah","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221594211844178"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#bukhari-preservation-of-torah)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-the-quran-uses-apocrypha-texts"],{"title":"The quran uses apocrypha texts","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"The quran uses apocrypha texts","tree":{"they":"The quran uses apocrypha texts","we":"The verse reads: This is Quran 5:110. Thomas Aquinas, a Doctor of the Catholic Church, claimed the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was a false Prophet because he quoted from many fables and false doctrine.","more":{"h":"The verse reads:","p":["The verse reads:","This is Quran 5:110. Thomas Aquinas, a Doctor of the Catholic Church, claimed the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was a false Prophet because he quoted from many fables and false doctrine. He claimed that the story described in this verse, how Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام molded clay into a bird and breathed life into it, was taken from the non-canonical, apocryphal work, the Infancy Gospel of Thomas, which he claimed was a false and non-historical text about the early years of Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام.","First of all, the Infancy Gospel of Thomas, although it does contain this story, is not non-historical; its early dating comes from its being quoted by Irenaeus:","Sure, the text is anonymous and Thomas, most likely, didn’t write it, but a text being anonymous and having some ahistorical information doesn’t mean it’s not reliable. A Christian would have to agree with this, as Paul himself, in the New Testament, quotes apocryphal, non-canonical writings:","Here, Paul references figures called “Jannes and Jambres”, but these figures aren’t a part of the Bible. Instead, they exist in non-canonical texts like the book of Jannes and Jambres:"],"imgs":4,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-quran-uses-apocrypha-texts","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221626562515045"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"This work is dated to the first century CE.","more":{"h":"The quran uses apocrypha texts","p":["This work is dated to the first century CE. Even if Christians don’t consider all of this text canonical, it shows that true information can come from an ahistorical, non-canonical work.","Moreover, even if we didn’t prove the possible truthfulness of apocryphal work like the Infancy Gospel of Thomas, there has been a newly discovered historical evidence of Jesus conducting this bird miracle.","Through a newly discovered manuscript titled “P.Hamb.Graec. 1011” dated to the 4th or 5th century, one of Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام’s earliest miracles has been confirmed.","This is because the manuscript contains part of what's called the 'Vivification of the Sparrows', the second chapter of the Gospel of Thomas, which describes Jesus making 12 birds out of clay and bringing them to life.","This recent discovery affirms the historicity of the Quran. Hence, on account of the plausible presence of true information in apocryphal works, and a recent discovery, Thomas Aquinas’ claim was incorrect."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-quran-uses-apocrypha-texts","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221626562515045"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#the-quran-uses-apocrypha-texts)."}});
topic(["islam","proofs","d-dr-the-prophet-did-no-miracles"],{"title":"The prophet did no miracles","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"The prophet did no miracles","tree":{"they":"The prophet did no miracles","we":"The verses read: The claim is that this shows the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ had no miracles.","more":{"h":"The verses read:","p":["The verses read:","The claim is that this shows the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ had no miracles. This is wrong, as these verses, to the contrary, detail how the Prophet ﷺ has no control over when, or if, a sign will come. This is similar to what Jesus said in the New Testament:","Additionally, even if we, hypothetically, failed to give a reconciliation to said Quran verses, we would still be able to conclude that the Prophet ﷺ had miracles from the Quran alone. While addressing the Prophet ﷺ, the Quran says:","The “this is nothing but pure magic” is the same response given to Moses عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام and Aaron عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام in Quran 10:76:","This is also the same response given to Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام in Quran 61:6:","When these Prophets gave miracles to their people, they were given the same response as the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in Quran 37:15.","Moreover, Quran 37:14 alone is enough to prove the Prophet ﷺ did miracles. Note the word used for “sign”:"],"imgs":8,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophet-did-no-miracles","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221668216016957"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"In Arabic, ءَايَةًۭ/Ayah can mean one of three things: A verse from the Quran, a sign in nature, or a miraculous action.","more":{"h":"The prophet did no miracles","p":["In Arabic, ءَايَةًۭ/Ayah can mean one of three things: A verse from the Quran, a sign in nature, or a miraculous action.","The meaning “verse from the Quran” doesn’t work because the verse above specifies that this sign is being seen. One cannot see a verse of the Quran.","The meaning “a sign in nature” doesn’t work because verse 15 specifies that this sign was called “nothing but pure magic”; one wouldn’t call the viewing of nature “pure magic”.","Therefore, the only viable meaning of the term ayah, here, is a miraculous event. The most logical interpretation of these verses is that people, at the time of the Prophet ﷺ, witnessed him come with miracles, and called them “pure magic”, just like people did during the times of past Prophets like Moses عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام, Aaron عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام, and Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام.","This understanding is also present in the earliest Tafsir of these verses, from Muqatil bin Suleiman, who says that these verses refer to the miraculous splitting of the moon:","Thus, the Quran verses mentioned in the beginning do not claim that the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was without miracles. Rather, verses in the Quran affirm that he had miracles. This interpretation isn’t even a more modern one, as it is also present in the earliest available tafsir. Hence, the claim is wrong."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophet-did-no-miracles","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221668216016957"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#the-prophet-did-no-miracles)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","marriage","aisha","d-dr-aisha-would-wipe-semen-from-the-prophets-clothes"],{"title":"Aisha would wipe semen from the prophets clothes","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Aisha would wipe semen from the prophets clothes","tree":{"they":"Aisha would wipe semen from the prophets clothes","we":"I’m gonna keep it nice and short. A wife cleaning their husbands clothing is normal.","more":{"h":"Aisha would wipe semen from the prophets clothes","p":["I’m gonna keep it nice and short. A wife cleaning their husbands clothing is normal. The prophet SAWS could have semen on his clothing from nocturnal emissions or after having relations some drops of semen can still come out after putting the garments back on.","The reason why this was transmitted is so that scholars of jurisprudence can understand what sort of impurity is a man classified as when being touched by semen. Or does it require the semen spot to be completely not visible anymore before one can pray with the garment on again."],"imgs":4,"credit":"Deenresponds · #aisha-would-wipe-semen-from-the-prophets-clothes","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221703267680286"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#aisha-would-wipe-semen-from-the-prophets-clothes)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-prophet-had-relations-with-all-of-his-wives-in-one"],{"title":"Prophet had relations with all of his wives in one night","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Prophet had relations with all of his wives in one night","tree":{"they":"Prophet had relations with all of his wives in one night","we":"The Hadith reads: The claim is that- There doesn’t seem to be a claim to this.","more":{"h":"The Hadith reads:","p":["The Hadith reads:","The claim is that-","There doesn’t seem to be a claim to this. Maybe some misinterpret it, thinking the Prophet ﷺ had relations with all his wives at once, but that's not what it means. The Hadith shows the masculinity of the Prophet ﷺ; he was able to keep all his 9 wives satisfied— normal men wouldn’t be able to do this. A variant of this Hadith elaborates:","Also, one shouldn’t have a problem with polygamy, as Thomas Aquinas, a Doctor of the Catholic Church, said polygamy was made to be moral before Jesus came:","Additionally, in the Bible itself, God says the following about polygamy:","Did God give David multiple wives, although it was immoral? And did that same God, knowing it’s immoral, say he would’ve given David even more? Or, more plausibly, does the Old Testament support having multiple wives?","In terms of the original Hadith, it is not weird for the Prophet ﷺ to have multiple wives— something supported by the Old Testament. Moreover, it is also not weird for the Prophet ﷺ to be able to satisfy all his wives, and showcases his strength & masculinity."],"imgs":7,"credit":"Deenresponds · #prophet-had-relations-with-all-of-his-wives-in-one-night","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221776634581143"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#prophet-had-relations-with-all-of-his-wives-in-one-night)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-the-prophet-kissed-a-young-boy"],{"title":"The prophet kissed a young boy","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"The prophet kissed a young boy","tree":{"they":"The prophet kissed a young boy","we":"25:55 timestamp https://youtu.be/MjrizrmkyHU Refuting a Fake Ex Muslim (9 Reasons why Islam is False) @Ethrii Refuting a Fake Ex Muslim (9 Reasons why Islam is False) @Ethrii The Hadith reads: Proponents of this argue th…","more":{"h":"25:55 timestamp","p":["25:55 timestamp\nhttps://youtu.be/MjrizrmkyHU\nRefuting a Fake Ex Muslim (9 Reasons why Islam is False) @Ethrii\nRefuting a Fake Ex Muslim (9 Reasons why Islam is False) @Ethrii","The Hadith reads:","Proponents of this argue that this is weird, but there are some nuanced contentions:","Fabricator Detected, Hadith Rejected\n,\n,\nIf we shift our vision over to this hadith’s chain of narration, we find a person of interest:","We find the presence of Hisham ibn Sa’ad in the chain. This is interesting because of what scholars think of him (Farid Responds, https://youtu.be/jWWGA_607MI?t=315 )\nDavid Wood Challenged Me to Refute This Video! (5 Disgusting \"Facts\")\nDavid Wood Challenged Me to Refute This Video! (5 Disgusting \"Facts\")"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophet-kissed-a-young-boy","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221874923901029"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"We can see that many scholars believe he is weak.","more":{"h":"The prophet kissed a young boy","p":["We can see that many scholars believe he is weak. Some notable names here are Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal— an early, influential scholar who founded his own School of Fiqh that continues its influence today, as well as the author of the largest Hadith collection ever, Musnad Ahmad ibn Hanbal— and al-Nasa’i— another influential scholar who has his own widely respected Hadith collection, Sunan an-Nasa’i— both of which did not find him to be a good narrator.","Although al-Bani, a widely respected contemporary scholar of Hadith, graded this Hadith as “good”, he is not infallible, and the majority of opinions seem to point to Hisham ibn Sa’ad as a weak narrator. Due to his presence in the chain, this Hadith can be rejected as a fabrication.","Context\n,\n,\nEven ignoring how weak this is, this Hadith wouldn’t even mean the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ kisses little boys; the boy described in the narration is his grandson, Hasan:","One might think that kissing even your own grandson in this manner might be better not to do, but even that is subjective. However, we mustn’t forget how weak this Hadith is; this context just shows that, were this Hadith to be taken authoritatively, it wouldn’t mean the Prophet ﷺ went around kissing random little boys, نعوذ بالله.","In conclusion, this Hadith doesn’t mean the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ would kiss random little boys; rather, it shows that he kissed his grandson. Moreover, this is a weak report because of the presence of Hisham ibn Sa’ad, and it is rejected altogether."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophet-kissed-a-young-boy","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221874923901029"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#the-prophet-kissed-a-young-boy)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-the-followers-of-jesus-will-prevail"],{"title":"The followers of jesus will prevail","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"The followers of jesus will prevail","tree":{"they":"The followers of jesus will prevail","we":"‎ Yet again, Allah speaks about Islam, through the title of “religion of truth”.","more":{"h":"The followers of jesus will prevail","p":["‎ \nYet again, Allah speaks about Islam, through the title of “religion of truth”. Allah also speaks about the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, as well as guidance. Hence, this pattern continues.\n‎","‎ \nNote how this verse references the believers, the Muslims: “O you who have believed”.\n‎ ‎","‎ \nThe pattern continues; Allah continues to speak to the believers about believing in Him as well as His Messenger. He also speaks about striving for His sake using their lives, which will be expanded on in the next few verses.‎","‎ \nAllah says, very explicitly, that He will give the believers victory; that He will give them “imminent conquest.” He ends this by, again, explicitly referencing the believers.\n‎","This is the verse in question. The only nation that has prevailed over those who disbelieved is the Muslim nation, not past nations. This includes the nation of Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام, as verse 6 explicitly says that he was rejected by his people, or at least most of them.","This conclusion is supported by the early tafsir, as at-Tabari states:"],"imgs":8,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-followers-of-jesus-will-prevail","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221912219648121"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Translation: (So ​​We supported those who believed against their enemy) meaning: So We strengthened those who believed from the two groups of the Children of Israel against their enemy, those of them who disbelieved in M…","more":{"h":"Translation:","p":["Translation:\n(So ​​We supported those who believed against their enemy) meaning: So We strengthened those who believed from the two groups of the Children of Israel against their enemy, those of them who disbelieved in Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, by his confirmation to them that Jesus was the servant and messenger of God, and the denial of those who said he was a god, and those who said he was the son of God, may He be exalted, so they became victorious, so the group of believers became victorious over their disbelieving enemy among them.","The commentators said something similar to what we have said about this. (Tafsir at-Tabari 23/367)","We can see that the opinion of at-Tabari was that verse 14 refers to a group of the Children of Israel overcoming another, through belief in the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. Then, at-Tabari goes on to mention those with the same view. We do not see, however, people interpreting this to mean that the people during the time of Jesus, who believed, overcame those who disbelieved militarily.","In conclusion, neither of these verses, Quran 3:55 & 61:14, suggests that the true followers of Jesus would militarily prevail over their enemies; the context suggests spiritual superiority for one, and modern superiority for the other. Thus, the claim is incorrect."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-followers-of-jesus-will-prevail","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221912219648121"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#the-followers-of-jesus-will-prevail)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-jesus-is-god-quran-9-31"],{"title":"Jesus is god quran 9 31","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Jesus is god quran 9 31","tree":{"they":"Jesus is god quran 9 31","we":"The verse reads: The claim is that this verse claims people should worship the Messiah alongside Allah (نعوذ بالله).","more":{"h":"The verse reads:","p":["The verse reads:","The claim is that this verse claims people should worship the Messiah alongside Allah (نعوذ بالله). This is based off of a primitive reading of the Arabic; it says ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ (they have taken), ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ أَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَـٰنَهُمْ (their rabbis and their monks), أَرْبَابًۭا (as lords), أَرْبَابًۭا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ وَٱلْمَسِيحَ (besides Allah), وَٱلْمَسِيحَ ٱبْنَ مَرْيَمَ (and the Messiah, son of Mary). From the plain, primitive reading, it seems like the claim might be true due to the order of the figures mentioned, reading Arabic as if it’s English.","However, this doesn’t hold in the Arabic. The term ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ (they have taken) refers to the figures with the Fatha:","We can see that “Rabbis” and “monks” have the fatha, so the term ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ (they have taken) applies to them. Now, let us examine the words “Allah” and “Messiah”:","We see that the term “Allah” has a kasra, not a fatha. This is because the term أَرْبَابًۭا مِّن دُونِ (lords besides) applies to this word. Now, what about “Messiah”?"],"imgs":4,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-is-god-quran-9-31","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221961594867752"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"We see that the word “Messiah” has a fatha, so the term ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ (they have taken) applies to it, not أَرْبَابًۭا مِّن دُونِ (lords besides).","more":{"h":"Jesus is god quran 9 31","p":["We see that the word “Messiah” has a fatha, so the term ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ (they have taken) applies to it, not أَرْبَابًۭا مِّن دُونِ (lords besides). Now, the claim would be true if the term Messiah here had a kasra instead of a fatha [a line below the letter instead of above], but we clearly see that it’s not the case. Therefore, the claim is false.","As for why the term Messiah is separated from the others, some have said that it is because the Monks and Rabbis were calling people to “worship” them, while the Messiah was not. Another could be because the worship of the Monks and Rabbis is different from that of the Messiah, as at-Tabari notes:","“O Messenger of God, we do not worship them! He said: Do they not forbid what God has permitted, so you forbid it, and permit what God has forbidden, so you permit it? He said: I said: Yes! He said: That is their worship.” (Tafsir at-Tabari 14/210)","We see that the “worship” of the Rabbis and Monks isn’t literal deification, while we know the worship of the Messiah is. Therefore, Allah separated them in this verse. Both interpretations have merit, and neither one is necessarily right or wrong.","Another perspective is that there are clear and unclear verses in the Quran, as Allah says:"],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-is-god-quran-9-31","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221961594867752"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"‎ Allah states explicitly that some verses are clear, the foundation of the Book, while others are less specific in meaning.","more":{"h":"Jesus is god quran 9 31","p":["‎ \nAllah states explicitly that some verses are clear, the foundation of the Book, while others are less specific in meaning. He also points out that “no one knows its [true] interpretation except Allah” (Quran 3:7). Since this verse, Quran 9:31, may be seen as unclear, one should look to the clearer verses to conclude from. Such verses, concerning whether Jesus is divine, include:\n‎","Taking the overall message of the Quran into account, it's clear that it claims Jesus is not God, should not be worshipped, and never claimed otherwise. It would be incorrect to read into clear verses using unclear verses, so we, therefore, give context to the unclear verses using clear verses. In conclusion, no, the Quran doesn’t claim Jesus should be worshipped."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-is-god-quran-9-31","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221961594867752"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#jesus-is-god-quran-9-31)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-allah-came-in-a-dream-as-a-young-boy"],{"title":"Allah came in a dream as a young boy","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Allah came in a dream as a young boy","tree":{"they":"Allah came in a dream as a young boy","we":"The Hadith Claiming the Prophet ﷺ Saw His Lord as a Young Man is Rejected , The hadith stating that the Prophet ﷺ saw his Lord as a curly-haired, beardless young man in a green robe is considered objectionable (Munkar) a…","more":{"h":"The Hadith Claiming the Prophet ﷺ Saw His Lord as a Young Man is Rejected","p":["The Hadith Claiming the Prophet ﷺ Saw His Lord as a Young Man is Rejected\n,\nThe hadith stating that the Prophet ﷺ saw his Lord as a curly-haired, beardless young man in a green robe is considered objectionable (Munkar) and unauthentic for the following reasons:","Scholarly Rejections:\n,\nAl-Bayhaqi narrated it from Ibn ‘Abbas, but scholars ruled it inauthentic.\n,\nAl-Albani (As-Silsilah Adh-Dha'eefah) and Ath-Thahabi (As-Siyar) classified it as unreliable.\n,\nIbn Al-Jawzi (Al-‘Ilal Al-Mutanaahiyah) noted that its chain includes Hammad ibn Salamah, whose stepchild allegedly inserted false reports into his books.\n,\nA similar narration from Umm At-Tufayl describes Allah in a human-like form, but Ash-Shawkani (Al-Fawaa’id Al-Majmoo‘ah) labeled it fabricated (mawdhoo‘) due to unreliable narrators.\n,","The Hadith Conflicts with Established Islamic Principles\n,\nDreams of Allah Do Not Reflect His True Form","Seeing Allah in a dream is possible, but it does not represent His actual essence, as nothing resembles Him.\n,\n\"There is nothing like Him, and He is the All-Hearer, the All-Seer.\" [Ash-Shura 42:11]\n,\n,","Seeing Allah in This World is Impossible","In this life, no one can see Allah directly. The greatest reward for believers is seeing Him in the Hereafter.\n,\n\"[Some] faces, that Day, will be radiant, Looking at their Lord.\" [Al-Qiyamah 75:22-23]\n,\nHadith evidence: Sahih al-Bukhari (6088, 6883) & Sahih Muslim (267, 1002).\n,\n,","Even the Prophets did not see Allah in this world.\nWhen Musa (AS) requested to see Him, Allah replied: \"You cannot see Me.\" [Al-A'raf 7:143]\n,\n,","False Dreams Contradicting Islam are from Satan","Any dream that contradicts Islamic teachings—such as instructing a person to abandon a pillar of Islam—is false and likely a deception from Satan.\n,\n,"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #allah-came-in-a-dream-as-a-young-boy","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368221828811587685"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#allah-came-in-a-dream-as-a-young-boy)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-does-allah-wonder-quran-37-12"],{"title":"Does allah wonder quran 37 12","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Does allah wonder quran 37 12","tree":{"they":"Does allah wonder quran 37 12","we":"The verse reads: The claim is that this is a contradiction between two recitations of the Quran, Hafs and Khalaf.","more":{"h":"The verse reads:","p":["The verse reads:","The claim is that this is a contradiction between two recitations of the Quran, Hafs and Khalaf. However, there is no contradiction here, and the original claimant seems to be ignorant of what a contradiction is; there’s no reason both can’t be true at the same time. The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ wondered, and Allah also wondered. The claim is akin to the following reasoning:",">Your Mother knows your age\n>God knows your age\n>Therefore, contradiction","The same way it isn’t contradictory for your Mother to perform a certain action, and for God to perform that same action at the same time, it also isn’t contradictory for Allah and the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ to do so.","Now, here’s an example of a real contradiction:","Acts 1:18-20 reads:","Matthew 27:5-10 reads:"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #does-allah-wonder-quran-37-12","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222022358011975"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Now, these two accounts are contradictory in that Acts has the field called “Field of Blood” because Judas bought the field, and then died in it, while Matthew has the field called “Field of Blood” because Judas hanged h…","more":{"h":"Does allah wonder quran 37 12","p":["Now, these two accounts are contradictory in that Acts has the field called “Field of Blood” because Judas bought the field, and then died in it, while Matthew has the field called “Field of Blood” because Judas hanged himself, and then the priests used his money to buy the field. Since Judas can't have bought the field in both accounts, because Acts has him die after the field was bought and Matthew has him die before, these two verses constitute a contradiction.","However, this definition of a contradiction does not apply to the different recitations of Quran 37:12, as there’s no reason the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and Allah can’t “wonder” at the same time. Thus, there is no contradiction regarding said Quran verse.","Moreover, one shouldn't confuse the wondering of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ which the wondering of Allah; they technically do the same action, but the action by Allah is incomparable to that of a creation. This is an example of analogical predication:","\"The third sort of predication is analogical predication: the term is not predicated from both entities in exactly the same way (univocally), nor is merely the same word used with totally different meanings (equivocally), but there is similarity as well as difference\" (https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/10638512211017525?icid=int.sj-full-text.similar-articles.2#:~:text=The%20third%20sort%20of%20predication,similarity%20as%20well%20as%20difference. )","This verse is an example of this phenomenon. We can confirm this based off of the Tafsir of at-Tabari, one of the earliest commentaries on this verse:"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #does-allah-wonder-quran-37-12","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222022358011975"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"\"If someone were to ask: How can the reader of these two verses be correct when their meanings differ?","more":{"h":"Does allah wonder quran 37 12","p":["\"If someone were to ask: How can the reader of these two verses be correct when their meanings differ? The answer would be: Even though their meanings differ, each of their meanings is correct. Muhammad was amazed at the bounty Allah had bestowed upon him, and the polytheists mocked him. And our Lord was amazed at the enormity of what the polytheists said about Allah, and the polytheists mocked what they said\" (Tafsir at-Tabari 21/23)","Here, although both readings use the same term, \"wonder\", it is different for Allah and the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ; Allah was amazed at the enormity of what they said, while the Prophet ﷺ was amazed at what Allah had given him.\n‎","It is important to note that the wondering of Allah does not imply that He was surprised or deficient in knowledge, as He is the All-Knowing. It is wrong to say that any action of Allah is done in the same way our actions are, as Allah explicitly says:","Hence, His doing certain actions that, although they hold similarities to ours, are always in a manner that befits him, and cannot be perfectly compared to any actions we do."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #does-allah-wonder-quran-37-12","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222022358011975"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#does-allah-wonder-quran-37-12)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-everything-is-made-in-pairs"],{"title":"Everything is made in pairs","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Everything is made in pairs","tree":{"they":"Everything is made in pairs","we":"The verse reads: The claim is that this is incorrect, as there are things that exist which are not in pairs; this is mainly due to the interpretation that this verse refers to pairs of men and women.","more":{"h":"The verse reads:","p":["The verse reads:","The claim is that this is incorrect, as there are things that exist which are not in pairs; this is mainly due to the interpretation that this verse refers to pairs of men and women. However, the earliest tafsir of this verse, from Muqatil bin Suleiman, says otherwise:","Translation: {And of everything We have created pairs} meaning two types, meaning night and day, this world and the Hereafter, the sun and the moon, land and sea, winter and summer, cold and heat, plains and mountains, salt marshes and freshwater” (Tafsir Muqatil bin Suleiman)","We can see that, instead of males and females, the verse refers to the parallels found within nature. Thus, it would not be correct to call this contradictory to empirical science on the basis that there are creatures without males or females.","Additionally, the “all things” aspect of this verse is not necessarily absolute. There are places in the Quran where Allah speaks of a group, but what He’s saying is not an absolute description of that group. Take, for example, the story of Iblis’ denial:","This verse has the angels being commanded to prostrate, and they do prostrate; however, Allah says, “except for Iblis.” One might see this as implying that Iblis was an angel, but this isn’t true because Allah explicitly states that he was a Jinn:"],"imgs":7,"credit":"Deenresponds · #everything-is-made-in-pairs","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222058349203466"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Hence, we see that Quranic language, even when speaking about absolutes, just refers to the mass majority of instances, not absolutely every single one.","more":{"h":"Everything is made in pairs","p":["Hence, we see that Quranic language, even when speaking about absolutes, just refers to the mass majority of instances, not absolutely every single one. Therefore, the claim is incorrect as a result of the most classical interpretations, as well as through the overall language of the Quran."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #everything-is-made-in-pairs","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222058349203466"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#everything-is-made-in-pairs)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-uzayr-being-the-son-of-allah"],{"title":"Uzayr being the son of allah","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Uzayr being the son of allah","tree":{"they":"Uzayr being the son of allah","we":"The verse reads: The claim is that the Quran is mistaken here, as Jews have never called Ezra the son of Allah/God.","more":{"h":"The verse reads:","p":["The verse reads:","The claim is that the Quran is mistaken here, as Jews have never called Ezra the son of Allah/God. This claim is false, as the “Jews” being referenced here are either a singular individual or a small group of them. This is supported by Tafsir at-Tabari, an early exegesis of the Quran, which mentions these as possible opinions, and doesn’t say the verse applies to all Jews:","Translation: “Abu Ja'far said: The commentators differed about who said, 'Ezra is the son of God.’ Some of them said, ‘It was a single man, namely Finhas.’","Those who said this:","16619 - Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying, Al-Husayn narrated to us, saying, Hajjaj narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, saying, ‘I heard Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umair say, 'And the Jews say, 'Ezra is the son of God.’’ He said, ‘It was a single man who said it. They said, 'His name was Phinehas.' They said, 'He is the one who said, 'Indeed, God is poor, and we are rich.’’ [Surah Al Imran: 181]” (Tafsir at-Tabari)","At-Tabari also mentions how some people thought it was a small group of Jews:"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #uzayr-being-the-son-of-allah","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222108945088522"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Translation: “Salam ibn Mishkam, Nu'man ibn Awfa, Sha's ibn Qays, and Malik ibn al-Sayf came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ‘How can we follow you when you have abandoned our Qibla,…","more":{"h":"Uzayr being the son of allah","p":["Translation: “Salam ibn Mishkam, Nu'man ibn Awfa, Sha's ibn Qays, and Malik ibn al-Sayf came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ‘How can we follow you when you have abandoned our Qibla, and you do not claim that Ezra is the son of God?’ So, in response to their words, Allah revealed [Quran 9:30]” (Tafsir at-Tabari)","One must also note the general structure of at-Tabari’s Tafisr; he mentions all opinions accessible to him. Therefore, we can conclude that the verse, Quran 9:30, means that either a single man or a small group believed this; in no way does this reference the beliefs of wider Judaism.","We must also take into account the language of the Quran itself when it says “the Jews” said something. For example, Quran 5:64 says:","The earliest commentator on this verse, Muqatil bin Suleiman, commented:","Translation: “(And the Jews said), meaning Ibn Suriya and Finhas, the two Jews, and Azar ibn Abi Azar” (Tafsir Muqatil bin Suleiman)","We can see that this verse, although it uses the same statement “the Jews said”, was referring to a mere group of 3 people: Ibn Suriya, Finhas, and Azar ibn abi Azar. Note how Finhas has reappeared, the same one charged with saying whats mentioned in 9:30, according to the “One person” interpretation. This means that the statement of the Quran, “the Jews said”, doesn’t reference all of Judaism, but, instead, a small number of them near the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. Hence, the original claim is invalid."],"imgs":4,"credit":"Deenresponds · #uzayr-being-the-son-of-allah","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222108945088522"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#uzayr-being-the-son-of-allah)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-jesus-never-said-ahmed"],{"title":"Jesus never said ahmed","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"5 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Jesus never said ahmed","tree":{"they":"Jesus never said ahmed","we":"The claim is that Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام, before Islam, has never been documented to talk about an “Ahmad” coming after him.","more":{"h":"Jesus never said ahmed","p":["The claim is that Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام, before Islam, has never been documented to talk about an “Ahmad” coming after him. Islam, therefore, must be wrong. This is wrong for several reasons.","This is not a Written Statement of Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام\n,\n,\nThis verse, in the Quran, never claims that this statement of Jesus was written down. Other places in the Quran do make this claim, which this passage is in contrast with:"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-never-said-ahmed","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222148484665365"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"This verse, Quran 7:157, explicitly states that the description of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was written down, and is accessible through what remains of the Torah and Gospel.","more":{"h":"Jesus never said ahmed","p":["This verse, Quran 7:157, explicitly states that the description of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was written down, and is accessible through what remains of the Torah and Gospel. Note how such language is absent from the passage that says Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام prophesied the coming of a messenger named Ahmad.","This Argument is Falacious\n,\n,\nSeeing the Quran claim that Jesus predicted the coming of an Ahmad, noticing how it isn’t written in any historical works we have, and concluding that the claim is false, is an argument from silence, which is when one concludes through lack of evidence. Although arguments from silence aren’t always fallacious, when one would expect evidence to be present, it is in this case. This reasoning is synonymous with the following:",">Claim Abraham never existed\n>Point out how there is no archaeological evidence for the existence of Abraham\n>Conclude that Abraham never existed","This reasoning would also be fallacious because the existence of archaeological evidence is not necessitated by the existence of Abraham. In contrast, an example of where an argument from silence wouldn’t be fallacious is the following hypothetical:",">Claim George Bush never existed\n>Bring up a lack of evidence for his existence\n>Reason that he supposedly lived in a time when myriad people were literate, many people witnessed him, he was very recent, and people would have surely written about him\n>Conclude that George Bush never existed","This hypothetical wouldn’t be fallacious because you would expect there to be evidence present/ evidence is necessitated by the existence of George Bush/ it is highly implausible to say that he did exist, if the evidence is missing.","Concerning the verse, 61:6, the reasoning is a fallacious argument from silence; the New Testament itself even admits that Jesus said and did many things which were not recorded, in places like John 21:25 and John 20:30:"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-never-said-ahmed","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222148484665365"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Could Fit as the Paraklete Sayings , , The Paraklete prophecy in the Gospel of John could be seen as the remnants of this prophecy about an Ahmed: (Also, it is quite clear that the prophecies don't refer to the Holy Spir…","more":{"h":"Could Fit as the Paraklete Sayings","p":["Could Fit as the Paraklete Sayings\n,\n,\nThe Paraklete prophecy in the Gospel of John could be seen as the remnants of this prophecy about an Ahmed:","(Also, it is quite clear that the prophecies don't refer to the Holy Spirit; see ⁠paraklete-prophecy for more)","This conjecture is a possibility; note John 14:16:","The Greek for “advocate” is παράκλητος/Parakletos. If we took the Arabic term “Ahmad” and tried to represent it in Greek, the closest we would get is περικλυτός/Periklutos. Its possible that Periklutos was the original term used in this passage. However, this remains only a possibility, as there aren’t any manuscripts that include Periklutos in place of Parakletos. On a side note, this has no impact on the argument that the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ fits the prophesied Paraclete. The point is, Christians are willing to concede numerous scribal errors in manuscript copying, many, if not all, of which have no manuscripts that support the idea of scribal error. For example, 1 Chronicles 21:5 vs 2 Samuel 24:9"],"imgs":4,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-never-said-ahmed","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222148484665365"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"If Christians are willing to claim scribal error on many sets of verses that lack manuscripts to support such claims, there is less reason to conclude that the right term in the Paraklete Saying, although different in th…","more":{"h":"Jesus never said ahmed","p":["If Christians are willing to claim scribal error on many sets of verses that lack manuscripts to support such claims, there is less reason to conclude that the right term in the Paraklete Saying, although different in that multiple verses use it, can’t be περικλυτός/Periklutos in place of παράκλητος/Parakletos.","Additionally, its possible that in Quran 61:6, Jesus عَلَیهِ‌السَّلام was quoting Isaiah 42, which wouldn't be unusual because he's known to often quote from the Old Testament. This is important because Isaiah 42 talks about a servant using the term אתמך, \"etmek\" which is strikingly similar to the Hebrew term אחמד, \"ackamed\" which is Hebrew for \"Ahmad\". Due to how similar the words are, and keeping in mind how open Christians are to accepting scribal error, its entirely possible that אחמד, \"ackamed\" was the original word, and the Quran verse speaks on Jesus quoting said verse. Also, its important that its possible \"Ahmad\" appears in Isaiah 42 because it clearly refers to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ: ⁠unknown","In summary, the argument that Islam is wrong due to Quran 61:6 is flawed; although there are possible places where this saying of Jesus could’ve been written down, it’s fallacious to expect this to be written down, especially when the Quran doesn’t say this was written, and the New Testament claims Jesus did many things that weren’t written down. Hence, this argument has no weight."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-never-said-ahmed","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222148484665365"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Second Response: Jesus did say Ahmed in Meaning!","more":{"h":"Second Response: Jesus did say Ahmed in Meaning!","p":["Second Response: Jesus did say Ahmed in Meaning!\n,","There is a respectable position in scholarship that jesus envisioned a salvific figure who is distinct from himself that will come in the future!","One example of a scholar holding this view is Bart Erhman","4 Add Reaction"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-never-said-ahmed","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222148484665365"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#jesus-never-said-ahmed)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","women","d-dr-quran-4-34-beating-your-wife"],{"title":"Qurʾān 4:34","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"5 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Qurʾān 4:34","tree":{"they":"Qurʾān 4:34","we":"“Bukhari 5825 Shows the Prophet Muhammad [ﷺ] Siding with a Wife Beater” , Critics argue that this hadith, which seemingly shows the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ siding with a man who beat his wife.","more":{"h":"“Bukhari 5825 Shows the Prophet Muhammad [ﷺ] Siding with a Wife Beater”","p":["“Bukhari 5825 Shows the Prophet Muhammad [ﷺ] Siding with a Wife Beater”\n,\nCritics argue that this hadith, which seemingly shows the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ siding with a man who beat his wife. However, this ignores the context. This is the full hadith:","We can see that the woman divorced a man named Rifa’a, but then wanted to return to him. Commentaries say that this was the third time they had divorced; in Islamic law, those who have married and divorced each other 3 times may not remarry unless they consummate a marriage with someone else. This is exactly what the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ explained to this woman. The significance of this is that this woman was attempting to find a loophole: she wanted an excuse to divorce her current husband so she could return to Rifa’a. Since she was involved in such suspicious and untrustworthy behavior. As for the bruises the woman had, she potentially bruised herself. This inference is logical, as she’s proven to be untrustworthy. The Prophet ﷺ, hence, didn’t side with her.","“Bukhari 8:82:827 & 8:82:828 show Abu Bakr Punching Aisha in front of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ”\n,\nThe hadiths read:"],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-4-34-beating-your-wife","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222209558052894"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Here, during times of war (both hadiths are found in book 82 of Sahih Bukhari, which is titled the Book of Disbelievers, specifically having wars with them), Abu Bakr discipled Aisha in front of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ.","more":{"h":"Qurʾān 4:34","p":["Here, during times of war (both hadiths are found in book 82 of Sahih Bukhari, which is titled the Book of Disbelievers, specifically having wars with them), Abu Bakr discipled Aisha in front of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. There are a few things to note:","The Prophet ﷺ was asleep\n,\nAisha specifies that she didn’t move, fearing that she would wake the Prophet ﷺ. This indicates that he was asleep, and one shouldn’t, therefore, expect him to condemn Abu Bakr","The Companions aren’t perfect\n,\nJust like other human beings, Abu Bakr can do things out of anger, as long as they aren't degrading to his character. We can say that punching Aisha here was wrong.","The Relationship between Abu Bakr and Aisha\n,\nThis is quite noteworthy, as Aisha is the daughter of Abu Bakr. These hadith are of a father discipling his daughter. Even if one were to ignore the aforementioned and the Prophet ﷺ hypothetically did allow this action, Abu Bakr doing this to his daughter doesn’t mean beating your wife is allowed. This would fall under the false equivocation fallacy, and it doesn’t justify interpreting 4:34 as a harsh beating.","“Sahih Muslim 974b Says The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ Painfully Shoved Aisha”\n,\nThe relevant parts of the hadith are as follows:"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-4-34-beating-your-wife","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222209558052894"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The phrase “nudge in the chest which I felt” is sometimes translated as “struck me on the chest which caused me pain” or “he gave me a painful shove on the chest.” Even if the “worst” of these translations is to be taken…","more":{"h":"Qurʾān 4:34","p":["The phrase “nudge in the chest which I felt” is sometimes translated as “struck me on the chest which caused me pain” or “he gave me a painful shove on the chest.” Even if the “worst” of these translations is to be taken, we would then say that the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ struck Aisha on the chest, and she felt pain. If someone wanted to hit their wife, they would not resort to a mere push, shove, or nudge; such a person would undoubtedly begin beating their wife with their knuckles or the like. Note that this is not present here.","Also, if what Aisha felt was pain, as some translations would suggest, why does the conversation continue in a peaceful manner? If it truly happened as the critics claim, Aisha would’ve reacted to the pain and made her feelings known. The fact, that she didn’t, weakens this interpretation.","Moreover, such translations are flawed; the word, translated as shove more so refers to a poke or general application of pressure:","(https://islamqa.info/en/answers/164216/did-the-prophet-blessings-and-peace-of-allah-be-upon-him-ever-hit-his-wife-aaishah-may-allah-be-pleased-with-her )\nDid the Prophet (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) ever hit...\nDid the Prophet (blessings and peace of Allah be upon him) ever hit..."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-4-34-beating-your-wife","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222209558052894"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The more correct understanding is that the Prophet ﷺ did not hit or beat his wife brutally, but rather that he poked or pushed her in a way that she could feel it, to teach and point something out.","more":{"h":"Qurʾān 4:34","p":["The more correct understanding is that the Prophet ﷺ did not hit or beat his wife brutally, but rather that he poked or pushed her in a way that she could feel it, to teach and point something out. If Aisha did feel pain, it was mild and unintended by the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ.","In summary, this doesn’t prove that the Prophet ﷺ intended to cause her pain; if she felt pain, he either pushed slightly too hard, or her body couldn’t take the push that he had given.","Additionally, Aisha herself mentions in another hadith:","Since Aisha herself believed that the Prophet ﷺ never beat anyone except in times of war, this means that she didn’t consider the prior event a beating or an attack. It’s also important to note that this was not out of character for the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, as in another narration it’s mentioned that he lightly struck (same word used in 4:34) the shoulder of one of his companions to teach him a lesson, not to cause harm:","In another narration, the Prophet ﷺ, again, lightly strikes (same word used in 4:34) the chest of another one of his companions to rectify his doubts, not to cause harm:"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-4-34-beating-your-wife","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222209558052894"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Thus, critics are wrong to try to impose their interpretation upon what the Prophet ﷺ did with Aisha, when it wasn’t out of character for him to do, nor was it to cause harm.","more":{"h":"Qurʾān 4:34","p":["Thus, critics are wrong to try to impose their interpretation upon what the Prophet ﷺ did with Aisha, when it wasn’t out of character for him to do, nor was it to cause harm. To the contrary, the hadiths mentioned above support the “light beating” interpretation of 4:34, as they use the same diction the verse utilized.","“Abu Dawood 2142 States that ‘A man will not be asked as to why he beats his wife’”*\n,\nThis is a weak hadith. Although some scholars, like al-Bani, found it hassan, that doesn’t change the fact that it’s weak.","And even if we take this hadith to be authentic it doesn’t then mean beating is allowed. To not undermine the man’s authority in the household and exacerbate the situation a man shouldn’t be questioned about his misjudgements. It’s like a king leading his people and in front of everyone the king is criticised, the people will lose faith in the kings competency as ruler."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-4-34-beating-your-wife","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222209558052894"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#quran-4-34-beating-your-wife)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","women","d-dr-quran-65-4"],{"title":"Quran 65 4","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Quran 65 4","tree":{"they":"Quran 65 4","we":"So we know that this is a girl who has not menstruated yet due to young age.","more":{"h":"Quran 65 4","p":["so we know that this is a girl who has not menstruated yet due to young age. However does that mean this gir; is pre pubescent? No. Because menstruation comes at the second last stage of puberty. So this verse is discussing those who havent reached the age of menstruation but have reached puberty.","this depiction shows a woman’s whole body doesn’t morph into a woman after menstruation. She can be pubescent and ready to have sex before menstruation.","here are references backing up the commentary on 65:4","Argument from the Fitra","Another argument is to say that Allah swt would never legislate that pre pubescent consummation is ok, because being sexually attracted to a. prepubescent child is against the natural disposition of man."],"imgs":6,"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-65-4","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222256400040049"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"This is in the book al-Mabsut by Shams al-A'immah al-Sarakhsi proving its abnormal because there’s no hadd , Because it becomes evident that she was a proper locus for that act when she was capable of intercourse.","more":{"h":"This is in the book al-Mabsut by Shams al-A'immah al-Sarakhsi proving its abnormal because there’s no hadd","p":["This is in the book al-Mabsut by Shams al-A'immah al-Sarakhsi proving its abnormal because there’s no hadd\n,","Because it becomes evident that she was a proper locus for that act when she was capable of intercourse. And since the prescribed hadd punishment is legislated as a deterrent, and deterrence is only legislated regarding matters toward which human nature inclines — and the natural disposition of rational people does not incline toward intercourse with a young girl who is neither desired nor capable of intercourse — therefore no hadd punishment is applied to him; however, he is subject to discretionary punishment (taʿzīr) for committing something unlawful."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-65-4","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222256400040049"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#quran-65-4)."}});
topic(["islam","hadith","d-dr-the-prophets-aorta-severed"],{"title":"The prophets aorta severed","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"The prophets aorta severed","tree":{"they":"The prophets aorta severed","we":"In the hadith however the prophet SAWS didn’t experience a swift death it was slow even after feeling the pain of the poison at khaybar 3) If one wants to take an ultra literal interpretation it doesn’t make any sense.","more":{"h":"The prophets aorta severed","p":["in the hadith however the prophet SAWS didn’t experience a swift death it was slow even after feeling the pain of the poison at khaybar","3) If one wants to take an ultra literal interpretation it doesn’t make any sense. If we take an approach whereby we say the quran is merely utilising an idiom to denote an immediate death it would make a lot more sense with the seizing of the hand. But even if one takes a literal approach to try and force a link with the hadith it destroys their point because the prophet was never seized by his right hand","4) The “Wateen” is the Thoracic Aorta","While the “Abhar” is the abdominal aorta.","This is mentioned in classical arabic dictionaries. Although some lexicons do say they are the same it’s merely because the Wateen is part of the abhar which makes one aorta.","So even under this lexical usage of the terms, the claimant still has to prove when the prophet SAWS said “abhar” he specifically meant the part that includes the “wateen”","5) the hadith is merely an idiom","in conclusion this claim can be refuted in many different ways all being seen to be viable and doesn’t require any mental gymnastics at all. No one used this as an argument early on and only these fools in the modern age equivocating on arabic terms while being ignorant of arab idioms use this argument to their own embarrassment"],"imgs":5,"credit":"Deenresponds · #the-prophets-aorta-severed","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222302218621089"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#the-prophets-aorta-severed)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-what-is-the-injil"],{"title":"What is the injil","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"What is the injil","tree":{"they":"What is the injil","we":"The Quran mentions a parable about the companions being mentioned there found in matthew There’s a parallel in the quran here with the gospel of matthew again showing jesus parables are revelation in parts within the gos…","more":{"h":"The Quran mentions a parable about the companions being mentioned there found in matthew","p":["The Quran mentions a parable about the companions being mentioned there found in matthew","There’s a parallel in the quran here with the gospel of matthew again showing jesus parables are revelation in parts within the gospels","Parable in Matthew 20 about a vineyard seen in a hadith","The Banquet In luke:","In Luke he also identifies the kingdom of god as being part of the gospel he is preaching. We believe that the muslims brought about the kingdom of God and that jesus was talking about them.\nTo add onto this, the Qur'an says that Jesus gave glad tidings/good news of Ahmad which is identical to the good news of the kingdom of God."],"imgs":9,"credit":"Deenresponds · #what-is-the-injil","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222344123908256"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Injil is likely most similar to ethiopic ,","more":{"h":"Injil is likely most similar to ethiopic","p":["Injil is likely most similar to ethiopic\n,"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #what-is-the-injil","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222344123908256"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#what-is-the-injil)."}});
topic(["islam","creed","d-dr-allah-deceives"],{"title":"Allah deceives","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Allah deceives","tree":{"they":"Allah deceives","we":"God says in the new testament (cited in the above commentary 2 thessalonians 2:11) for rejecting truth and accepting falsehood of the anti christ god will send them a delusion so they can believe the lie Another response…","more":{"h":"Allah deceives","p":["God says in the new testament (cited in the above commentary 2 thessalonians 2:11) for rejecting truth and accepting falsehood of the anti christ god will send them a delusion so they can believe the lie","Another response is to point out that certain attributes can be of perfection or of deficiency. We would understand what the word signifies based on the context.","The objections are based on the claim that God deceiving someone is against His nature because deception is a detestable act. This would entail conflicting attributes.","To deceive or mislead are generally deficient or detestable traits, especially when unprovoked. However, when someone is on the receiving end of deception, it is a praiseworthy trait to retaliate and beat them at their own game. It shows that you are capable and have more power than the one initiating. If a person allows himself to be deceived, he has deficiencies such as being unaware, lacking foresight and being unwise.","Thus, when these words are attributed to subjects that fall into the first category, they are deficiencies. When they are retaliatory and justified, they are praiseworthy.","The following passage of القواعد المثلى (Al-Qawaa’id al-Muthlaa) by Shaykh Muhammad Bin Saalih al-Uthaymeen r.a. expresses this point in detail:"],"imgs":7,"credit":"Deenresponds · #allah-deceives","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222385085616218"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#allah-deceives)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-islamic-dilemma"],{"title":"Islamic dilemma","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Islamic dilemma","tree":{"they":"Islamic dilemma","we":"Moses sees god vs he doesn’t see god difference between adam and eve they get forgiven David and possibility of sin here but not major sin Torah can be used in two ways as ibn qayim puts it^ Hilary of poiters (4th centur…","more":{"h":"Islamic dilemma","p":["Moses sees god vs he doesn’t see god","difference between adam and eve they get forgiven","David and possibility of sin here but not major sin","Torah can be used in two ways as ibn qayim puts it^","Hilary of poiters (4th century church father) believes that Jesus did a general confirmation of the pharisees oral teachings and that’s why the septuagint was translated so well. It was because they possessed these oral traditions to help them translate the more ambiguous passages.","2 2 Add Reaction"],"imgs":8,"credit":"Deenresponds · #islamic-dilemma","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222423878471710"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#islamic-dilemma)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","d-dr-satanic-verses-debunked"],{"title":"Satanic verses debunked","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Satanic verses debunked","tree":{"they":"Satanic verses debunked","we":"\"Thus, many people used to deny this, even if they allowed for other possibilities regarding him, whether before prophethood or after it, due to their assumption that this would imply an error in delivering the message, …","more":{"h":"Satanic verses debunked","p":["\"Thus, many people used to deny this, even if they allowed for other possibilities regarding him, whether before prophethood or after it, due to their assumption that this would imply an error in delivering the message, and he is infallible in delivering the message by consensus. The agreed-upon infallibility is that he cannot persist in an error in delivering the message by consensus. Therefore, it is not known that any of the polytheists ever became alienated from him because of this. Rather, it was reported that they became alienated when he returned to condemning their idols after they thought he had praised them. Thus, their alienation was due to his persistence in condemning their idols, not because he said something and then claimed that Satan had cast it upon him.","If this did not cause alienation, then other things are even less likely to do so. Moreover, it is established that abrogation (of previous rulings) alienated some groups, as stated: ‘The foolish among the people will say, “What has turned them away from their qiblah (direction of prayer) which they used to face?”’ [Surah Al-Baqarah: 142]. And His saying: ‘And when We replace a verse in place of another – and Allah knows best what He reveals – they say, “You are but an inventor [of lies].” But most of them do not know. Say, “The Holy Spirit has brought it down from your Lord in truth to strengthen those who believe.”’ [Surah An-Nahl: 101-102].","Thus, the substitution that they explicitly stated was alienating and used to drive people away from him was not something that must be denied about him. How, then, with returning to the truth – something that has not been known to alienate them – which is far less alienating? For abrogation involves transitioning from one truth to another truth, while this involves returning to the truth from something that is not the truth."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #satanic-verses-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222459995619349"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Allah, the Exalted, said regarding Dawud (David, peace be upon him): \"And Dawud became certain that We had tested him, and he asked forgiveness of his Lord and fell down bowing [in prostration] and turned in repentance.","more":{"h":"Allah, the Exalted, said regarding Dawud (David, peace be upon him):","p":["Allah, the Exalted, said regarding Dawud (David, peace be upon him):","\"And Dawud became certain that We had tested him, and he asked forgiveness of his Lord and fell down bowing [in prostration] and turned in repentance. So We forgave him that, and indeed, for him is nearness to Us and a good place of return\" [Surah Sad: 24–25].","And He said to Musa (Moses, peace be upon him):","\"Indeed, the messengers do not fear in My presence, except he who has wronged; then substituted good after evil—indeed, I am Forgiving and Merciful\" [Surah An-Naml: 10–11].","As for the argument that it is impossible for prophets to err because they are meant to be followed and one cannot follow a sin, it is said to such a person: One is only commanded to follow what the prophets were affirmed and approved upon, not what they were prohibited from. Similarly, one follows them in what they were affirmed upon and not abrogated, and not in what was abrogated.","Thus, emulating them becomes a legislated and commanded practice. This does not negate the possibility of them doing something prohibited,*for which they are corrected and not affirmed upon. Nor does it negate the occurrence of abrogation in some commands, even though it is agreed upon that following abrogated laws is not permissible.","What further clarifies this point is that abrogation creates a greater aversion for people. When a person transitions from one position to another and states: \"What I was upon before was the truth, commanded by Allah, and my transition from it is also the truth, commanded by Allah,\" this is more likely to create hesitation than if one were to say: \"I abandoned what Allah did not command me to do.\"","Indeed, everyone praises the one who says the latter. However, for the one who says, \"My command for this was true, and my prohibition from it is also true,\" this creates aversion among many ignorant individuals and is rejected by some, including the Jews and others."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #satanic-verses-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222459995619349"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The Christian hypocrisy Christian’s believe that bad fruits = someone being a false prophet.","more":{"h":"The Christian hypocrisy","p":["The Christian hypocrisy","Christian’s believe that bad fruits = someone being a false prophet. And bad fruits here is characterised as bad deeds as mentioned by augustine.","John chrysostom wrestles with the idea that this would mean that true prophets like david in the old testament were false prophets. However he reconciles this by saying a prophet can turn into a false prophet and later be redeemed as a true one.","“What then? Did not David, being good, bear evil fruit? Not continuing good, but being changed; since, undoubtedly, had he remained always what he was, he would not have brought forth such fruit. For not surely while abiding in the habit of virtue, did he commit what he committed.”","The Difference between Christianity’s standards and Islam’s","Here we see a christian has no problem with a prophet becoming a false prophet while intentionally doing sin and after rectifying his behaviour, as christian’s believe david died was a prophet.","But they have a problem with a prophet making a mistake caused by satan and god immediately rectifying it afterwards…"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #satanic-verses-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368222459995619349"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#satanic-verses-debunked)."}});
topic(["christianity","church","d-dr-origen-of-alexandria"],{"title":"Origen of alexandria","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Origen of alexandria","tree":{"they":"Origen of alexandria","we":"Origen Uses John 17:3 to prove that the Father is the only True God and that jesus is a lesser god Commentary on the Gospel of John, Book 2, Chapter 2 Origen is a pretty straightforward case here.","more":{"h":"Origen of alexandria","p":["Origen Uses John 17:3 to prove that the Father is the only True God and that jesus is a lesser god Commentary on the Gospel of John, Book 2, Chapter 2","Origen is a pretty straightforward case here. Even though he did believe the Son was eternally generated from the father he clearly doesn’t believe i the co-equality.","Book - Origen on Prayer Origen links Mark 10:18 as being a reason why you can’t pray to the son.","Website for the book - https://www.tertullian.org/fathers/origen_on_prayer_02_text.htm","another bad ss but in De Principiis by origen, book 1, chap 2, sec 6, he explains the understanding of the son being in the image of the father, and at the end explains what it means where in John 14:9, states “whoever has seen me has seen the father”"],"imgs":5,"credit":"Deenresponds · #origen-of-alexandria","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1366947428040708126"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Live now with rami david wood and co refuse to tise me https://www.youtube.com/live/zKvx_sEdgwg?si=b7dYa1bwu3RfI-YO Muslim ENDS The \"Islamic Dilemma\" in Muslim vs Christian Debate Muslim ENDS The \"Islamic Dilemma\" in Mus…","more":{"h":"Origen of alexandria","p":["live now with rami david wood and co refuse to tise me https://www.youtube.com/live/zKvx_sEdgwg?si=b7dYa1bwu3RfI-YO\nMuslim ENDS The \"Islamic Dilemma\" in Muslim vs Christian Debate\nMuslim ENDS The \"Islamic Dilemma\" in Muslim vs Christian Debate"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #origen-of-alexandria","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1366947428040708126"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#origen-of-alexandria)."}});
topic(["christianity","practice","d-dr-sources"],{"title":"Sources","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Sources","tree":{"they":"Sources","we":"Tertulian “To His Wife” ,","more":{"h":"Tertulian “To His Wife”","p":["Tertulian “To His Wife”\n,"],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #sources","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1423750214967230616"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"@Deen couldn't this be a channel in another category?","more":{"h":"Sources","p":["@Deen \ncouldn't this be a channel in another category? and then we call the channel \"Polygamy in the OT\""],"credit":"Deenresponds · #sources","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1423750214967230616"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#sources)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-disciples-worship-jesus-debunked"],{"title":"Disciples worship jesus debunked","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Disciples worship jesus debunked","tree":{"they":"Disciples worship jesus debunked","we":"These verses portray the angels prostrating to Adam, and Joseph’s parents prostrating to him.","more":{"h":"Disciples worship jesus debunked","p":["These verses portray the angels prostrating to Adam, and Joseph’s parents prostrating to him. This was permissible in the past as a sign of respect and extreme reverence, as Ibn Kathir comments:","In the laws of these and previous Prophets, it was allowed for the people to prostrate before the men of authority, when they met them. This practice was allowed in the law of Adam until the law of `Isa, peace be upon them, but was later prohibited in our law. Islam made prostration exclusively for Allah Alone, the Exalted and Most Honored (Tafsir Ibn Kathir on Quran 12:100)","Instead of the original claim being proven by the aforementioned Gospel verses, this shows that these translations of the Bible are dishonest. This is especially clear after viewing some academic translations of the same verses:","The claim is mistaken; the Gospels do not suggest the disciples worshipped Jesus, but instead show that they prostrated to him, which is entirely acceptable under the Islamic paradigm and does not suggest that he was divine or that he accepted worship.","Nevertheless, one may object based on another verse, which has the disciple John worshiping an angel; the word for worship used is the same Greek word as before, προσεκύνησεν (prosekynēsen), meaning prostration:","This critique is flawed for multiple reasons:","The Elevated Rank of Mankind\n,\n,","The Quran mentions on multiple occasions how God ordered the angels to prostrate towards mankind:","In addition to this, the Quran also explicitly mentions the elevated rank of mankind:"],"imgs":6,"credit":"Deenresponds · #disciples-worship-jesus-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368591010883698768"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"With this in mind, it would be proper for an angel to prostrate to a man, but not for a man to prostrate to an angel; God ordered the angels to prostrate to Adam and elevated the rank of mankind.","more":{"h":"Disciples worship jesus debunked","p":["With this in mind, it would be proper for an angel to prostrate to a man, but not for a man to prostrate to an angel; God ordered the angels to prostrate to Adam and elevated the rank of mankind. The aforementioned verses in Revelation 22, hence, show that man shouldn’t prostrate to angels; they don’t comment on the act of a man prostrating to another man.","Wording\n,\n,\nThe verses in Revelation have the angel saying to John,","“Don't do that!...Worship God”\n (Revelation 22:9)","Note how the angel doesn’t specify that John should onlyworship/prostrate towards God, but that he mentions God as more deserving of worship/prostration than an angel. This means that these verses, again, can’t be used as commentary for mankind prostrating to mankind, and don’t refute the idea that the disciples prostrated to Jesus instead of worshiping him.","Context\n,\n,\nThis verse actually backfires on the critic, as it demonstrates that John, even after Jesus's ministry, understood προσεκύνησεν (prosekynēsen) to not be exclusive to God. This means that when John worshipped Jesus, he did not understand the worship he was doing as a worship exclusive to God. This critique, instead of rebutting the refutation, ends up aiding it."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #disciples-worship-jesus-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368591010883698768"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#disciples-worship-jesus-debunked)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-mark-1-1-3-debunked"],{"title":"Mark 1 1 3 debunked","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Mark 1 1 3 debunked","tree":{"they":"Mark 1 1 3 debunked","we":"Mark 1:1-3 is referring to the preparation by John the Baptist to have the the spirit of the Lord dwell or come upon Jesus(as) and empowers Jesus(as) to do his ministry.","more":{"h":"Mark 1 1 3 debunked","p":["Mark 1:1-3 is referring to the preparation by John the Baptist to have the the spirit of the Lord dwell or come upon Jesus(as) and empowers Jesus(as) to do his ministry. This can be seen by John the Baptist’s baptism which causes the spirit of God to come upon Jesus(as) in Mark 1:10.","This doesn’t entail that Jesus(as) himself is Yahweh, because as we see Mark 1:4 establishes that the baptism of John was for the forgiveness of sins, and so per Mark Jesus(as) had to be baptized to be forgiven of his sins. This would be inconsistent with the gospel of Mark seeing Jesus Christ as God who is sinless.","The spirit of God coming upon Jesus(as) or dwelling within him does not make him divine as the spirit of the lord came upon the tabernacle and the temple but neither of those are seen as divine itself but simply places where the spirit or presence of God was"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark-1-1-3-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368590776958980096"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Response #2: This could also be a case of shaliach or divine agency, where the agent acts as the representative of the individual.","more":{"h":"Mark 1 1 3 debunked","p":["Response #2: This could also be a case of shaliach or divine agency, where the agent acts as the representative of the individual. For instance we read in Exodus that God says that he will put the staff in the water and we find that Aaron puts the staff in this water, now according to your logic this would entail that Aaron(as) himself is Yahweh.","Exodus 7:17-20\nThus says the Lord, “By this you shall know that I am the Lord: behold, with the staff that is in my hand I will strike the water that is in the Nile, and it shall turn into blood. .. 19 And the Lord said to Moses, “Say to Aaron, ‘Take your staff and stretch out your hand over the waters of Egypt, over their rivers, their canals, and their ponds, and all their pools of water, so that they may become blood, and there shall be blood throughout all the land of Egypt, even in vessels of wood and in vessels of stone","All commentaries understand God saying here that the staff is in the hand of Aaron and that he is the one who will do it, but because he is doing the will or action of God, God can identify the actions of Aaron as being done by himself. And so likewise we can say the same about the preparation or the way of the lord referring to a representative of lord who is doing the actions of God on earth."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark-1-1-3-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368590776958980096"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Also Mark 10:18 is way more clear to then any passage someone can bring from mark to insinuate Mark believes in jesus being god like the Father.","more":{"h":"Mark 1 1 3 debunked","p":["Also Mark 10:18 is way more clear to then any passage someone can bring from mark to insinuate Mark believes in jesus being god like the Father. We should use the clear verses to inform our understanding of the implicit verses. And no doubt Mark 10:18 is clear jesus is ontologically subordinate to the Father.","Check out ⁠mark-10-18"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark-1-1-3-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368590776958980096"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#mark-1-1-3-debunked)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-jesus-is-called-lord-debunked"],{"title":"Jesus is called lord debunked","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Jesus is called lord debunked","tree":{"they":"Jesus is called lord debunked","we":"There has long been speculative discourse among apologetics on whether the Greek κύριος (kurios, Strong’s G2962) in the NT, when referring to Jesus, implies divine lordship like that of the Father or human lordship like Abraham.","more":{"h":"Jesus is called lord debunked","p":["There has long been speculative discourse among apologetics on whether the Greek κύριος (kurios, Strong’s G2962) in the NT, when referring to Jesus, implies divine lordship like that of the Father or human lordship like Abraham. In Hebrew, there are three common forms of “lord/master”: אָדוֹן (adon, Strong’s H113), אֲדֹנָי (Adonai, Strong’s H136) and יְהוָה (Yahweh, Strong’s H3068).","Yahweh has always been understood as divine, but if we were to say that Adon was always divine we would have to attribute Abraham and David pbut as divine as well, the issue is that the LXX translate both of these as kurios. we can see this most evidently in Psalms 110:1 where \"the LORD said to my lord\" gets translated to 'the kyrios said to my kyriō'. Please note: The difference in suffix isn't indicating a distinction in human or divine lordship but purely a grammatical one where: κύριος (kyrios) is nominative (subject: \"lord\") and κυρίῳ (kyriō) is dative (indirect object or means: \"to/for/by/in the lord\"). Which means: the ending of the word simply shows whether it's acting as the main subject or as the recipient/object within a sentence.","So if we only have the greek we can only speculate whether the kurios is a Yawhey/ Adonai or Adon as these all get translated equivocally, however we have some prophecies in the OT that keep the hebrew and thus keep the meaning","also important to note, that in the strong's concordances for 113, it says \"it is used to refer to human lords or masters, as well as to God\" in the brown's driver briggs dictionaries when they have a section for \"b. Adonay proper name of God\" the verses they provide seem to all be for strongs 136 rather than strongs 113, i have checked 5 and they were all 136, but i haven't checked every verse in that section"],"imgs":14,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-is-called-lord-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368590745375608922"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"So jesus being called lord is a later interpretation and as a result a translation made with a preconceived idea read into the text of the bible Jesus can not even possibly fulfil the requirements of being Lord like yahw…","more":{"h":"Jesus is called lord debunked","p":["So jesus being called lord is a later interpretation and as a result a translation made with a preconceived idea read into the text of the bible","Jesus can not even possibly fulfil the requirements of being Lord like yahweh as he is missing necessary qualities as a result of him being identified by the early church as the angel of the lord. This results in jesus being contained while. THE LORD can not be contained.","Solomon lays out this being a necessary quality for THE LORD","and jesus lacks it in his PRE INCARNATED (before jesus became a man) state according to early fathers for example:"],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-is-called-lord-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368590745375608922"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#jesus-is-called-lord-debunked)."}});
topic(["christianity","trinity","d-dr-john-1-1-debunked"],{"title":"John 1 1 debunked","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"John 1 1 debunked","tree":{"they":"John 1 1 debunked","we":"Theres so much about john 1:1 but the most summative and academic piece of evidence I have used in the past is here https://www.areopage.net/colwell.pdf it shows grammar rules, and gives sources at the end of the documen…","more":{"h":"John 1 1 debunked","p":["theres so much about john 1:1 but the most summative and academic piece of evidence I have used in the past is here https://www.areopage.net/colwell.pdf it shows grammar rules, and gives sources at the end of the document, I'll also post below a photo of Bart Erhman saying john 1:1-1:18 (the prologue of john) was likely a later addition by scribes so even if john did write john (still highly disputed- but even if we grant it) its highly likely that 'the blessed disciple' never wrote 1:1, 1:14 and 1:18 for example","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Kw3mVyDTLSo\nJesus is NOT the \"Logos\" in John 1 - Part 1 #bible #jesus #islam\nJesus is NOT the \"Logos\" in John 1 - Part 1 #bible #jesus #islam","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NzmVaXlUtTE\nJesus is NOT the \"Logos\" in John 1 - Part 2 with @transfigured3673 ...\nJesus is NOT the \"Logos\" in John 1 - Part 2 with @transfigured3673 ...","https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/e/2PACX-1vSC6AxmAhdN936lB17SevTwxR3cZItP2cmE0giojW1l4UR5MQeKRCgOHlOvVowT8cHCNI4qJSRgRAPw/pub?start=false&loop=false&delayms=3000\nJohn 1 presentation\nJohn 1 presentation\nWho is the “Logos” in John 1:1? In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God (Theon), and the Word was God (Theos). Λόγος - Logos (Word) Θεόν - Theon (God) Θεὸς - Theos (God) Who is the “Word”? Same God mentioned twice or 2 different Gods?"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #john-1-1-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368591306556969050"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#john-1-1-debunked)."}});
topic(["christianity","trinity","d-dr-john-20-28-debunked"],{"title":"John 20 28 debunked","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"John 20 28 debunked","tree":{"they":"According to John 20:28, Jesus was called God by his apostle Thomas and Jesus told him he is blessed if you believe I am God Context First, Jesus isn’t saying that Thomas was blessed for calling him the lord, God but rat…","we":"Now, being called God doesn’t mean someone is consubstantial(possessing the divine essence).","more":{"h":"John 20 28 debunked","p":["Argument\nAccording to John 20:28, Jesus was called God by his apostle Thomas and Jesus told him he is blessed if you believe I am God","Context\nFirst, Jesus isn’t saying that Thomas was blessed for calling him the lord, God but rather, for seeing and believing in the resurrection. When we read verse 24 & 25, Thomas rejected that Jesus has resurrected and wanted evidence. When he got his “evidence” in verse 27, he calls Jesus his God. So we see clearly that Jesus wasn’t saying he was blessed for believing he was God but that he believed in the resurrection.","Refutation\nNow, being called God doesn’t mean someone is consubstantial(possessing the divine essence). “God” was a very loose term in the 1st century and prior. We read that in 2 Corinthians 4:4, Satan was called “Theos”(God), the same word Thomas used to refer to Jesus.","Moses was also “a God” to both Aaron and Pharaoh in the Exodus verses 4:16 and 7:1","So, Jesus simply being called God, does not mean he needs to possess the divine essence or be equal with the father to have this name, just like Satan and Moses. Justin martyr believes that all man are able to becoming God based off psalms 82 when God called a group of Israelites “Gods”.","Dialogue with Trypho Chapter 124","“let the interpretation of the Psalm be held just as you wish, yet thereby it is demonstrated that all men are deemed worthy of becoming \"gods,\" and of having power to become sons of the Highest;”"],"imgs":6,"credit":"Deenresponds · #john-20-28-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368591200764039238"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"This idea that Jesus is co-equal, co-eternal with the father, is an idea that emerged in the 4th by the council of Nicaea.","more":{"h":"John 20 28 debunked","p":["This idea that Jesus is co-equal, co-eternal with the father, is an idea that emerged in the 4th by the council of Nicaea. According to Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, No theologian in the first three centuries was a trinitarian.","The early church fathers understood Jesus as being god in a lesser sense to the father(Subordinationism), not equal.","Conclusion\nJesus being called “God” doesn’t make him co-equal co-eternal with the father just like how Satan, Moses, and a group of Israelites are called “God” but they’re not co-equal co-eternal with the father."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #john-20-28-debunked","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368591200764039238"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#john-20-28-debunked)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-mark-5-30"],{"title":"Mark 5 30","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Mark 5 30","tree":{"they":"Mark 5 30","we":"In Mark 5:30, we read: , At once Jesus realized that power had gone out from him.","more":{"h":"In Mark 5:30, we read:","p":["In Mark 5:30, we read:\n,\nAt once Jesus realized that power had gone out from him. He turned around in the crowd and asked, 'Who touched my clothes?'\"","This passage is problematic when it comes to explaining jesus's divinity, there is an incident here that raises questions about the nature of Isa's divinity.","To break it down, we have to discuss the following:\nLimited Knowledge:\nThe verse indicates that Jesus did not initially know who had touched him. If jesus was god, and god is omniscent, then his lack of immediate knowledge is problematic again. His question, \"Who touched my clothes?\" suggests a moment of uncertainty or the need for further information. Now one might argue that this happens due to his human nature to evade this problem. However, this explanation causes another problem. if Jesus is fully God and fully man, is his divine nature switched off in moments like this? If he is still divine, then any missing knowledge, would be contradicting to that attribute.","Dependence on External Power:\nJesus' acknowledgment that power left him implies that his healing abilities were not inherently his to grant but were only displayed by external faith. This challenges the notion of an all-powerful, self-sustaining deity. It suggests that Jesus' power was dependent on external factors like the woman's faith and isn't at will."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark-5-30","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368592584636760105"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#mark-5-30)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-mark-10-18"],{"title":"Mark 10 18","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Mark 10 18","tree":{"they":"Mark 10 18","we":"@Muslim🌹 do me a favour habibi and transcribe the points from this powerpoint here https://youtu.be/gmaFCMKeDBk?si=gcmMFNAbxqqd-WKX DAWAH BOOTCAMP W/@AliDawah (Episode 1 Mark 10:18) DAWAH BOOTCAMP W/@AliDawah (Episode 1…","more":{"h":"@Muslim🌹","p":["@Muslim🌹","do me a favour habibi and transcribe the points from this powerpoint here","https://youtu.be/gmaFCMKeDBk?si=gcmMFNAbxqqd-WKX\nDAWAH BOOTCAMP W/@AliDawah (Episode 1 Mark 10:18)\nDAWAH BOOTCAMP W/@AliDawah (Episode 1 Mark 10:18)","Presentation 18.pptx 5.21 MB"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark-10-18","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368591752394444800"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#mark-10-18)."}});
topic(["christianity","trinity","d-dr-john-17-3"],{"title":"John 17 3","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"John 17 3","tree":{"they":"John 17 3","we":"Firstly, the internal evidence of the new testament shows us that the father has exclusively been titled titled True God, repeatedly John 17:3 says \"You are the only True God\", 1 thessalonians 1:9-10, \"Serve the living a…","more":{"h":"John 17 3","p":["Firstly, the internal evidence of the new testament shows us that the father has exclusively been titled titled True God, repeatedly","John 17:3 says \"You are the only True God\", 1 thessalonians 1:9-10, \"Serve the living and true God\" referring to the father , 1 John 5:20, him who is true and he is The True God and eternal life, 1 Corinthians 8:6, there is but \"one God\", the Father and one lord , Jesus christ. Distinguishing the \"One God\" title from Jesus and exclusively giving it to the father yet again. In John 5:44, Seek the glory, Jesus says that comes from \"The only God\", so it's very clear the father is represented all across the new testament as having this title exclusively, not once Jesus is titled as The True God so stop your semantical word games, Mr. Doglogic."],"imgs":6,"credit":"Deenresponds · #john-17-3","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368593013735166102"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Secondly, irenaus who is an early churchfather and the author of \"against heresies\" , wrote in his book about this very topic, irenaus was a student of polycarp who is also a churchfather, he is a student of John , the p…","more":{"h":"John 17 3","p":["Secondly, irenaus who is an early churchfather and the author of \"against heresies\" , wrote in his book about this very topic, irenaus was a student of polycarp who is also a churchfather, he is a student of John , the person who wrote the gospel of John according to the Christians, so if anyone was going to give us a theological interpretation of John 17:3, it's going to be irenaus who is a direct student of a student of the author. Now irenaus says regarding John 17:3 that this means no one else besides the father can be called True God and if Jesus and the disciples taught you could call anyone else, True God besides the father then they would have been teachers of transgression, meaning irenaus believes Doglogic is a teacher of transgression for saying you could call anyone but the father , The True God.","https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/0103401.htm\nCHURCH FATHERS: Against Heresies, IV.1 (St. Irenaeus)\nCHURCH FATHERS: Against Heresies, IV.1 (St. Irenaeus)\nFeaturing the Church Fathers, Catholic Encyclopedia, Summa Theologica and more.","https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/0103401.htm\nAlso another point I like to mention is that, Avery actually said explicitly that no Christian believes that jesus isn't the True God, so i guess Avery considers irenaus a kaffir then by that Logic.","Lastly, we have augustine who was a trinitarian and struggled heavily to reconcile the verse with trinitarian doctrine"],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #john-17-3","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368593013735166102"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"So augustine says the proper order of the words is different to what John says, indicating that the trinitarian for augustine Requires distorting the apparent meaning of the text and even when he distorted the apparent m…","more":{"h":"John 17 3","p":["So augustine says the proper order of the words is different to what John says, indicating that the trinitarian for augustine Requires distorting the apparent meaning of the text and even when he distorted the apparent meaning of the text by including Jesus and the father as having the title of True God he came up with a terrible explanation on how the holy spirit is included.","So in Conclusion, We have the new testament itself professing the father as the True God and not once is the Holy spirit or the Son called that title. We also have irenaus a direct student of the student of John, who says anyone who teaches what Avery teaches is a teacher of transgression and finally we have augustine who clearly was coping with the apparent reading of the text and saw it as problematic to the trinitarian Doctrine, try better next time with your weak barking."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #john-17-3","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368593013735166102"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#john-17-3)."}});
topic(["christianity","church","d-dr-no-forgiveness-of-sin-outside-of-shedding-blood"],{"title":"No forgiveness of sin outside of shedding blood","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"5 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"No forgiveness of sin outside of shedding blood","tree":{"they":"No forgiveness of sin outside of shedding blood","we":"The last primary purpose that blood was used for the day of atonement, which is detailed in Leviticus 16.","more":{"h":"No forgiveness of sin outside of shedding blood","p":["The last primary purpose that blood was used for the day of atonement, which is detailed in Leviticus 16. This is a ceremonial sacrifice that took place once per year for all of Israel.","Two goats were taken, one to be sacrificed for the uncleanliness and rebellion of the Israelites, and one to have all of the sins of Israel put on its head.","The goat that had the sins of Israel put on its head is made the \"scapegoat\" and is simply sent out into the wilderness, carrying all the sins. It is not sacrificed; another example of blood not being required."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #no-forgiveness-of-sin-outside-of-shedding-blood","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368286258903908526"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"So what is the main way of seeking forgiveness?","more":{"h":"So what is the main way of seeking forgiveness?","p":["So what is the main way of seeking forgiveness?","Ezekiel 18: 20-22\n\"20 The one who sins is the one who will die. The child will not share the guilt of the parent, nor will the parent share the guilt of the child. The righteousness of the righteous will be credited to them, and the wickedness of the wicked will be charged against them.\" 21 “But if a wicked person turns away from all the sins they have committed and keeps all my decrees and does what is just and right, that person will surely live; they will not die.(AJ) 22 None of the offenses they have committed will be remembered against them. Because of the righteous things they have done, they will live. 23 Do I take any pleasure in the death of the wicked? declares the Sovereign Lord. Rather, am I not pleased when they turn from their ways and live?\"","You'll notice from this passage multiple things that conflict with the crucifixion narrative. For example, one cannot inherit sins, so the concept of original sin is out the window. One cannot pay for the sins of someone else, so Jesus paying for everyone else's sins is also out the window. The way for forgiveness is clear, and is the same as in Islam. You have to turn away from your sins, keep the decrees of God, and you're forgiven. In short, repentance is the key to forgiveness."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #no-forgiveness-of-sin-outside-of-shedding-blood","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368286258903908526"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"\"Say, 'O My servants who have transgressed against themselves [by sinning], do not despair of the mercy of Allāh.","more":{"h":"No forgiveness of sin outside of shedding blood","p":["\"Say, 'O My servants who have transgressed against themselves [by sinning], do not despair of the mercy of Allāh. Indeed, Allāh forgives all sins.1 Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful.'\" Quran 39:53","\"As for those who repent, believe, and do good deeds, they are the ones whose evil deeds Allah will change into good deeds. For Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.\" Quran 25:70","Al-Tirmidhi narrated that Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Allah, may He be blessed and exalted, said: ‘O son of Adam, so long as you call upon Me and ask of Me, I shall forgive you for what you have done, and I shall not mind. O son of Adam, were your sins to reach the clouds of the sky and were you then to ask forgiveness of Me, I would forgive you and I would not mind.’” [Sahih al-Tirmidhi]","Ibn Majah narrated that ‘Abd-Allah ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The one who repents from sin is like one who did not sin.” [Sahih Ibn Majah]","1 John 1:9–10 says, \"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness. If we say that we have not sinned, we make him a liar, and his word is not in us\"","The goat that had the sins of Israel put on its head is made the \"scapegoat\" and is simply sent out into the wilderness, carrying all the sins. It is not sacrificed; another example of blood not being required."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #no-forgiveness-of-sin-outside-of-shedding-blood","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368286258903908526"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"As established earlier, the animal offerings are to be sacrificed for the intentional sins of the people, and very rarely for intentional ones.","more":{"h":"No forgiveness of sin outside of shedding blood","p":["As established earlier, the animal offerings are to be sacrificed for the intentional sins of the people, and very rarely for intentional ones. However, unknown to some people, there are, in fact, three exceptions to this rule.","Swearing an oath, either knowingly or unknowingly, and then breaking it. (Leviticus 5:4-5)\n,\nDeception / Fraud (Leviticus 6:2)\n,\nViolating a betrothed slave woman (Leviticus 19:20-22)\n,\nPlease note that certain rabbis hold the view that there is in fact a fourth exception to this rule, which is breaking the nazarite vow.\nHowever, the point still stands that the sacrifices, generally speaking, are only to be given when the individual sins intentionally.\nWhy is this so problematic?\nThe answer is quite simple.\nChristians believe that Jesus atoned for the entirety of the world's sins by fulfilling the atoning practices of the old testament, including the sacrificial system.\nHowever, the sacrificial system contradicts their doctrine of atonement completely.\nHence, there is a contradiction between the Christian doctrine of atonement, and the old testament.\nChristians have there ways of getting out of this dilemma.","Jesus didn't fulfill the old testament atonement.\n,\nJesus atoned for unintentional sins only.\n,\nthe old testament does not contradict with the Christian doctrine of atonement, argument for that.\n,\nAn argument to prove this will be refuted in the next post."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #no-forgiveness-of-sin-outside-of-shedding-blood","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368286258903908526"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The day of atonement in lev 16 is often brought up to demonstrate that blood does have a roll in atoning sins.","more":{"h":"No forgiveness of sin outside of shedding blood","p":["The day of atonement in lev 16 is often brought up to demonstrate that blood does have a roll in atoning sins. The Christians might use verse 11 and 16 to support their nonsense claims. Such objections will be thoroughly dismanteled.","But kaper is only used when speaking of a blood atonement!\n,","Argument: Some Christians contend that the hebrew word kaper, meaning atonement is found in conjunction with a blood sacrifice only, as it represents a certain clenzing from sin not available without it.","However, the Christian argument is predicated on a lie. The word kaper is used to refer to other things not at all relevant to blood sacrifices, including.\nExodus 30:15; 32:30; Leviticus 5:13; 16:6,10,11; Numbers 17:11; 31:50; Proverbs 16:6)."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #no-forgiveness-of-sin-outside-of-shedding-blood","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368286258903908526"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#no-forgiveness-of-sin-outside-of-shedding-blood)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-deens-paraklete-exegesis-of-john-14"],{"title":"Deens paraklete exegesis of john 14","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Deens paraklete exegesis of john 14","tree":{"they":"Deens paraklete exegesis of john 14","we":"In Luke Chapter 16 verse 29; Jesus(as) gives a parable, in it he quotes Abraham(as) as saying: They have [literally:to possess] Moses and the Prophets, let them HEAR[primary meaning audible] them.","more":{"h":"In Luke Chapter 16 verse 29; Jesus(as) gives a parable, in it he quotes Abraham(as) as saying:","p":["In Luke Chapter 16 verse 29; Jesus(as) gives a parable, in it he quotes Abraham(as) as saying:","They have [literally:to possess] Moses and the Prophets, let them HEAR[primary meaning audible] them.","Now the jews at the time did not literally posess Moses or the prophets neither could they audibly hear them, but they had acess to their teachings and doctrines. This is an example which shows that the paraclete being with the believers does not necessitate him being literally present but could refer either to his teachings or his description being in their foreknowlegde","In John 15:7 Jesus(as) interchanges him abididng in the disciples with his words abiding within the disciples. The word for \"abide\" in john 15:7 is the same word used in john 14:17. Given words cannot literally dwell within induviduals and this is universally interpreted as referring to either his teachings, or the faith. If this is the case then John 14:17, the paraclete dwelling with them can refer to either the revelation/teachings of the paraclete being with them forever. Or it can refer to the disciples being given information on the revelation/teachings/functions of the prophet(SAW)"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #deens-paraklete-exegesis-of-john-14","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368235621570838639"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"As for the words \"because it neither sees him nor knows him.","more":{"h":"Deens paraklete exegesis of john 14","p":["As for the words \"because it neither sees him nor knows him. But you know him, for he lives with you and will be in you\", The term for \"see\" should understand to spiritual insight not literal insight. The world is not receptive or does not have the correct attitude and therefore it cannot accept not because the world does not have the literal eyesight ability to see the Holy Spirit.","Raymond brown notes in his commentary that the world cannot receive him is an issue of attitude, not literally being unable to see the Holy Spirit. The verb of sight in greek can refer to bodily or spiritual insight.","So in this context it would mean the world cannot receive him because they are not ready for him or looking for him, as the NLT translates it as “The world cannot receive him, because it isn’t looking for him and doesn’t recognize him. But you know him, because he lives with you now and later will be in you.” And the world cannot see him spiritually because they are not yet ready for it. But the disciple are, since Jesus has told them about him and are receptive to his coming.","It'd be ridiculous for jesus to be like \"the world can't accept him because the holy spirit is not 3D\"","Hippolytus against noetus^"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #deens-paraklete-exegesis-of-john-14","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368235621570838639"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":":sob: Click to react :smiling_face_with_tear: Click to react :skull: Click to react Add Reaction Forward More “I will send the paraklete” John 15:26 and John 16:7 , @Talib","more":{"h":":sob: Click to react :smilingfacewithtear: Click to react :skull: Click to react Add Reaction Forward More","p":[":sob: Click to react :smiling_face_with_tear: Click to react :skull: Click to react Add Reaction Forward More","“I will send the paraklete” John 15:26 and John 16:7\n,","@Talib"],"imgs":4,"credit":"Deenresponds · #deens-paraklete-exegesis-of-john-14","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368235621570838639"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#deens-paraklete-exegesis-of-john-14)."}});
