topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-isaiah-21"],{"title":"Isaiah 21","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Isaiah 21","tree":{"they":"Isaiah 21","we":"This can’t be individuals if it’s plural so what’s going on here?","more":{"h":"Isaiah 21","p":["This can’t be individuals if it’s plural so what’s going on here? Which reading should we prefer and why is there this difference?","The Hebrew has a plural\n(riders = a|rekhev) but the Arabic is\nsingular (rider = ر|كب|rakib).","Why the muslim translators reading is earliest while the jews have distorted this prophecy in the masonic text:","Many early Texts--such as the famous Isaiah Scroll from Qumran, support the Arabic translatio: reading rokhev (ai,\n'rider' rather than rekhev). Dating around 150BC","The Septuagint , the early Greek translation, also reads: \"I saw two mounted horsemen, and a rider on an ass, and a rider on a camel.\"","Credits: Muslim brothers who aided me and a thread by Sean anthony on twitter. https://x.com/shahansean/status/1162756325463547905\nSean W. Anthony (@shahanSean) on X\nSean W. Anthony (@shahanSean) on X\nThis leaf from a 14th cent. copy of al-Āṯār al-bāqiyah, composed in 1000 CE by the Muslim polymath Abū l-Rayḥān al-Bīrūnī, contains one of my favorite depictions of a biblical passage. It illustrates 3 prophets: Isaiah, Jesus, + Muḥammad. But what’s going one here? A thread …","https://youtu.be/xNz8Rhfirt0\nIsaiah 21 Prophecy of Jesus & Muhammad ﷺ Prophets of Allah\nIsaiah 21 Prophecy of Jesus & Muhammad ﷺ Prophets of Allah"],"imgs":4,"credit":"Deenresponds · #isaiah-21","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368284476127318107"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#isaiah-21)."}});
