topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-isaiah-42"],{"title":"Isaiah 42","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Isaiah 42","tree":{"they":"Isaiah 42","we":"Https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL_W2HLp2VYbjN5efvE5Wy3J47RknS5ZAe Muhammad ‎ﷺ in the Bible Muhammad ‎ﷺ in the Bible https://x.com/vegitowrath/status/1427645614851072020 Vegito (@VegitoWrath) on X Vegito (@VegitoWr…","more":{"h":"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLW2HLp2VYbjN5efvE5Wy3J47RknS5ZAe","p":["https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL_W2HLp2VYbjN5efvE5Wy3J47RknS5ZAe\nMuhammad ‎ﷺ in the Bible\nMuhammad ‎ﷺ in the Bible","https://x.com/vegitowrath/status/1427645614851072020\nVegito (@VegitoWrath) on X\nVegito (@VegitoWrath) on X\nChristopher R. North in his commentary on Isaiah mentions that a lot of commentators believe that the “justice” (mišpāt) which will be brought forth by the servant of Isaiah 42 to the Gentiles is better explained as something similar to the “Arab Dîn” (i.e Islam)","https://x.com/vegitowrath/status/1426929059129405442\nVegito (@VegitoWrath) on X\nVegito (@VegitoWrath) on X\n@Abe_Kuyper @provingislam 1/2 The Qur’an (7:157-158 more specifically) does not quote Isaiah 42 but it strongly alludes to it in both meaning and wording as some modern scholars have pointed out:","dwt justin martyr 65","https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSrANMnGA/\nTikTok · deenrespondsyt\nTikTok · deenrespondsyt","550 likes, 227 comments. “#islam #muslim #quran #hadith @Ahraz @Isayahya7 @AntiShubuhat🦁⚔️ @Anwar @🇩🇴🏴 @AbuNajla @Dawah Over Dunya @Sanza @The Based Bengali @turkishskeptic”","https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSrANrwPw/\nTikTok · deenrespondsyt\nTikTok · deenrespondsyt","375 likes, 82 comments. “#islam #muslim #quran #hadith #sunnah #bible @Ahraz @Isayahya7 @AntiShubuhat🦁⚔️ @Anwar @Ehsan Al-Hanafi @Ibn ash shuwayer @Isa Caba 🇩🇴 @Sanza @Dawah Over Dunya @The Based Bengali @turkishskeptic @Nazam Guffoor”"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #isaiah-42","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1365148240756084747"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Https://x.com/alukbari/status/1958597760317333842?s=46 In a verse of poetry attributed to Waraqa ibn Nawfal in the seerah of Ibn Hishām, Waraqa says about Muḥammad ﷺ: ❝He will shine a bright light in the midst of the nat…","more":{"h":"https://x.com/alukbari/status/1958597760317333842?s=46","p":["https://x.com/alukbari/status/1958597760317333842?s=46\nIn a verse of poetry attributed to Waraqa ibn Nawfal in the seerah of Ibn Hishām, Waraqa says about Muḥammad ﷺ:","❝He will shine a bright light in the midst of the nations… setting with it the wilderness upright, lest it sways.❞","The closest intertext to this is Isaiah 42:16"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #isaiah-42","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1365148240756084747"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#isaiah-42)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-isaiah-45"],{"title":"Isaiah 45","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Isaiah 45","tree":{"they":"Isaiah 45","we":"Https://youtu.be/ZjJ6DcGKU2I?si=raIdu2vRK4lfFAHQ Isaiah 45 Foretells Islam!","more":{"h":"https://youtu.be/ZjJ6DcGKU2I?si=raIdu2vRK4lfFAHQ","p":["https://youtu.be/ZjJ6DcGKU2I?si=raIdu2vRK4lfFAHQ\nIsaiah 45 Foretells Islam! Connection Revealed!\nIsaiah 45 Foretells Islam! Connection Revealed!"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #isaiah-45","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1365152052241760277"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#isaiah-45)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-isaiah-54"],{"title":"Isaiah 54","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Isaiah 54","tree":{"they":"Isaiah 54","we":"Isaiah 54 Prophesies Mecca , al-Imam ibn Qutaybah al-Dīnawarī (d 276) mentioned that Isaiah 54 is a prophecy about Mecca, a city likened to a barren woman because no prophet was sent to it, yet it will receive a prophet …","more":{"h":"Isaiah 54 Prophesies Mecca","p":["Isaiah 54 Prophesies Mecca\n,","al-Imam ibn Qutaybah al-Dīnawarī (d 276) mentioned that Isaiah 54 is a prophecy about Mecca, a city likened to a barren woman because no prophet was sent to it, yet it will receive a prophet and a revelation and will bear more children than the married woman (Jerusalem).","https://shamela.ws/book/847/26#p1\nص178 - كتاب أعلام رسول الله المنزلة على...\nص178 - كتاب أعلام رسول الله المنزلة على...\nص178 - كتاب أعلام رسول الله المنزلة على رسله - وقال شعيا في ذكر مكة - المكتبة الشاملة","Translation: (And Isaiah mentioned Makkah:)","“Rejoice and be glad, O barren one who has not given birth! Break forth and speak with praise, and be happy without shame, for your descendants will be more than the children of my people.”","This means: the people of Jerusalem from among the Children of Israel, and what is intended by “your people” are the people of Makkah —\nwho will be visited by more pilgrims and inhabitants than those of Jerusalem.","So, Makkah is likened to a barren woman who did not give birth, because no prophet appeared in it before except Ismā‘īl alone, and no book was revealed there.\nAnd it is not appropriate that the barren woman refers to Jerusalem, because it is the house of the prophets and the place of revelation —\nso it cannot be likened to a barren woman among women.","And Isaiah also mentioned Makkah elsewhere:","Jesus himself quoted Isaiah 54:13 in the Gospels: “They shall all be taught by God” (John 6:45),","it’s from the same section as isaiah 42 Isaiah; 40–55"],"imgs":6,"credit":"Deenresponds · #isaiah-54","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1365792870404980837"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#isaiah-54)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-psalm-72"],{"title":"Psalm 72","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Psalm 72","tree":{"they":"Psalm 72","we":"The septuagint translation of verse 15 renders it as him being “praised” https://x.com/vegitowrath/status/1372717551172657155 Vegito (@VegitoWrath) on X Vegito (@VegitoWrath) on X @CJ21493 “A Psalm of Solomon” is omitted in his version.","more":{"h":"the septuagint translation of verse 15 renders it as him being “praised”","p":["the septuagint translation of verse 15 renders it as him being “praised”","https://x.com/vegitowrath/status/1372717551172657155\nVegito (@VegitoWrath) on X\nVegito (@VegitoWrath) on X\n@CJ21493 “A Psalm of Solomon” is omitted in his version. If that’s not what you’re referring to, then clarify your argument.","Response to royal son point","He is the son of Abraham, Abraham in the Talmud is referred to in royal terms and called a king in the context of the war he waged against the kings in Genesis","Some medieval Jews also proposed that Abraham is the king mentioned in Isaiah 41","“Who has aroused one from the east\nand called him to his feet in righteousness?\nHe hands nations over to him\nand subdues kings before him.”"],"imgs":5,"credit":"Deenresponds · #psalm-72","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368284283793313883"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Https://youtu.be/CGIh3cLaEZ4?si=cglH7t7FRLiuNjOc Apostate Prophet GETS BAKED on Muhammed ﷺ in the Bible (Psalm 72) Apostate Prophet GETS BAKED on Muhammed ﷺ in the Bible (Psalm 72)","more":{"h":"https://youtu.be/CGIh3cLaEZ4?si=cglH7t7FRLiuNjOc","p":["https://youtu.be/CGIh3cLaEZ4?si=cglH7t7FRLiuNjOc\nApostate Prophet GETS BAKED on Muhammed ﷺ in the Bible (Psalm 72)\nApostate Prophet GETS BAKED on Muhammed ﷺ in the Bible (Psalm 72)"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #psalm-72","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368284283793313883"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#psalm-72)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-psalm-9"],{"title":"Psalm 9","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Psalm 9","tree":{"they":"Psalm 9","we":"Https://x.com/vegitowrath/status/1401578434543894529 Vegito (@VegitoWrath) on X Vegito (@VegitoWrath) on X Psalm 9’s prophecy about prophet Muhammad PBUH Mini Thread: Psalm 9 Prophecy of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , According to…","more":{"h":"https://x.com/vegitowrath/status/1401578434543894529","p":["https://x.com/vegitowrath/status/1401578434543894529\nVegito (@VegitoWrath) on X\nVegito (@VegitoWrath) on X\nPsalm 9’s prophecy about prophet Muhammad PBUH","Mini Thread:","Psalm 9 Prophecy of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ \n,","According to the Greek, Latin, and Syriac versions of Psalm 9:20, David asks God to judge the nations by sending a lawgiver to them:","Harun Al-Rashid in his letter to Constantine VI makes the brilliant argument that this prophecy can only apply to our holy prophet since he is the only prophet who brought a law after Moses. Jesus on the other hand followed the Mosaic law."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #psalm-9","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368284421630988420"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#psalm-9)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-quran-2-85"],{"title":"Quran 2 85","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Quran 2 85","tree":{"they":"Quran 2 85","we":"Tafsir Tabari: , Al-Ṭabarī says: This verse rebukes the Jews.","more":{"h":"Tafsir Tabari:","p":["Tafsir Tabari:\n,\nAl-Ṭabarī says:\nThis verse rebukes the Jews. Allah reminds them of their evil actions. After having accepted the covenant not to shed each other’s blood or expel one another from their homes, they began killing and expelling each other. Yet if a captive from among them fell into the hands of their enemies, they would ransom them – even though killing and expelling them was also forbidden. So how could they justify killing them, yet be unwilling to leave them in captivity? Or how could they be eager to ransom them, yet not avoid killing them?\nBoth actions – killing and refusing to ransom – were equally forbidden. So believing in the ransom law while rejecting the prohibition on killing and expelling was partial belief and partial disbelief.","Zamakhshari\n,\n{Do you then believe in part of the Book and disbelieve in another part?}\nMeaning: you believe in the part about ransoming captives but disbelieve in the part that forbids killing and expulsion.","Baghawi\n,\n{Do you then believe in part of the Book and disbelieve in another part?}\nMujāhid said:\nThis means, “If you find him in someone else’s hands, you ransom him—while you yourself kill him with your own hand.”","Muqatil\n,\nAnd if they come to you as captives, you ransom them, while it is forbidden for you to expel them. Do you then believe in part of the Book…?}\nHe says: You affirm part of what is in the Torah—regarding killing and expelling from homes—while it is forbidden for you to expel them."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #quran-2-85","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1369829228039770122"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#quran-2-85)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-5-47"],{"title":"5 47","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"5 47","tree":{"they":"5 47","we":"Zamakshari on 5:47 , Even though it may be permissible for someone to interpret the verse as meaning: “Let them judge by what Allah revealed in it [i.e., the Gospel] in terms of requiring them to act according to the rul…","more":{"h":"Zamakshari on 5:47","p":["Zamakshari on 5:47\n,\n Even though it may be permissible for someone to interpret the verse as meaning:","“Let them judge by what Allah revealed in it [i.e., the Gospel] in terms of requiring them to act according to the rulings of the Torah.”"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #5-47","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1370673888501039165"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#5-47)."}});
topic(["christianity","islam-vs","d-dr-5-48"],{"title":"5 48","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"5 48","tree":{"they":"5 48","we":"Baghawi Quran 5:48 , And the meanings are all close in meaning.","more":{"h":"Baghawi Quran 5:48","p":["Baghawi Quran 5:48\n,\nAnd the meanings are all close in meaning. The overall meaning is:\nEvery scripture that the Qur’an testifies to its truthfulness — then it is the Book of Allah, and whatever it does not (testify to), then it is not."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #5-48","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1370668845601390642"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#5-48)."}});
topic(["islam","general","d-dr-refuting-sam"],{"title":"Refuting sam","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"11 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Refuting sam","tree":{"they":"Refuting sam","we":"The Haashiyah “Raddul Muhtaar” of Ibn ‘Aabideen إبن عابدين – حاشية رد المحتار – الجزء : ( 3 ) – رقم الصفحة : ( 223 ) – ….","more":{"h":"The Haashiyah “Raddul Muhtaar” of Ibn ‘Aabideen","p":["The Haashiyah “Raddul Muhtaar” of Ibn ‘Aabideen","إبن عابدين – حاشية رد المحتار – الجزء : ( 3 ) – رقم الصفحة : ( 223 )\n– …. وقد صرحوا عندنا بأن الزوجة إذا كانت صغيرة لا تطيق الوطئ لا تسلم إلى الزوج حتى تطيقه ، والصحيح أنه غير مقدر بالسن ، بل يفوض إلى القاضي بالنظر إليها من سمن أو هزال \n\"It has been stated among us that if the wife is young and cannot endure intercourse, she is not to be handed over to the husband until she is able to bear it. The correct view is that this is not determined by age, but rather it is left to the judgment of the judge, who considers her physical condition—whether she is robust or frail.","وقدمنا عن التاتر خانية أن البالغة إذا كانت لا تحتمل لا يؤمر بدفعها إلى الزوج أيضاً ، فقوله : لا تحتمل يشمل ما لو كان لضعفها أو هزالها أو لكبر آلته \nWe previously quoted from the Tatar Khaniyyah that if a woman has reached puberty but cannot endure (intercourse), she also should not be handed over to the husband. So, the phrase 'she cannot endure' refers to her weakness, frailty, or the large size of the husband’s organ.","وفي الأشباه من أحكام غيبوبة الحشفة فيما يحرم على الزوج وطئ زوجته مع بقاء النكاح ، قال : وفيما إذا كانت لا تحتمله لصغر أو مرض أو سمنة اه‍ ، وربما يفهم من سمنه عظم آلته \nIn al-Ashbah, under the (section on) rulings related to the glans penetrating (the vagina), which make intercourse impermissible while the marriage still stands, it is stated: '...and in the case where she cannot bear it due to young age, illness, or corpulence.' It may be inferred from corpulence the meaning of the husband's large organ."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"وحرر الشرنبلالي في شرحه على الوهبانية أنه لو جامع زوجته فماتت أو صارت مفضّاة ، فإن كانت صغيرة أو مكرهة أولا تطيق تلزمه الدية إتفاقاً Al-Shurunbulaali clarified in his commentary on al-Wahbaniyyah that if a man has interc…","more":{"h":"Refuting sam","p":["وحرر الشرنبلالي في شرحه على الوهبانية أنه لو جامع زوجته فماتت أو صارت مفضّاة ، فإن كانت صغيرة أو مكرهة أولا تطيق تلزمه الدية إتفاقاً\nAl-Shurunbulaali clarified in his commentary on al-Wahbaniyyah that if a man has intercourse with his wife and she dies or suffers a vaginal injury, then if she was young, coerced, or unable to bear it, the husband is liable for blood money by consensus.","، فعلم من هذا كله أنه لا يحل له وطؤها بما يؤدي إلى إضرارها ، فيقتصر على ما تطيق منه عدداً بنظر القاضي أو أخبار النساء ، وإن لم يعلم بذلك فبقولها \nFrom all of this, it is understood that it is not permissible for the husband to have intercourse with his wife in a way that causes her harm. He must limit himself to what she can bear, as determined by the judge or the testimony of women. If that cannot be known (by the judge or by other women), then by her statement.","وكذا في غلظ الآلة ، ويؤمر في طولها بإدخال قدر ما تطيقه منها أو بقدر آلة رجل معتدل الخلقة ، والله أعلم\nThe same applies regarding the girth of the organ, and with regard to its length, he is instructed to insert only as much as she can tolerate, or an amount equivalent to the size of an average man's organ. And Allah knows best.\"","Additional Hanafi sources:\n ((البحر الرائق)) لابن نجيم (3/128)، ((الفتاوى الهندية)) (1/287)."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"1- Not able > don’t send her to him 2- Same but this mentions even if she is baalighah> she wont be handed over a.","more":{"h":"Refuting sam","p":["1- Not able > don’t send her to him 2- Same but this mentions even if she is baalighah> she wont be handed over a. These both show protection and safety of the woman b. Also they show that thighing isn’t an option while the husband waits for maturity because she shouldn’t be handed over until she’s ready. c. Thighing and the like are thus replacements for intercourse when she is in the state of haydh or another similar state (nifaas). 3- The husbands organ size matters 4- Shows that if the husband has intercourse in any state that she can’t handle it, he is liable. 5- It is not permissible to have intercourse in a way which harms her\nhere is an additional paragraph summary","And I just confirmed with a Hanafi Mufty that based on this text, any of the dawaa'ee (such as thighing) would not be allowed before her being ready (based on the fact that she isn't to be handed over to the husband until she is ready)","The following are quotes from authoritative Hanbali and Shafi texts:"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"أما بخصوص الاستمتاع.. فإن كانت قد بلغت مبلغا تطيق فيه الرجال فيجوز له الاستمتاع بها بالوطء وغيره ولو لم تبلغ الحلم، وبعضهم قيد هذا السن بتسع سنوات ولكن الظاهر أنه لا يتقيد بهذا فكم من صبية بلغت تسع سنوات وهي لا تطيق الوطء لضعف بنيتها.","more":{"h":"Refuting sam","p":["أما بخصوص الاستمتاع.. فإن كانت قد بلغت مبلغا تطيق فيه الرجال فيجوز له الاستمتاع بها بالوطء وغيره ولو لم تبلغ الحلم، وبعضهم قيد هذا السن بتسع سنوات ولكن الظاهر أنه لا يتقيد بهذا فكم من صبية بلغت تسع سنوات وهي لا تطيق الوطء لضعف بنيتها.\nAs for enjoyment (sexual or otherwise):\nIf the girl has reached an age at which she is physically capable of intercourse, then it is permissible for the husband to enjoy her, through intercourse or otherwise, even if she has not yet reached puberty. Some scholars restrict this age to nine years, but what is apparent is that it is not limited to this, for many girls may reach nine years of age but still be physically incapable of intercourse due to physical weakness.","أما إذا كانت لا تطيق الوطء فإما أن تكون في سن الرضاع وما قاربه كبنت الثالثة والرابعة ونحو ذلك، وهذه لا يستمتع بها لا بوطء ولا بغيره لأنها ليست بأهل لذلك\nوأما من يمكن الاستمتاع بها – دون الوطء - كبنت الثامنة مثلا فهذه ينبغي ترك الاستمتاع بها أيضا لأنه لا يؤمن أن يقود هذا إلى مواقعة الزوج لها لغلبة شهوته فيلحق بها الضرر فينبغي لأهلها أن يمنعوها منه ولا يسلموها له أصلا حتى وإن طلبها حذرا من ذلك\nAs for the scenario in which she is not capable of intercourse, either because she is still at the breastfeeding age or near it — like a girl of three or four years old — then it is not permissible for the husband to enjoy her, neither through intercourse nor otherwise, because she is not fit for such interactions.\nAs for a girl who can be enjoyed in ways other than intercourse — such as an eight-year-old, for example — then it is still recommended to avoid doing so. There is fear that such actions could lead the husband, due to overwhelming desire, to engage in intercourse with her, which would result in harm. Therefore, her guardians should prevent her from being handed over to him, even if he requests her, out of caution."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"يقول ابن قدامة: فمتى كانت لا تصلح للوطء لم يجب على أهلها تسليمها إليه وإن ذكر أنه يحضنها ويربيها وله من يخدمها لأنه لا يملك الاستمتاع بها وليست له بمحل ولا يؤمن شرة نفسه إلى مواقعتها فيفضها أو يقتلها وفي المجموع شرح المه…","more":{"h":"Refuting sam","p":["يقول ابن قدامة: فمتى كانت لا تصلح للوطء لم يجب على أهلها تسليمها إليه وإن ذكر أنه يحضنها ويربيها وله من يخدمها لأنه لا يملك الاستمتاع بها وليست له بمحل ولا يؤمن شرة نفسه إلى مواقعتها فيفضها أو يقتلها\nوفي المجموع شرح المهذب: وإن كانت المنكوحة صغيرة لا يجامع مثلها أو مريضة مرضا يرجى زواله وطالب الزوج بها لم يجب تسليمها إليه، لان المعقود عليه هو المنفعة، وذلك لا يوجد في حقها، ولانه لا يؤمن أن يحمله فرط الشهوة على جماعها، فيوقع ذلك جناية بها. انتهى.\nIbn Qudāmah said:\n“If she is unfit for intercourse, it is not obligatory upon her guardians to hand her over to him, even if he claims he only wants to raise her and has someone to serve her. He does not have the right to enjoy her, and she is not suitable for him. One cannot trust his desires, which may lead him to have intercourse with her, thereby causing injury or even death.”\nIn al-Majmūʿ Sharḥ al-Muhadhdhab, (Imam al-Nawawi r.a.) says:\n“If the married girl is too young for intercourse or is sick in a way expected to be temporary, and the husband requests her, it is not obligatory to hand her over. The object of the contract is benefit (enjoyment), and that benefit does not exist in her case. Also, there is a fear that excessive desire may push him to engage in intercourse, which would cause her harm.”"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"وفي الحاوي في فقه الشافعي: وإذا كان الاستمتاع بها غير ممكن لم يلزم تسليمها إليه ، ولم يلزمه تسليم الصداق إليها فإن طلب تسليمها إليه ليقوم بحضانتها وتربيتها لم يلزم تسليمها إليه أيضا ؛ لأنه لا حق له في حضانتها ، وإنما حقه…","more":{"h":"Refuting sam","p":["وفي الحاوي في فقه الشافعي: وإذا كان الاستمتاع بها غير ممكن لم يلزم تسليمها إليه ، ولم يلزمه تسليم الصداق إليها فإن طلب تسليمها إليه ليقوم بحضانتها وتربيتها لم يلزم تسليمها إليه أيضا ؛ لأنه لا حق له في حضانتها ، وإنما حقه في الاستمتاع الذي لم يخلق فيها فيستحقه الزوج منها ، ولأنه لا يؤمن أن تغلبه الشهوة على مواقعتها ، فربما أفضى إلى تلفها ونكايتها. انتهى\nIn al-Ḥāwī, from the Shāfiʿī school:\n“If enjoyment with her is not possible, then it is not obligatory to hand her over, nor to hand over the dowry. If the husband requests her to raise or care for her, it is also not obligatory to hand her over, because he has no right to custody — his right is in enjoyment, which she is not yet fit for. Also, he cannot be trusted to restrain his desire, and it could lead to harming or even killing her.”"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"وفي المغني لابن قدامة: وإمكان الوطء في الصغيرة معتبر بحالها واحتمالها لذلك قاله القاضي: وذكر أنهن يختلفن فقد تكون صغيرة السن تصلح وكبيرة لا تصلح وحدّه أحمد بتسع سنين فقال في رواية أبي الحارث في الصغيرة يطلبها زوجها: فإن …","more":{"h":"Refuting sam","p":["وفي المغني لابن قدامة: وإمكان الوطء في الصغيرة معتبر بحالها واحتمالها لذلك قاله القاضي: وذكر أنهن يختلفن فقد تكون صغيرة السن تصلح وكبيرة لا تصلح وحدّه أحمد بتسع سنين فقال في رواية أبي الحارث في الصغيرة يطلبها زوجها: فإن أتى عليها تسع سنين دفعت إليه ليس أن يحبسوها بعد التسع وذهب في ذلك إلى أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بنى بعائشة وهي ابنة تسع قال القاضي: وهذا عندي ليس على طريق التحديد وإنما ذكره لأن الغالب أن ابنة تسع يتمكن من الاستمتاع بها. انتهى\nوالله أعلم.\nIn Al-Mughni by Ibn Qudamah, it is stated: \n\"The possibility of intercourse with a young girl is considered based on her condition and her ability to withstand it. Therefore, Al-Qadi said: ‘And he mentioned that they differ, for a young girl may be fit, and an older one may not be fit’. \nImam Ahmad limited it to nine years, and in the narration of Abu Al-Harith, he said regarding a young girl whose husband seeks her: ‘If she reaches nine years of age, she is given to him; it is not that they should detain her after nine years’. And he based that on the fact that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, consummated his marriage with Aisha when she was nine years old.\"\nAl-Qadi said: \"In my opinion, this is not by way of a strict limit, but rather he mentioned it because it is generally the case that a nine-year-old girl is capable of being enjoyed.\"","__"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"This is from a Islam web fatwa https://www.islamweb.net/ar/fatwa/130882 بين العقد على الصغيرة والاستمتاع بها بين العقد على الصغيرة والاستمتاع بها اكتشف النقاش حول حكم نكاح الصغيرة والاستمتاع بها في الفتوى رقم 21361، حيث …","more":{"h":"This is from a Islam web fatwa https://www.islamweb.net/ar/fatwa/130882","p":["This is from a Islam web fatwa https://www.islamweb.net/ar/fatwa/130882\nبين العقد على الصغيرة والاستمتاع بها\nبين العقد على الصغيرة والاستمتاع بها\nاكتشف النقاش حول حكم نكاح الصغيرة والاستمتاع بها في الفتوى رقم 21361، حيث يتم التعارض مع الفتوى رقم 11251. تتناول الفتوى جواز العقد على الصغيرة وفقاً لما ورد في النصوص الشرعية، مع توضيح أنه يُجوز ...","I confirmed with a Maliki scholar that they have the same view pretty much","I don't really have the drive to comb their (Maliki) sources tho lol If you insist I can find them","Therefore, based on these opinions, Ummul Mumineen Aisha r.a. was handed over because she was ready. If there is any thighing mentioned, it has to be after tasleem/handed over and therefore she was ready.","From الموسوعة الفقهية (a popular modern encyclopaedia of fiqh) Shows that there is agreement between all four schools المسألةُ الثَّالثةُ: تسليمُ الصغيرةِ لِزَوجِها للاستِمتاعِ بها لا تُسلَّمُ الصَّغيرةُ التي لا تُطيقُ الوَطءَ لِزَوجِها للاستمتاعِ بها، وهذا باتِّفاقِ المَذاهِبِ الفِقهيَّةِ الأربَعةِ: الحَنَفيَّةِ، والمالِكيَّةِ، والشَّافِعيَّةِ، والحَنابِلةِ The third issue: handing over a minor girl to her husband for sexual enjoyment. A minor girl who cannot tolerate sexual intercourse is not to be handed over to her husband for sexual enjoyment. This is agreed upon by the four schools of Islamic jurisprudence: The Hanafi, Maliki, Shafi'i, and Hanbali schools.\nThis should also be a point worth highlighting in the video/refutation. It's not often that there is complete agreement of something (from the furoo') across the 4 schools."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The following are relevant Tafseers for 65:4: __ Abu Ja‘far al-Ṭabarī (d.","more":{"h":"The following are relevant Tafseers for 65:4:","p":["The following are relevant Tafseers for 65:4:","__","Abu Ja‘far al-Ṭabarī (d. 310 AH)\nيقول: وكذلك عدد اللائي لم يحضن من الجواري لصغر إذا طلقهنّ أزواجهنّ بعد الدخول.\nThe same applies to the waiting period of young girls who have not menstruated due to their young age, if their husbands divorce them after consummation.\n__\nAbū Bakr al-Jaṣṣāṣ (d. 370 AH)\n﴿واللائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ لِمَن ثَبَتَ أنَّها لَمْ تَحِضْ\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to those confirmed not to have had menstruation.\n__\nMakki ibn Abī Ṭālib (d. 437 AH)\n﴿وَاللَّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ من الصغار، لم يبلغن وقد مُسِسْنَ فعدتهن ثلاثةُ أشهر. وهو قول قتادة.\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to young girls who have not reached puberty but have had sexual relations; their ‘iddah is three months. This was also the view of Qatadah.\n__\nAl-Māwardī (d. 450 AH)\n﴿واللائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ يَعْنِي كَذَلِكَ عِدَّتُهُنَّ ثَلاثَةُ أشْهُرٍ، فَجَعَلَ لِكُلِّ قُرْءٍ شَهرًا، لِأنَّها تَجْمَعُ في الأغْلَبِ حَيْضًا وطُهْرًا.\n“Those who have not menstruated” — their waiting period is also three months, assigning one month per cycle, since a normal cycle generally combines menstruation and purity.\n__\nAl-Baghawī (d. 516 AH)\n﴿وَاللَّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ يَعْنِي الصِّغَارَ اللَّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ فَعِدَّتُهُنَّ أَيْضًا ثَلَاثَة أشهُر.\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to young girls who have not menstruated. Their waiting period is also three months.\n__\nAl-Zamakhsharī (d. 538 AH)\n﴿وَاللَّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ هنّ الصغائر.\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to young girls.\n__"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Fakhr al-Dīn al-Rāzī (d. 606 AH) ﴿واللّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ أيْ هي بِمَنزِلَةِ الكَبِيرَةِ الَّتِي قَدْ يَئِسَتْ، عِدَّتُها ثَلاثَةُ أشْهُرٍ.","more":{"h":"Fakhr al-Dīn al-Rāzī (d. 606 AH)","p":["Fakhr al-Dīn al-Rāzī (d. 606 AH)\n﴿واللّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ أيْ هي بِمَنزِلَةِ الكَبِيرَةِ الَّتِي قَدْ يَئِسَتْ، عِدَّتُها ثَلاثَةُ أشْهُرٍ.\n“Those who have not menstruated” are treated like elderly women who no longer menstruate—their waiting period is three months.\n__\nAl-Nasafī (d. 710 AH)\nArabic:\n﴿واللائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾، هُنَّ الصَّغائِرُ\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to young girls.\n__\nAl-Qurṭubī (d. 671 AH)\n﴿وَاللَّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ - يَعْنِي الصَّغِيرَةَ - فَعِدَّتُهُنَّ ثَلَاثَةُ أَشْهُرٍ...\nفَإِذَا رَأَتِ الدَّمَ فِي زَمَنِ احْتِمَالِهِ عِنْدَ النِّسَاءِ انْتَقَلَتْ إِلَى الدَّمِ... وَهَذَا إِجْمَاعٌ.\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to young girls. Their ‘iddah is three months...\nIf she begins menstruating during her ‘iddah and it is within the age when women typically menstruate, her waiting period switches to the menstrual-based count. This is by consensus (ijmā‘).\n__\nAl-Shawkānī (d. 1250 AH)\n﴿واللّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ لِصِغَرِهِنَّ وعَدَمِ بُلُوغِهِنَّ سِنَّ المَحِيضِ.\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to girls due to their young age and not having reached the age of menstruation.\n__\nAl-Suyūṭī (d. 911 AH) – Al-Durr al-Manthūr\n﴿واللائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ فَهُنَّ الأبْكارُ الجَوارِي اللّائِي لَمْ يَبْلُغْنَ المَحِيضَ\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to virgin slave girls who have not yet reached the age of menstruation.\n__\nAl-Ālūsī (d. 1270 AH)\n﴿واللائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾... والمُرادُ الصِّغارُ اللّائِي لَمْ يَبْلُغْنَ سِنَّ الحَيْضِ\n“Those who have not menstruated” refers to young girls who have not reached the age of menstruation.\n__"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Al-Sa‘dī (d. 1376 AH) ﴿وَاللَّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ أي: الصغار، اللائي لم يأتهن الحيض بعد، والبالغات اللاتي لم يأتهن حيض بالكلية “Those who have not menstruated” includes young girls who have not yet menstruated, and matur…","more":{"h":"Al-Sa‘dī (d. 1376 AH)","p":["Al-Sa‘dī (d. 1376 AH)\n﴿وَاللَّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ﴾ أي: الصغار، اللائي لم يأتهن الحيض بعد، والبالغات اللاتي لم يأتهن حيض بالكلية\n“Those who have not menstruated” includes young girls who have not yet menstruated, and mature women who have never menstruated at all.","Now, I checked an additional 10+ tafseer. All of them (except Imam al-Suyuti in al-Durr al-Manthur)) say it refers to \"non baalighah\" or general has not had haydh yet.","Imam Suyuti says \" virgin slave girls who have not yet reached the age of menstruation\". In Jalaalayn, he says the same as others.","A point to note is that these comments are all extremely straight forward and seemed to not need much discussion. This to me shows that the details of age/time of intercourse/istimtaa/enjoyment was well known and common knowledge.","These verses DO NOT mention any minimum age for intercourse/istimtaa/enjoyment, even the Ahkaam related tafseer (such as Ahkaamul Quran of al-Jassaas)","So we would need to go to the other discussion to understand those points.","___However, from the fact that there is an iddah tells us that they either had intercourse or khalwah saheehah.","___The assumption is that it is referring to a marriage that was consumated in a halal/safe way which means she fit the description mentioned in our fiqh discussion","I'll clarify this here since I want to avoid confusions in the future. The notes in here were made by @Dawud so when it says \"i have checked...\" etc etc it's him. Any further questions can be directed to him regarding the notes here."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #refuting-sam","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283554202521650"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]}]}]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#refuting-sam)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","marriage","aisha","d-dr-consummation-with-prepubescents"],{"title":"Consummation with prepubescents","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"5 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Consummation with prepubescents","tree":{"they":"Consummation with prepubescents","we":"Ibn Battal [d. 449 A.H] said… , \"The scholars unanimously agreed that it is permissible for the fathers to marry off their young girls even if they were in a cradle,but [agreed] it is not permissible for their husbands t…","more":{"h":"Ibn Battal [d. 449 A.H] said…","p":["Ibn Battal [d. 449 A.H] said…\n,\n\"The scholars unanimously agreed that it is permissible for the fathers to marry off their young girls even if they were in a cradle,but [agreed] it is not permissible for their husbands to take them in [into their house]/interact with them (sexually) until they can safely handle intercorse and handle a man.And their conditions in this regard vary according to how they are built[physically] and their capacity.[mentally]\"","(Sharh Sahih al-Bukhari by Ibn Battal Volume 7 Pages 172-173)","Ibn Yunus al-Siqilli [d. 451 A.H] reporting the opinion of Imam Malik [d. 179 A.H]:\n,\n\"Malik said: If she is young, he cannot have intercourse with her because of her young age. then he is told: 'Enter upon her or spend on her,' It is not obligatory for him to provide for her maintenance or her dowry because enjoyment is not possible from her until she reaches the age of intercourse, even if she has not menstruated because enjoyment is possible from her as would be with an adult\"","(Al-Jami' li-Masail al-Mudawwanah by Ibn Yunus al-Siqilli, Volume 4 Page 311)"],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #consummation-with-prepubescents","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283657806020648"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Ibn Qudamah al-Hanbali [d. 620 A.H] quoting Al-Qadi who explains the opinion of consummating with a 9 year old: , \"Al-Qadi said: “In my view, this is not meant to be a fixed rule.","more":{"h":"Consummation with prepubescents","p":["Ibn Qudamah al-Hanbali [d. 620 A.H] quoting Al-Qadi who explains the opinion of consummating with a 9 year old:\n,\n\"Al-Qadi said: “In my view, this is not meant to be a fixed rule. Rather he mentioned it because it is commonly observed and most likely that a nine-year-old girl is capable of marital relations. Therefore, if she is not suitable for consummation, her family is not to hand her over to him. Even if he claims he will care for and raise her and have someone serve her, it is because he does not have the right to enjoy her, and she is not yet in a condition for him. Additionally, there is a concern that he might harm her, either by causing her injury or even killing her.","(Al-Mughni by Ibn Qudamah Volume 9 Pages 527-528)","A Popular Fatwa Book Within The Hanafi Madhab says this:\n,\n\"The majority of scholars are of the opinion that age is not the determining factor, rather the determining factor is her ability, if she is strong and large/healthy, and capable of sexual relations without fearing illness/harm, then the husband can consummate the marriage with her\"","(Al-Fatwa al-Hindiya [Fatwa Alamgir] Volume 1 Page 316)"],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #consummation-with-prepubescents","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283657806020648"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Al-Baghawi al-Shafi'i [d. 516 A.H] said: , \"If it's not possible to have sexual intercourse with her because she cannot handle it because she's prepubescent or if she has an illness or weakness that prevents her from hav…","more":{"h":"Al-Baghawi al-Shafi'i [d. 516 A.H] said:","p":["Al-Baghawi al-Shafi'i [d. 516 A.H] said:\n,\n\"If it's not possible to have sexual intercourse with her because she cannot handle it because she's prepubescent or if she has an illness or weakness that prevents her from having sexual intercourse with him - She should be given TIME until SHE'S READY\"","If the husband says, 'Hand her over to me, and I will not have intercourse with her until she can handle it,' If she is young [prepubescent], her guardians are to prevent her [from intercourse and being handed over]. If she is ill, she can be handed over to him, because the custody of a young [prepubescent] girl through a close relative is more preferable and appropriate.\"","Al-Tahdhib fi Fiqh al-Imam al-Shafi'i by Al-Baghawi Volume 5 Page 521"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #consummation-with-prepubescents","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283657806020648"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Al-Umrani al-Shafi'i [d. 558 A.H] said: , [If there's harm involved intercourse isn't allowed] Imam Al Shaf'i said: “And if intercourse with her causes severe harm...","more":{"h":"Al-Umrani al-Shafi'i [d. 558 A.H] said:","p":["Al-Umrani al-Shafi'i [d. 558 A.H] said:\n,\n[If there's harm involved intercourse isn't allowed] Imam Al Shaf'i said: “And if intercourse with her causes severe harm... he is forbidden from intercourse with her, and it is taken At her expense\" If the man has a large body and the wife of small body, and there is harm upon her during intercourse that he fears from excessive force or severe pain/hardship, or there is a wound in her private area that can cause harm, and he agrees with her on the harm that his intercourse may cause her, then it is not permissible for him to have sexual intercourse with her due to the saying of Allah\n‎۞وَعَاشِرُوهُنَّ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ۞\n\"Treat them fairly\"[surah al nisa' verse 19]\nAnd from the known/المعروف:that it's impermissible to have intercourse with her. If he chooses to divorce her and divorces her, then there is no talk. If he does not choose to divorce her, then he is obligated to support her. Because she is confined to him, and he can enjoy her without intercourse.","[Al Bayan Fi-Madhab Imam al-Shaf'i' Volume 11 Pages 193-194]","Ibn Nujaym al-Hanafi [d. 970 A.H] said:\n,\n\"What prohibits a man from having intercourse with his wife while the marriage remains valid:","…and if she is unable to handle intercourse because she is young\"","(Al-Ashbah wa al-Nazair ala Madhhab Abi Hanifah al-Nu'man by Ibn Nujaym Page 289)"],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #consummation-with-prepubescents","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283657806020648"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Al-Nawawi said… , “If it is possible to have intercourse with her without harming her, he may do that.","more":{"h":"Al-Nawawi said…","p":["Al-Nawawi said…\n,\n“If it is possible to have intercourse with her without harming her, he may do that. If it is not possible for him to have intercourse with her except by harming her[be it of young age], then he does not have permission to have intercourse with her.”","(Al-Majmu Sharh al-Muhadhab 16/409)"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #consummation-with-prepubescents","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283657806020648"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#consummation-with-prepubescents)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","marriage","aisha","d-dr-early-christians-had-no-issue"],{"title":"Early christians had no issue","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Early christians had no issue","tree":{"they":"Early christians had no issue","we":"Https://youtu.be/X9nhT9TuCVw Will Sam Shamoun CONDEMN THE EARLY CHURCH?","more":{"h":"https://youtu.be/X9nhT9TuCVw","p":["https://youtu.be/X9nhT9TuCVw\nWill Sam Shamoun CONDEMN THE EARLY CHURCH?\nWill Sam Shamoun CONDEMN THE EARLY CHURCH?"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #early-christians-had-no-issue","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283682648887498"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#early-christians-had-no-issue)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","marriage","aisha","d-dr-aisha-played-with-dolls"],{"title":"Aisha played with dolls","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Aisha played with dolls","tree":{"they":"Aisha played with dolls","we":"Argument Sahih al-Bukhari 6130 Narrated Aisha: I used to play with the dolls in the presence of the Prophet, and my girl friends also used to play with me.","more":{"h":"Aisha played with dolls","p":["Argument\nSahih al-Bukhari 6130\nNarrated Aisha:\nI used to play with the dolls in the presence of the Prophet, and my girl friends also used to play with me. When Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) used to enter (my dwelling place) they used to hide themselves, but the Prophet would call them to join and play with me. (The playing with the dolls and similar images is forbidden, but it was allowed for Aisha at that time, as she was a little girl, not yet reached the age of puberty.) (Fath-ul-Bari page 143, Vol.13)","Explained\nThe part where it says [The playing with the dolls and similar images is forbidden, but it was allowed for Aisha at that time, as she was a little girl, not yet reached the age of puberty] is a commentary from Fath-ul-Bari written by Ibn Hajar al-'Asqalani who lived in the 14 to 15th century who isn’t even saying his own opinion here, he’s quoting a scholar named Al-khattabi who concluded this based on the fact that only kids(prior to puberty) are allowed to play with dolls. Ibn hajar said himself that this is a questionable position because Aisha still had her dolls either during the time of Tabuk or Khaybar(Sunan Abi Dawud 4932) when she was either 14 or 15, definitely when she attained or surpassed puberty."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Deenresponds · #aisha-played-with-dolls","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283761372041347"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"We see that it is allowed for her to have images of horse and dolls while’s she had already attained puberty.","more":{"h":"Aisha played with dolls","p":["We see that it is allowed for her to have images of horse and dolls while’s she had already attained puberty. So Fath-ul-Bari commentary on Al-Bukhari 6130 is not accurate.","Ahmad Ibn Husayn Bayhaqi a scholar who lived in the 10 to 11th century holds the position found in Al-Sunan Al-Kubra, V. 10 Pg. 371 that it was after the battle of Khaybar, it was forbidden to play with dolls or have images of living things in your house.","Conclusion\nThe commentary added in Al-bukhari 6130 that suggest that Aisha had not hit puberty after consummation because she played with dolls is inaccurate. Aisha still had her dolls at Tabuk or Khaybar when she was either 14 or 15, most definitely already attained puberty or surpassed it. The playing of dolls or having images had not been forbidden until after the battle of Khaybar. Other scholars also say that the dolls Aisha had, did not have a face and would deem it to be permissible but it is certain that aisha being allowed to play with dolls was not due to her not yet attaining puberty."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #aisha-played-with-dolls","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368283761372041347"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#aisha-played-with-dolls)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","marriage","aisha","d-dr-this-doesn-t-contradict-the-bible"],{"title":"This doesn’t contradict the bible","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"This doesn’t contradict the bible","tree":{"they":"This doesn’t contradict the bible","we":"Since numbers 31:18 has been discussed already, I will be dedicating my notes to answering some objections posed by christians against it.","more":{"h":"This doesn’t contradict the bible","p":["Since numbers 31:18 has been discussed already, I will be dedicating my notes to answering some objections posed by christians against it.","The tipical response of the Christian is to say that Moses gave the command and not God, hence God was not culpable for the incident.","Answer: There are two main reasons why it is completely justified to say that God is perfectly in agreement with what happened.","in numbers 31:25-31, the biblical God is giving instructions for what to do with what has been captured. Not only did he not reproach Moses for the command, he even instructed the Israelites on what to do with what has been taken as a result of it, including the girls, showing that the biblical God did not view what Moses did as sinful.\n,","The exact same command is given by God himself in duteronomy, which the Isrealites are to obey when fighting with certain nations.\n,","but the women and the little ones, the livestock, and everything else in the city, all its spoil, you shall take as plunder for yourselves. And you shall enjoy the spoil of your enemies, which the Lord your God has given you duteronomy 20:14.","This is God speaking and not Moses so they can't get out of this one."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #this-doesn’t-contradict-the-bible","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1351842444899127347"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"More objections: Objection: The children were taken as slaves of the soldiers.","more":{"h":"More objections:","p":["More objections:","Objection: The children were taken as slaves of the soldiers.","Answer: This does not get rid of the problem at all, it is completely permissible to have relations with your slave according to the bible.","Exitus 21","7 “If a man sells his daughter as a servant, she is not to go free as male servants do.","8 If she does not please the master who has selected her for himself, he must let her be redeemed. He has no right to sell her to foreigners, because he has broken faith with her.","Objection: God giving the Isrealites instructions on what to do with the plunder doesn't mean he's ok with it but he uses the sins of the people for the greater good. Many prophets and kings made bad decision but God still works with those.","Answer: This makes no sense, every single time a king or a prophet makes a bad decision in the bible they are clearly reprimanded for it. This is just coping.","Objection: God was silent on what happened in numbers 31 because Moses was doomed to die anyway according to numbers 20:12 and duteronomy 32:48-52.","Answer: This would make sense if Moses were the only guilty party. But the soldiers and the high priests received no punishment or reprimand either.","Also if this is true, Moses, according to the bible, would have died as a mass-murderer and would have went to hell.","But this is impossible because of the mount of transfiguration incedent where Moses was with Jesus according to Luke 9:28-31."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #this-doesn’t-contradict-the-bible","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1351842444899127347"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#this-doesn’t-contradict-the-bible)."}});
topic(["islam","morality","marriage","aisha","d-dr-puberty-at-9-is-impossible"],{"title":"Puberty at 9 is impossible","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Puberty at 9 is impossible","tree":{"they":"Puberty at 9 is impossible","we":"First study.pdf 203.47 KB Download Evidence Aisha May Allah be Pleased with her was gaining a lot of weight before consummation.","more":{"h":"First study.pdf 203.47 KB Download","p":["First study.pdf 203.47 KB Download","Evidence Aisha May Allah be Pleased with her was gaining a lot of weight before consummation.","Second Study showing the linkage of race and gaining of weight to early menarche (Ages below 11)","maturational-timing-and-overweight-prevalence-in-us-adolescent-g-2001.pdf 66.32 KB Download","A French western philosopher named Montesquieu said in 1748 (and I quote): “Woman, in hot climates, are marriageable at eight, nine or ten years of age.”","https://classicliberal.tripod.com/montesquieu/sol16.html"],"imgs":7,"credit":"Deenresponds · #puberty-at-9-is-impossible","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368284008689045525"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#puberty-at-9-is-impossible)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","preservation","d-dr-defense-of-ahruf"],{"title":"Defense of ahruf","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Defense of ahruf","tree":{"they":"Defense of ahruf","we":"Https://yaqeeninstitute.ca/read/paper/the-uthmanic-codex-understanding-how-the-quran-was-preserved The ʿUthmānic Codex: Understanding how the Qur’an was Preserved...","more":{"h":"https://yaqeeninstitute.ca/read/paper/the-uthmanic-codex-understanding-how-the-quran-was-preserved","p":["https://yaqeeninstitute.ca/read/paper/the-uthmanic-codex-understanding-how-the-quran-was-preserved\nThe ʿUthmānic Codex: Understanding how the Qur’an was Preserved...\nThe ʿUthmānic Codex: Understanding how the Qur’an was Preserved...\nAn overview of the history behind the Uthmanic codex and how it was compiled to preserve the Quran as it was revealed to the Prophet Muhammad through memorization, written recordings and direct testimony."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #defense-of-ahruf","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368287219273695232"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#defense-of-ahruf)."}});
topic(["islam","quran","preservation","d-dr-defense-of-qiraat"],{"title":"Defense of qiraat","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Defense of qiraat","tree":{"they":"Defense of qiraat","we":"Https://youtu.be/3tS7X2j4PkA The Origins and Canonization of Qirāʾāt with Sh.","more":{"h":"https://youtu.be/3tS7X2j4PkA","p":["https://youtu.be/3tS7X2j4PkA\nThe Origins and Canonization of Qirāʾāt with Sh. Yousef Wahb\nThe Origins and Canonization of Qirāʾāt with Sh. Yousef Wahb","https://yaqeeninstitute.ca/read/paper/can-the-quran-be-recited-in-different-ways-the-meaning-and-wisdom-of-qiraat\nCan the Qur'an Be Recited in Different Ways? The Meaning and Wisdom...\nCan the Qur'an Be Recited in Different Ways? The Meaning and Wisdom...\nIf the Qur’an is a timeless, unchanged book, how can it be read in multiple ways? What is the meaning behind these multiple readings (qirāʾāt), and how many are there?"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #defense-of-qiraat","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1368287248558198784"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#defense-of-qiraat)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-mark"],{"title":"Mark","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"5 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Mark","tree":{"they":"Mark","we":"Https://letthetruthcomeoutblog.wordpress.com/2019/04/28/the-rider-on-the-clouds-a-critique-of-dr-michael-heisers-view-of-daniel-7/ The Rider On The Clouds – A Critique Of Dr.","more":{"h":"Mark","p":["https://letthetruthcomeoutblog.wordpress.com/2019/04/28/the-rider-on-the-clouds-a-critique-of-dr-michael-heisers-view-of-daniel-7/\nThe Rider On The Clouds – A Critique Of Dr. Michael Heiser’s Vi...\nThe Rider On The Clouds – A Critique Of Dr. Michael Heiser’s Vi...\nI will be critiquing Michael Heiser’s view on Daniel 7 as found in the condensed form of chapter 6 of his dissertation on the Divine Council. Here is the PDF: daniel7 Daniel 7 – A Divin…"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1396880233910632508"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Mark 12:35-40 David Calls Jesus Lord , @leafywashere","more":{"h":"Mark 12:35-40 David Calls Jesus Lord","p":["Mark 12:35-40 David Calls Jesus Lord\n,","@leafywashere"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1396880233910632508"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The New Testament contains no explicit trinitarian doctrine.","more":{"h":"Mark","p":["The New Testament contains no explicit trinitarian doctrine. However, many Christian theologians, apologists, and philosophers hold that the doctrine can be inferred from what the New Testament does teach about God. But how may it be inferred? Is the inference deductive, or is it an inference to the best explanation? And is it based on what is implicitly taught there, or on what is merely assumed there? Many Christian theologians and apologists seem to hold it is a deductive inference.","In contrast, other Christians admit that their preferred doctrine of the Trinity not only (1) can’t be inferred from the Bible alone, but also (2) that there’s inadequate or no evidence for it there, and even (3) that what is taught in the Bible is incompatible with the doctrine. These Christians believe the doctrine solely on the authority of later doctrinal pronouncements of the True Christian Church (typically one of: the Catholic Church, the Eastern Orthodox tradition, or the mainstream of the Christian tradition, broadly understood). Some Catholic apologists have argued that this doctrine shows the necessity of the teaching authority of the Church, this doctrine being constitutive of Christianity but underivable from the Bible apart from the Church’s guidance in interpreting it. This stance is not popular among Christians who are neither Catholic nor Eastern Orthodox. (2) would be the main sticking point, although some groups deny all three.","Many Christian apologists argue that the doctrine of the Trinity is “biblical” (i.e. either it is implicitly taught there, or it is the best explanation of what is taught there) using three sorts of arguments. They begin by claiming that the Father of Jesus Christ is the one true God taught in the Old Testament. They then argue that given what the Bible teaches about Christ and the Holy Spirit, they must be “fully divine” as well. Thus, we must, as it were, “move them within” the nature of the one God. Therefore, there are three fully divine persons “in God”. While this may be paradoxical, it is argued that this is what God has revealed to humankind through the Bible.","The types of arguments employed to show the “full divinity” of Christ and the Holy Spirit work as follows.","S did action A.\nFor any x, if x does action A, x is fully divine.\nTherefore, S is fully divine.\nE.g., A = non-culpably pronouncing the forgiveness of sins, non-culpably receiving worship, raising the dead, truly saying “Before Abraham was, I am”, creating the cosmos.","The Bible applies title or description “F” to S.\nFor any x, if the Bible applies title “F” to x, then x is fully divine.\nTherefore, S is fully divine.\nE.g., F = the first and the last, a god, the God, our savior","S has quality Q.\nFor any x, if x has quality Q, then x is fully divine.\nS is fully divine."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1396880233910632508"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"E.g., Q = sinlessness, omniscience, the power to perform miracles, something Christians should be baptized in the name of While such arguments are deductively valid, they suffer from a crucial ambiguity: What is meant by “fully divine”?","more":{"h":"Mark","p":["E.g., Q = sinlessness, omniscience, the power to perform miracles, something Christians should be baptized in the name of","While such arguments are deductively valid, they suffer from a crucial ambiguity: What is meant by “fully divine”? Until this is made clear, it isn’t clear which of the trinitarian theories is being argued for. A person being “fully divine” might, according to various theorists, amount to being constituted by the matter-like divine nature, being identical to God, being a mind of God, being a way God relates to himself or the world, and so on. Further, the epistemic status of each argument’s second premise may depend on what “divine” means.","Opponents of these sorts of argument typically give biblical counterexamples to the second premise (e.g., humans who are called “gods” but aren’t divine in the relevant sense, humans who are authorized by God to forgive sins but aren’t divine in the relevant sense). In other cases, they also challenge the first premise (e.g., Jesus denied being omniscient, there are inadequate grounds to say that the Son of God created the cosmos).","Another form of argument runs as follows.","Passage E is a true prophecy predicting that the God of Israel, Yahweh, will do action A.\nPassage F truly asserts that the prophecy in E was fulfilled in the life of Jesus Christ.\nTherefore, Jesus Christ just is the God of Israel, Yahweh.\nOpponents reply that this argument is invalid; it is possible for the premises to be true even though the conclusion is false. Even though the prediction “George W. Bush will conquer Iraq” may be said to be fulfilled by the actions of General Smith, it doesn’t follow that Smith and Bush are one and the same. Rather, Smith acted as the agent of Bush. Similarly, Yahweh acts through his servant Jesus. Another disadvantage of this argument is that even if it is sound, the conclusion is undesirable. If Jesus and God are held to be (numerically) identical, and one adds that the Father is “fully divine” in this same sense, i.e. the Father is numerically identical to God, then it logically follows that Jesus just is (is numerically identical to) the Father. And yet, according to any trinitarian, some things are true of one that are not true of the other. This is why nearly all trinitarian theories decline to identify more than one of the three persons with God. On the other hand, some embrace this as a mystery —something which appears contradictory but is in fact true. (See main entry section 4.2.)","This traditional case for the divinity of Jesus and the Holy Spirit may be best construed not as a collection of deductive arguments, but rather as an inference to the best explanation, an attempt to infer what best explains all the biblical texts considered together. In this genre, however, alternate explanations are rarely explored in any detail, much less shown to be inferior.","Many arguments of the above types date back to ancient times, and have been repeated in similar forms whenever mainstream trinitarianism has been attacked (Beckwith 2007; Bowman 2007; Bowman and Komoszewski 2007; George 2006; Stuart 1834; Waterland 1856a-e). A number of well developed refutations of these arguments dating from the 17th to 19th centuries have been largely forgotten by present-day theologians, philosophers, and apologists (Burnap 1845; Clarke 1978; Crellius Racovian; Crellius 1691; Emlyn 1746; Haynes 1797; Lardner 1793; Lindsey 1776, 1818; Norton 1859; Nye 1691b; Priestley 1791a-c; Wilson 1846)."],"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1396880233910632508"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"@Deen should this category be deleted?","more":{"h":"@Deen should this category be deleted?","p":["@Deen should this category be deleted?"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #mark","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1396880233910632508"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#mark)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-dr-matthew"],{"title":"Matthew","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Matthew","tree":{"they":"Matthew","we":"Paul Joyce Commentary on Ezekiel tells us that it is likely the original practise of the septuagint was to render “Lord Lord” as just “kyrios” not doubled 2) Matthew 1:23 “Jesus is prophecied in Isaiah 7:14 as God” , 1 A…","more":{"h":"Matthew","p":["Paul Joyce Commentary on Ezekiel tells us that it is likely the original practise of the septuagint was to render “Lord Lord” as just “kyrios” not doubled","2) Matthew 1:23 “Jesus is prophecied in Isaiah 7:14 as God”\n,","1 Add Reaction","There are two major problems with this","1) the initial context of the prophecy of Matthew 1:23 is about a birth to occur at the time of king ahaz, Matthew seems to think there’s a dual fulfillment going on here. However the fact that the first fulfillment had a boy named emmanuel be born in Ahaz time WITHOUT being God shows us that for a second fulfillment to mean that jesus is God is extremely far fetched\n,","2) The fulfilment with jesus being god hinges on the understanding of “emmanuel” meaning “God with us” as meaning “God is literally with us”.\n,\nnames including Gods name shouldn’t be taken literally in hebrew for example elijah’s name is God jehovah, that doesn’t mean that he is God. So when jesus is on earth God is with us in a symbolic sense palatable with the gospels with the spiritual idea that the father dwells in jesus empowering his ministry and not that jesus is identical to the God of israel.","Davies and Alisson (Christian Scholarly Commentary) Suggests these reasons for this alternative explanation of Isaiah 7:14 not meaning jesus is literally God but rather it is Gods presence."],"imgs":6,"credit":"Deenresponds · #matthew","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1397832084130758727"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Here'd be my response to the whole Lord Lord = God arg","more":{"h":"here'd be my response to the whole Lord Lord = God arg","p":["here'd be my response to the whole Lord Lord = God arg"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Deenresponds · #matthew","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1397832084130758727"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#matthew)."}});
topic(["christianity","trinity","d-dr-jesus-is-worshipped"],{"title":"Jesus is worshipped","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Jesus is worshipped","tree":{"they":"Jesus is worshipped","we":"Here is a lexical definition of the term Jesus only uses this term once and applies it to God, it is never applied to himself in the Gospels while “Proskuneo” is applied to those who prostrate to Jesus Here’s one Example…","more":{"h":"Jesus is worshipped","p":["here is a lexical definition of the term","Jesus only uses this term once and applies it to God, it is never applied to himself in the Gospels while “Proskuneo” is applied to those who prostrate to Jesus","Here’s one Example in Matthew 2:2 where the term Proskuneo is used when the Magi prostrate to Jesus","Here is a lexical definition for “Proskuneo”","Davies and Alisson (A scholarly Christian Commentary) Says in their commentary of Matthew that Proskuneo is used all across the OT to mean a type of prostration to kings and high officials which aligns with Jesus being the messiah and worthy of that same sort of reverence"],"imgs":9,"credit":"Deenresponds · #jesus-is-worshipped","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1398935078708707328"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#jesus-is-worshipped)."}});
topic(["christianity","trinity","d-dr-john-1-1"],{"title":"John 1 1","k":"Deenresponds","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"John 1 1","tree":{"they":"John 1 1","we":"Https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSSFbppPq/ TikTok · Coley TikTok · Coley 2054 likes, 578 comments.","more":{"h":"https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSSFbppPq/","p":["https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSSFbppPq/\nTikTok · Coley\nTikTok · Coley","2054 likes, 578 comments. “@whitemuslimguy”","1) There is a definite article in the Greek where it mentions the Father as god but there isn’t one for the son. So the Father is the god while the son is “a god” and as we know god is a fluid term in the bible","2) Our earliest commentary on John 1:1 theophilus of antioch tells us that at first the father was alone then The son was begotten. This isn’t coeternality and is how the earlier christian’s understood john 1:1 in 180AD"],"credit":"Deenresponds · #john-1-1","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1328402309297733662/1398950332662419567"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Deenresponds (#john-1-1)."}});
