topic(["christianity","church","d-ia-paul-related"],{"title":"Paul related","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"3 threads","children":{"t-paul-rebuked-by-jesus":{"title":"Paul rebuked by Jesus","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Paul rebuked by Jesus","tree":{"they":"Paul rebuked by Jesus","we":"Https://youtu.be/xf4JmdFbm4I Jesus REBUKES Paul | EXPLAINED Jesus REBUKES Paul | EXPLAINED","more":{"h":"https://youtu.be/xf4JmdFbm4I","p":["https://youtu.be/xf4JmdFbm4I\nJesus REBUKES Paul | EXPLAINED\nJesus REBUKES Paul | EXPLAINED"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #paul-related › Paul rebuked by Jesus","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1516263304463519815"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#paul-related)."}},"t-torah-dilemma":{"title":"Torah dilemma","k":"IA","blurb":"4 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Torah dilemma","tree":{"they":"Torah dilemma","we":"P1: Paul teaches that believers no longer have to observe the Mosaic Law.","more":{"h":"P1: Paul teaches that believers no longer have to observe the Mosaic Law.","p":["P1: Paul teaches that believers no longer have to observe the Mosaic Law.","P2: Jesus and the apostles teach that the Mosaic Law must continue to be observed.","P3 (hidden assumption): If one teacher affirms a claim and another teacher affirms its denial, then the second teacher's teaching is not in continuity with the first's.","P4 (hidden assumption): Continuity between two teachings runs both ways — if A's teaching is in continuity with B's, then B's is in continuity with A's.","C: Therefore, Paul's teaching is not in continuity with the teaching of Jesus and the apostles.","From Premise 1 and Premise 2 together, we get: Jesus and the apostles affirm that the Law must continue, and Paul denies that the Law must continue.","(Rule used: Conjunction, combining two established statements into a single joint statement.)","Premise 3 is a general rule about any two teachers and any claim. We apply it to this specific case: Jesus/the apostles as the affirming teacher, Paul as the denying teacher, and \"the Law must continue\" as the claim in question.","(Rule used: Universal Instantiation, taking a general principle and applying it to a particular case.)","Premise 4 is a general rule about any two teachings. We apply it to this case: Paul's teaching and the teaching of Jesus/the apostles.","(Rule used: Universal Instantiation, again.)","Step 4 tells us that continuity between Paul and Jesus/the apostles holds in one direction exactly when it holds in the other. Step 3 already told us it does not hold in the Jesus-to-Paul direction. So it cannot hold in the Paul-to-Jesus direction either.","(Rule used: Biconditional Elimination combined with Modus Tollens — from \"X if and only if Y\" and \"not Y,\" infer \"not X.\")","Creds to: @Teto for the syllogism"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #paul-related › Torah dilemma","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1516263304463519815"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"JESUS AND THE APOSTLES ON THE TORAH , Matthew 5:17-20 Matthew 15:1-4 Matthew 23:1-3 Luke 16:17 James 1:20-25 James 2:8-12","more":{"h":"JESUS AND THE APOSTLES ON THE TORAH","p":["JESUS AND THE APOSTLES ON THE TORAH\n,","Matthew 5:17-20 Matthew 15:1-4 Matthew 23:1-3 Luke 16:17 James 1:20-25 James 2:8-12"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #paul-related › Torah dilemma","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1516263304463519815"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Matthew 5:17-20 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , The Law and the Prophets , <17> \"Think not that I have come to abolish the law and the prophets; I have come not to abolish them but to fulfil them.","more":{"h":"Torah dilemma","p":["Matthew 5:17-20 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , The Law and the Prophets , <17> \"Think not that I have come to abolish the law and the prophets; I have come not to abolish them but to fulfil them. <18> For truly, I say to you, till heaven and earth pass away, not an iota, not a dot, will pass from the law until all is accomplished. <19> Whoever then relaxes one of the least of these commandments and teaches men so, shall be called least in the kingdom of heaven; but he who does them and teaches them shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven. <20> For I tell you, unless your righteousness exceeds that of the scribes and Pharisees, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven. , , BibleBot v15.1.0 by Kerygma Digital , , Matthew 15:1-4 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , The Tradition of the Elders , <1> Then Pharisees and scribes came to Jesus from Jerusalem and said, <2> \"Why do your disciples transgress the tradition of the elders? For they do not wash their hands when they eat.\" <3> He answered them, \"And why do you transgress the commandment of God for the sake of your tradition? <4> For God commanded, 'Honor your father and your mother,' and, 'He who speaks evil of father or mother, let him surely die.' , , BibleBot v15.1.0 by Kerygma Digital , , Matthew 23:1-3 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , Jesus Denounces Scribes and Pharisees , <1> Then said Jesus to the crowds and to his disciples, <2> \"The scribes and the Pharisees sit on Moses'seat; <3> so practice and observe whatever they tell you, but not what they do; for they preach, but do not practice. , , BibleBot v15.1.0 by Kerygma Digital , , Luke 16:17 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , <17> But it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away, than for one dot of the law to become void. , , BibleBot v15.1.0 by Kerygma Digital , , James 1:20-25 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , <20> for the anger of man does not work the righteousness of God. <21> Therefore put away all filthiness and rank growth of wickedness and receive with meekness the implanted word, which is able to save your souls. <22> But be doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving yourselves. <23> For if any one is a hearer of the word and not a doer, he is like a man who observes his natural face in a mirror; <24> for he observes himself and goes away and at once forgets what he was like. <25> But he who looks into the perfect law, the law of liberty, and perseveres, being no hearer that forgets but a doer that acts, he shall be blessed in his doing. , , BibleBot v15.1.0 by Kerygma Digital , , James 2:8-12 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , <8> If you really fulfil the royal law, according to the scripture, \"You shall love your neighbor as yourself,\" you do well. <9> But if you show partiality, you commit sin, and are convicted by the law as transgressors. <10> For whoever keeps the whole law but fails in one point has become gui"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #paul-related › Torah dilemma","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1516263304463519815"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"According to Jesus and the apostles, the law must be followed to be called great in the kingdom of heaven.","more":{"h":"According to Jesus and the apostles, the law must be followed to be called great in the kingdom of heaven.","p":["According to Jesus and the apostles, the law must be followed to be called great in the kingdom of heaven.\n,\nIt’s easier for heaven and earth to pass away than for a single dot of the law to become invalid.\n,\nThe Pharisees are to be obeyed in everything they teach (which includes the Torah)\n,\nThe law is perfect and it gives us liberty meaning it sets us free.\n,"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #paul-related › Torah dilemma","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1516263304463519815"},"next":[]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#paul-related)."}},"t-paulinian-dilemma":{"title":"Paulinian Dilemma","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Paulinian Dilemma","tree":{"they":"Paulinian Dilemma","we":"Pauliniandilemmamaxxer","more":{"h":"pauliniandilemmamaxxer","p":["pauliniandilemmamaxxer"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #paul-related › Paulinian Dilemma","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1516263304463519815"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#paul-related)."}}}});
topic(["christianity","bible","d-ia-authorship-of-the-new-testament"],{"title":"Authorship of the new testament","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Authorship of the new testament","tree":{"they":"Authorship of the new testament","we":"‎السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته mag started a thread: 1 and 2 Peter.","more":{"h":"‎السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته","p":["‎السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته","mag\n started a thread: 1 and 2 Peter. See all threads.","Frisk\n started a thread: Gospel of Mark. See all threads."],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #authorship-of-the-new-testament","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1520751809612873789"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#authorship-of-the-new-testament)."}});
topic(["christianity","jesus","d-ia-messianic-prophecies"],{"title":"Messianic prophecies","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"3 threads","children":{"t-pinned":{"title":"Pinned","k":"IA","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Pinned","tree":{"they":"Pinned","we":"Messianic Prophecies: A Question of Double Standards , Messianic prophecies are Old Testament passages that Christians believe predict the coming of Jesus.","more":{"h":"Messianic Prophecies: A Question of Double Standards","p":["Messianic Prophecies: A Question of Double Standards\n,\nMessianic prophecies are Old Testament passages that Christians believe predict the coming of Jesus. They are used to show that Jesus fulfills earlier biblical prophecy.","To support this, Christians rely heavily on an interpretive method known as typology. This approach allows them to set aside the original historical and linguistic context of a passage and read it as a \"spiritual foreshadowing\" of the New Testament. Whether a verse originally referred to Israel, a king, or a local event, its original context is ignored and reinterpreted as a \"type\" pointing to Jesus. So in practice the context becomes flexible and the meaning of the passage is reshaped to read Jesus in the OT.","Yet a clear double standard appears when Muslims point to these same texts as containing references to Prophet Muhammad ﷺ\nHis name in the Song of Solomon, the location of Paran in Deuteronomy, or the Arabian context of Isaiah 42. Many Christians then shift away from typology and turn to strict literalism! \nThe flexibility they use for their own readings is not accepted in these cases."],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #messianic-prophecies › Pinned","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1523412650393080008"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Now we Muslims also believe that Isa عليه السلام is the Messiah.","more":{"h":"Now we Muslims also believe that Isa عليه السلام is the Messiah. But we are not dependant on this framework.","p":["Now we Muslims also believe that Isa عليه السلام is the Messiah. But we are not dependant on this framework.","We believe in Prophet Isa عليه السلام because of what Allah has revealed about him in the Qur an. We don't need the Old Testament to confirm Jesus, we have Allah’s direct word. So we don't have to defend these so-called prophecies or this framework.","We believe the Bible has been altered, so we are not bound by the Jewish objections to Jesus' messiahship.","However, Christians don't believe the Old Testament is corrupted, they believe it is fully authentic and accurate. So they have to defend Hosea 11, Isaiah 53, Micah 5:1-2 etc because the New Testament explicitly cites these and presents them as prophecies of Jesus.\nThat's a position christians have to defend, muslims have no such burden"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #messianic-prophecies › Pinned","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1523412650393080008"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Micah 5:1-2 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , The Ruler from Bethlehem , <1> Now you are walled about with a wall; siege is laid against us; with a rod they strike upon the cheek the ruler of Israel.","more":{"h":"Pinned","p":["Micah 5:1-2 - Revised Standard Version (RSV) , , The Ruler from Bethlehem , <1> Now you are walled about with a wall; siege is laid against us; with a rod they strike upon the cheek the ruler of Israel. <2> But you, O Bethlehem Eph'rathah, who are little to be among the clans of Judah, from you shall come forth for me one who is to be ruler in Israel, whose origin is from of old, from ancient days. , , BibleBot v15.1.0 by Kerygma Digital , ,"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #messianic-prophecies › Pinned","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1523412650393080008"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#messianic-prophecies)."}},"t-isaiah-53-islamic-prophecy":{"title":"Isaiah 53 Islamic Prophecy","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Isaiah 53 Islamic Prophecy","tree":{"they":"Isaiah 53 Islamic Prophecy","we":"Full refutation of the Christian understanding of Isaiah 53 and showing how its actually an Islamic prophecy that proves 4:157 of the Quran (first I show how isa53 itself is not messianic, neither was its earliest interp…","more":{"h":"Isaiah 53 Islamic Prophecy","p":["Full refutation of the Christian understanding of Isaiah 53 and showing how its actually an Islamic prophecy that proves 4:157 of the Quran (first I show how isa53 itself is not messianic, neither was its earliest interpretetion, however later during the time of christ there is an expected messianic interpretetion of it, and it fully alligns with Islam)","Isaiah 53 Full Refutation.pdf 11.26 MB","this is heavily interrelated to ⁠Jesus Raised to Heaven Alive","added 2 slides"],"imgs":3,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #messianic-prophecies › Isaiah 53 Islamic Prophecy","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1523412650393080008"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#messianic-prophecies)."}},"t-jesus-raised-to-heaven-alive":{"title":"Jesus Raised to Heaven Alive","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Jesus Raised to Heaven Alive","tree":{"they":"Jesus Raised to Heaven Alive","we":"Extent slides on how the OT and Jesus' prophecy that he will be raised to heaven while appearing to suffer, and how the earliest Christians attest to this Jesus Raised to Heaven Alive (4).pdf 9.98 MB ⁠Isaiah 53 Islamic P…","more":{"h":"Jesus Raised to Heaven Alive","p":["Extent slides on how the OT and Jesus' prophecy that he will be raised to heaven while appearing to suffer, and how the earliest Christians attest to this","Jesus Raised to Heaven Alive (4).pdf 9.98 MB","⁠Isaiah 53 Islamic Prophecy view to see how Judah the Teacher of Righteousness also applies Isa53 to himself in a way that alligns with Islam and therefore we can now interpret Isa53 to Jesus in the same manner as above"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #messianic-prophecies › Jesus Raised to Heaven Alive","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1523412650393080008"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#messianic-prophecies)."}}}});
topic(["islam","morality","d-ia-apostasy-and-blasphemy-laws"],{"title":"Apostasy and blasphemy laws","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Apostasy and blasphemy laws","tree":{"they":"Apostasy and blasphemy laws","we":"Deuteronomy 17:2-5 We find an explicit command from the Lord to stone the apostate who worships other gods after the testimony of two or three witnesses.","more":{"h":"Deuteronomy 17:2-5","p":["Deuteronomy 17:2-5","We find an explicit command from the Lord to stone the apostate who worships other gods after the testimony of two or three witnesses.","In Exodus 32, the Lord commanded the Prophet Moses to kill the apostates from the tribe of Levi who worshipped the calf because they had turned away from the God of Israel. He killed three thousand of them.","In the Book of Numbers 25, when the people of Israel turned away and clung to Baal, the Lord commanded Moses to kill every one of his people who were clung to the worship of Baal. This was the only way for the Lord to spare the children of Israel.","Anyone who did not seek the Lord were to be put to death","In Leviticus, God commands Moses to have anyone who blasphemes His name stoned to death, whether native or foreigner (Leviticus 24:16).","Qadr | قَدَر\n started a thread: church/fathers, who believed in these laws. See all threads."],"imgs":7,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #apostasy-and-blasphemy-laws","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1534588327691550930"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Conclusion The only Christians that oppose apostasy/blasphemy laws are modern day Christians who are effected by secular liberalism and the enlightenment If we look back in history before the enlightenment Christian soci…","more":{"h":"Conclusion","p":["Conclusion","The only Christians that oppose apostasy/blasphemy laws are modern day Christians who are effected by secular liberalism and the enlightenment If we look back in history before the enlightenment Christian societys implemented apostasy/blasphemy laws. Church fathers and theologians whether Catholic, Protestant or Orthodox believed in them some Christians might say o that’s the Old Testament Jesus fulfilled the law he abolished it that’s just cope churches implanted these laws Christian societies implanted these laws church fathers believed in them some Christians might say they were wrong we reply by saying for following God’s law?","apostasy/blasphemy laws are found within Christianity","Captain Majora | ماجورا القبطان\n started a thread: Apostasy Law in Deuterocanon. See all threads."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #apostasy-and-blasphemy-laws","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1534588327691550930"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#apostasy-and-blasphemy-laws)."}});
topic(["atheism","d-ia-arguments-for-god"],{"title":"Arguments for god","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"5 threads","children":{"t-arguments-for-god":{"title":"Arguments for God","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Arguments for God","tree":{"they":"Arguments for God","we":"P1: Logical absolutes exist. P2: Logical absolutes are conceptual.","more":{"h":"P1: Logical absolutes exist.","p":["P1: Logical absolutes exist.","P2: Logical absolutes are conceptual.","P3: Concepts exist in the mind only (they are mental).","P4: Logical absolutes would exist even if your minds did not","P5: Therefore, logical absolutes are transcendent","P6: Since logical absolutes are transcendent and conceptual, they must exist in a transcendent mind.","• P7: This transcendent mind is that we recognize as God.","__","Either God exists or does not exist.","God can neither come into existence nor go out of existence.","If God exists, then He cannot cease to exist.","Therefore, if God exists, He exists necessarily.","If God does not exist, then He cannot come into existence.","Therefore, if God does not exist, His existence is impossible.","Therefore, God’s existence is either necessary or impossible.","However, God’s existence is only impossible if the concept of God is self-contradictory.","The concept of God is not self-contradictory.","Therefore, God’s existence is not impossible.","Therefore, from 7 and 10, God’s existence is necessary.","___"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #arguments-for-god › Arguments for God","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514404863285395656"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#arguments-for-god)."}},"t-god-design-and-fine-tuning":{"title":"God, Design, and Fine Tuning","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"God, Design, and Fine Tuning","tree":{"they":"God, Design, and Fine Tuning","we":"God_Design_and_Fine_Tuning.pdf 207.25 KB Download","more":{"h":"GodDesignandFineTuning.pdf 207.25 KB Download","p":["God_Design_and_Fine_Tuning.pdf 207.25 KB Download"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #arguments-for-god › God, Design, and Fine-Tuning","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514404863285395656"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#arguments-for-god)."}},"t-matter-to-consciousness":{"title":"Matter to consciousness","k":"IA","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Matter to consciousness","tree":{"they":"Matter to consciousness","we":"Majority of arguments that argue for the existence of God have one underlying issue.","more":{"h":"Matter to consciousness","p":["Majority of arguments that argue for the existence of God have one underlying issue. The issue is that they suddenly leap to a God with specific attributes or A god that is common in their society. Almost every Christian philosopher to be fair cuz Aquinas, William Craig, Paley and Descartes have all done it. I dont blame them but as muslims we know our belief and religion is so strong, we dont need to leap","Anyway heres the syllogism and ill further explain them:","Premise 1: The fundemental cause of the physical universe is either a conscious(a mind) or entirely unconscious(matter/energy)","Premise 2: An Entirely unconscious entity cannot produce a subjective conscious awareness purely from itself(since unconscious matter cannot possess intentionality or a subjective experience to pass on)","Premise 3: Empiraclly, conscious beings such as humans and animals exist in the universe","Premise 4: The deduction from P3 and P2 is; conciousness cannot have originated from an unconscious physical cause","Conclusion: Therefore the fundemental cause of the universe, itself, must be concious","With this we dont have to leap to anything, and im sure this reasoning would satisfy some atheists.","to be continued"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #arguments-for-god › matter-to-consciousness","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514404863285395656"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Explanatioins of each premise: Premise 1 and 2 Im sure you are aware of Al Ghazali and Aquinas's Cosmological argument.","more":{"h":"Explanatioins of each premise:","p":["Explanatioins of each premise:","Premise 1 and 2\nIm sure you are aware of Al Ghazali and Aquinas's Cosmological argument. So i dont have to try and prove the first cause now as there are a plethora of arguments pertaining to that. However one problem with most of these arguments is that they suddenly leap to a God we must all worship, whose all power and conscious. Thats how we derive our morality etc. For example the First Cause will be the Christian Triune God for whatever reason yet its UNSUBSTANITIATED. Im here to substantiate it","Say for example, the univeses first cause was a brute fact. Something with no will, consciousness or intentionality caused the existense of universe. It would be odd or rather illogical for conscious entities such as humans to roam the universe.","Yet they do","but but...its brain capacity that came from evolution\nOkay cool, then why do humans have a subjective expierence?","Yes i could i argue that we evolved and our brains created consciousness or whatever. Just like how our cells in our body attack other cells to protect us from diseases, and how plants grow and stretch towards sunlight unconscoiusly through a process known as phototropism. Computers calculate numbers and AI generates content yet remains unconscious.","Imagine a stone for the sake of argument called 'Stone 1'. Stone 1 holds the same properties as any other stone -- including a lack of consiousness. Say Stone 1 breaks and produces a new stone called 'Stone 2' . Miraculously, Stone 2 starts questioning their existence, they feel bored, they are sad, they are angry -- basically a subjective experiecne. How can Stone 2 possess properties of consciousness while its originator(Stone 1) does not possess these same properties?"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #arguments-for-god › matter-to-consciousness","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514404863285395656"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#arguments-for-god)."}},"t-psychological-harmony":{"title":"Psychological harmony","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Psychological harmony","tree":{"they":"Psychological harmony","we":"Brother @The general Mike and@صَيَّامُ بْنُ عِرْفَانَ sended this CUTPHAv2-2.pdf 239.42 KB https://youtu.be/JXyhRz1GcnQ?si=yNP1ugn61dUAfkTr I INVADED Athiest Tiktok!","more":{"h":"Brother @The general Mike and@صَيَّامُ بْنُ عِرْفَانَ sended this","p":["Brother @The general Mike and@صَيَّامُ بْنُ عِرْفَانَ sended this","CUTPHAv2-2.pdf 239.42 KB","https://youtu.be/JXyhRz1GcnQ?si=yNP1ugn61dUAfkTr\nI INVADED Athiest Tiktok! TOP Athiest STEAMROLLED On God's Existenc...\nI INVADED Athiest Tiktok! TOP Athiest STEAMROLLED On God's Existenc..."],"imgs":1,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #arguments-for-god › psychological-harmony","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514404863285395656"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#arguments-for-god)."}},"t-argument-from-the-default":{"title":"Argument from the default","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Argument from the default","tree":{"they":"Argument from the default","we":"Scans are by @صَيَّامُ بْنُ عِرْفَانَ Argument_From_Default.pdf Qadr | قَدَر changed the post title: Arguments from the default Qadr | قَدَر changed the post title: Argument from the default","more":{"h":"Scans are by @صَيَّامُ بْنُ عِرْفَانَ","p":["Scans are by @صَيَّامُ بْنُ عِرْفَانَ","Argument_From_Default.pdf","Qadr | قَدَر\n changed the post title: Arguments from the default","Qadr | قَدَر\n changed the post title: Argument from the default"],"imgs":4,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #arguments-for-god › Argument from the default","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514404863285395656"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#arguments-for-god)."}}}});
topic(["atheism","d-ia-religion-and-morals"],{"title":"Religion and morals","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"2 threads","children":{"t-the-is-ought-problem":{"title":"The Is Ought Problem","k":"IA","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"The Is Ought Problem","tree":{"they":"The Is Ought Problem","we":"The is–ought problem: what is possible doesn't decide what is right , People often move from what is to what ought to be.","more":{"h":"The Is Ought Problem","p":["The is–ought problem: what is possible doesn't decide what is right\n,\nPeople often move from what is to what ought to be. They're different questions.","Is: what's the case, what can happen, what people are capable of\n,\nOught: what people should do, what's right or wrong\n,","Hume noticed that moral conclusions don't follow automatically from descriptive facts.","Does \"can\" mean \"ought\"?\nNo.","Women can become excellent military leaders with training and experience.\n,\nTherefore women ought to become military leaders.\n,","The first is about ability. The second is about what people should do. The conclusion needs more than the premise.","The same goes for one person. Ahmed might be exceptionally good at maths, but that doesn't mean he ought to be a mathematician. He may have other goals, duties or reasons. To say someone ought to do something, you need extra premises about why it's good or required.","Does \"natural\" mean \"good\"?\nNo. A behaviour can have a biological explanation without being right. People may have natural tendencies toward aggression, jealousy or competition, but explaining them doesn't make every expression of them permissible.","Explaining why something happens isn't the same as justifying it."],"imgs":2,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #religion-and-morals › The Is-Ought Problem","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514406873565106288"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"What about men and women? Say someone argues that men or women can excel in a role with enough education, training and experience.","more":{"h":"What about men and women?","p":["What about men and women?\nSay someone argues that men or women can excel in a role with enough education, training and experience. Even if that's true, it shows what people can achieve. It doesn't settle what roles they ought to have, which should be encouraged, or whether any should be required or banned. Those need separate arguments about morality, duties and rights.","It cuts both ways. Showing that men can do a role doesn't show they ought to, and the same goes for women.","Ability and biology aren't irrelevant. They can matter when judging the wisdom of an arrangement. They just don't settle the moral question by themselves.","What does this mean for Muslims?\nWhen a ruling is established by the Qur'an and the authentic Sunnah, you don't have to find every biological or social benefit behind it first. Allah is al-Ḥakīm, the All-Wise.","Keep two things apart:","\"Allah and His Messenger ﷺ established this ruling.\" That's the evidence.\n,\n\"I think this is one of the reasons behind it.\" That's an explanation of the wisdom, which may be right, partial or wrong.\n,"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #religion-and-morals › The Is-Ought Problem","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514406873565106288"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"‎ So what's the key question? Not what people are capable of, but what justifies the conclusion that they ought to do it.","more":{"h":"The Is Ought Problem","p":["‎\nSo what's the key question?\nNot what people are capable of, but what justifies the conclusion that they ought to do it.","What someone can do doesn't decide what they ought to do.\n,\nWhat's natural isn't automatically good.\n,\nExplaining the cause of a behaviour doesn't justify it.\n,\nShowing that society could be organised differently doesn't prove the alternative is better.\n,","Further reading\n The Amorality of Social Constructionism\nhttps://islamicdiscourse.substack.com/p/the-amorality-of-social-constructionism\n Emphasizing Gods in Our Apologetics\nhttps://islamicdiscourse.substack.com/p/emphasizing-gods-in-our-apologetics"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #religion-and-morals › The Is-Ought Problem","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514406873565106288"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#religion-and-morals)."}},"t-atheist-rpe":{"title":"Atheist rpe","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Atheist rpe","tree":{"they":"Atheist rpe","we":"Atheist rape is a natural evolutionary behavior practiced by the ancestors of humans from animals.","more":{"h":"Atheist rape is a natural evolutionary behavior practiced by the ancestors of humans from animals.","p":["Atheist rape is a natural evolutionary behavior practiced by the ancestors of humans from animals.","Therefore, the largest rape crime recorded in history was carried out by atheists, as the atheist Russian army raped 2 million German women between the ages of 7 and 70, who gave birth to half a million children as a result of that, and some committed suicide before the atheists arrived."],"imgs":4,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #religion-and-morals › Atheist r🍇pe","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1514406873565106288"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#religion-and-morals)."}}}});
topic(["atheism","d-ia-atheist-arguments-1"],{"title":"Atheist arguments 1","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"3 threads","children":{"t-evolution":{"title":"Evolution","k":"IA","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Evolution","tree":{"they":"Evolution","we":"This argument works REALLY well against atheists/deists and such People who don't believe in god or don't believe God sent scripture Evolution has made/optimized us to survive.","more":{"h":"This argument works REALLY well against atheists/deists and such","p":["This argument works REALLY well against atheists/deists and such","People who don't believe in god or don't believe God sent scripture","Evolution has made/optimized us to survive.","Our senses are optimised for survival.","We can trust our senses for survival.","So, why is it the case that we trust our senses to find truth, when they (senses) are not made for it?","Its like using a pickaxe to fix nails into wood","Yes, sometimes it will work, but the majority of the time, it will not","But can we trust it (pickaxe on nail) to work? No","Similarly, yeah, sometimes we can find truth using our senses, but the majority of the time, we don't know if our senses will work or not","We don't know","The only response to this is that \"survival necessitates true beliefs","Therefore, by getting optimised to survive, our senses have automatically been optimised for \"truth finding\"\"","first of all, thats not true, second, natural selection doesn't care about true beliefs","Its only criteria is survival, even if the cost of it is to produce a false belief","For eg, some evolutionary scientists have said that the reason why we see faces/people in the dark even though they are not there is because of evolution","This feature of \"producing false beliefs\" is there to prevent us from harm","Like in forests at night time, there are many dangerous creatures, so we have evolved a feature of \"producing false beliefs\" so that we may be protected by whats out there","and forget all this yapping, lets grant that survival DOES need true beliefs","lets say that the paths of \"survival\" and \"truth finding\" does converge at a point","Whats the proof that it has converged?","coz it could be the case that it have not been converged but will after 10 million more years of evolution","therefore, we cant trust our senses now","back to the same problem","They have to now prove that currently we can trust our senses","if you go further with this reasoning, this argument pushes them towards hyper scepticism"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › Evolution","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"On the other hand, we theists DO have reasons to trust our senses for truth finding God made us so that we can be tested, and for tests, we need to have sound aql Who will believe in him and his scriptures and who wont O…","more":{"h":"on the other hand, we theists DO have reasons to trust our senses for truth finding","p":["on the other hand, we theists DO have reasons to trust our senses for truth finding","God made us so that we can be tested, and for tests, we need to have sound aql","Who will believe in him and his scriptures and who wont","One can think of more points as to why a theistic god would make us to find truth"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › Evolution","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#atheist-arguments 1)."}},"t-the-problem-of-evil-ibn-al-qayyim-s-comprehensive-":{"title":"The Problem of Evil: Ibn al Qayyim's Comprehensive Theodicy","k":"IA","blurb":"3 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"The Problem of Evil: Ibn al Qayyim's Comprehensive Theodicy","tree":{"they":"Does that mean Allah needs evil?","we":"No. There's a difference between having an attribute and manifesting an action toward creation.","more":{"h":"Does that mean Allah needs evil?","p":["No. There's a difference between having an attribute and manifesting an action toward creation. Allah doesn't need sinners to have forgiveness, or the sick to have healing. When a sinner exists, He may manifest forgiveness toward him.","Creation is where these actions appear. It doesn't give Allah His attributes or complete Him. The dependence is from creation on Allah, never the other way.","Divine Signs\n,\nThe clearest demonstrations of God's power come out of conflict between prophets and disbelievers: Noah's flood, the parting of the sea, Ibrāhīm (عليه السلام) emerging unharmed from the fire. Signs like these arise from adversity, not comfort.","Divine Love\n,\nSome of the highest ranks, like being a friend of Allah, are described as open to those who endure hardship for His sake. Ease alone doesn't produce that closeness. Struggle does.","The Greater Good\n,\nGod permits lesser harms as the path to greater goods that couldn't otherwise exist. Courage, patience, generosity and self-restraint are responses to difficulty. They can't exist in a world with no friction.","Some psychological research also finds that religious devotion and gratitude rise in populations facing real hardship, and fall where existential security is high. Ease tends to dull spiritual responsiveness.","Testing\n,\nTrials separate sincere faith from superficial faith, a theme throughout the Qur'an. Someone who worships only when things go well and leaves when they get hard is described as losing in both this world and the next.","Free Will\n,\nWorship is worth more when it's chosen, not forced like the submission of the natural world. That freedom means nothing without a real possibility of choosing wrongly.","Education\n,\nMeeting your own sin and weakness keeps you humble and aware that you depend on God. A hadith cited here says: \"If you did not sin, I would fear something worse for you than that, and that is pride.\"","Greater reward in the hereafter\n,\nSuffering makes the reward more fully appreciated. Paradise also has many levels, and filling the higher ones takes a wide range of effort and struggle. That requires a world where real variation between people is possible.","Mystery\n,\nNot every case of suffering has an explanation we can reach. Ibn al-Qayyim is direct about this: we can no more grasp every detail of divine wisdom than \"a bat can see the light of the sun.\"","He doesn't claim everything has a discoverable reason. God has shown enough of the pattern to trust that the unexplained cases fit the same wisdom."],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › The Problem of Evil: Ibn al-Qayyim's Comprehensive Theodicy","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[{"they":"Is this the \"best of all possible worlds\"?","we":"Ibn al-Qayyim seems to have quietly disagreed with al-Ghazālī's famous claim, without naming him.","more":{"h":"Is this the \"best of all possible worlds\"?","p":["Ibn al-Qayyim seems to have quietly disagreed with al-Ghazālī's famous claim, without naming him. His position is more precise: God is the most perfect Creator, and this world is the best possible system for the wise purposes He intended. That isn't the same as every single element being maximally good in isolation. Something better could always be imagined. The point is that the whole system, with good and hardship together, is calibrated for its purpose."],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › The Problem of Evil: Ibn al-Qayyim's Comprehensive Theodicy","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[{"they":"What about suffering that seems to serve no purpose?","we":"A more recent treatment takes the sharpest modern version of the problem, gratuitous evil.","more":{"h":"What about suffering that seems to serve no purpose?","p":["A more recent treatment takes the sharpest modern version of the problem, gratuitous evil. Evil with no obvious purpose can still serve one that appears later, sometimes generations later, through people who rise up to resist it.","Two more points:\nThe return of righteousness. A whole community turning back to righteousness is described as even more beloved to Allah than an individual's repentance. This is tied to the hadith that Islam \"began strange and will return to being strange,\" with a blessing for those who hold to it then. Without hardship and decline, there's nothing for renewal to rise against.","Hypocrisy. Sincere and hollow belief look identical when nothing costly is at stake. Hypocrisy as a distinct problem emerged once faith became advantageous, not costly. Hardship is what forces the gap between real and performed belief into the open.","Sources & Further Reading\nIbn al-Qayyim, Shifāʾ al-ʿAlīl (Arabic text)\nIbn al-Qayyim, Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya on Divine Wisdom and the Problem of Evil (English translation, Islamic Texts Society)\nIbn al-Qayyim, Miftāḥ Dār al-Saʿādah (Arabic text)\nIbn Qayyim al-Jawziyya on Divine Wisdom and the Problem of Evil\nIbn Qayyim al-Jawziyya on Divine Wisdom and the Problem of Evil\nالرئيسية | المكتبة الوقفية\nالرئيسية | المكتبة الوقفية\nمكتبة وقفية للكتب المصوّرة والفهارس: تصفّح أحدث الإضافات، الأكثر تحميلاً، الأقسام والوسوم.","https://islamicdiscourse.substack.com/p/answering-a-jews-question-about-collective?utm_source=publication-search\nAnswering a Jew’s Question About Collective Punishment\nAnswering a Jew’s Question About Collective Punishment\nOnce, I was in discussion with an orthodox Jew considering Islam, and he asked me how to reconcile the idea that “no one bears the burden of another” with the fact that God does at times collectively punish towns and cities along with the innocent and guilty alike."],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › The Problem of Evil: Ibn al-Qayyim's Comprehensive Theodicy","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#atheist-arguments 1)."}},"t-why-does-allah-test-humanity":{"title":"Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","k":"IA","blurb":"4 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","tree":{"they":"Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","we":"‎ Ahl al-Sunnah reconciles these verses by affirming that the servant truly chooses and acts, but his ability, existence, and opportunity are created by Allah.","more":{"h":"Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","p":["‎","Ahl al-Sunnah reconciles these verses by affirming that the servant truly chooses and acts, but his ability, existence, and opportunity are created by Allah. Shaykh Ibn Bāz explained: “The human being in his actions has choice, will, and intention… therefore he deserves punishment for sin and reward for obedience because he did that through will, intention, and ability, but despite this he does not exit the decree of Allah.” Likewise, the scholars stated: “Allah created the human and his actions, and granted him will, ability, choice, and intention… and He only held him accountable for actions done by his own will and choice; therefore the human is not compelled.”","This directly answers the claim that “our decisions are really God’s decisions.” In Islam, Allah is the Creator of the servant and his capacities, but the servant himself acquires and performs the act willingly. That is why punishment and reward are meaningful. If humans were compelled in the absolute sense, commanding and prohibiting them would be unjust and absurd. Scholars explicitly argued this point: “It is intellectually impossible that divine commands be directed to a being who does not possess the ability to choose obedience, because Allah is Wise and far above meaningless action.”","‎"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The Qur’an also grounds accountability in voluntary action: وَأَن لَّيْسَ لِلْإِنسَانِ إِلَّا مَا سَعَىٰ ۝ وَأَنَّ سَعْيَهُ سَوْفَ يُرَىٰ ۝ ثُمَّ يُجْزَاهُ الْجَزَاءَ الْأَوْفَىٰ “And that each person will only have what…","more":{"h":"The Qur’an also grounds accountability in voluntary action:","p":["The Qur’an also grounds accountability in voluntary action:","وَأَن لَّيْسَ لِلْإِنسَانِ إِلَّا مَا سَعَىٰ ۝ وَأَنَّ سَعْيَهُ سَوْفَ يُرَىٰ ۝ ثُمَّ يُجْزَاهُ الْجَزَاءَ الْأَوْفَىٰ","“And that each person will only have what they endeavoured towards, that their endeavours will be seen, and then they will be fully rewarded.” (Qur’an 53:39–41)","كُلُّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِينَةٌ","“Every soul is held in pledge for what it has earned.” (Qur’an 74:38)","‎","As for the objection, “Why test us if Allah already knows the result?” the answer is that knowledge is not the same as compulsion, and manifestation is not the same as ignorance. Allah’s knowledge of what people will choose does not force them into choosing it. Classical scholars explained that the purpose of the test is for deeds to become outward realities deserving reward or punishment. One scholar cited the saying attributed to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib that Allah tests people “so that actions may appear by which they deserve reward or punishment.” The Qur’an itself says:","وَلِيَبْتَلِيَ اللَّهُ مَا فِي صُدُورِكُمْ وَلِيُمَحِّصَ مَا فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ","“So that Allah may test what is in your hearts and purify what is within your hearts.” (Qur’an 3:154)","‎"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"The reason Islamic scholars give is that, without the lived reality of choice and action, there would be no meaningful manifestation of sincerity, patience, gratitude, oppression, repentance, or faith.","more":{"h":"Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","p":["The reason Islamic scholars give is that, without the lived reality of choice and action, there would be no meaningful manifestation of sincerity, patience, gratitude, oppression, repentance, or faith. Allah already knows all things eternally, but the servant must act so that judgment occurs upon manifested deeds, not merely hidden potential.","The argument concerning infants misunderstands the nature of the worldly test. The test is not imposed identically on every human being regardless of capacity or circumstance. Islam teaches that accountability depends upon ability, maturity, and comprehension. A newborn who dies has committed no disbelief or rebellion; therefore, there is nothing unjust in Allah granting mercy to such a soul. This does not prove that the test is unnecessary for morally responsible adults. Rather, it demonstrates that Allah does not punish without responsibility and does not burden anyone beyond their capacity. Scholars noted that one who lacks awareness and choice is not morally accountable.","In fact, sparing some souls from prolonged worldly trials is itself part of divine mercy and wisdom, not evidence against testing. Allah tests different people differently. Some are tested through long lives, others through hardship, others through ease, and some are taken before accountability begins. None of these cases negates the wisdom of testing morally responsible beings who possess intellect, desire, and choice.","The final claim, “It would be more merciful not to test humanity,” assumes that mercy means preventing every possibility of failure. In Islam, however, mercy includes creating beings capable of freely attaining nearness to Allah, eternal reward, virtue, repentance, love, sacrifice, and conscious worship. A world without choice would also be a world without moral meaning. The Qur’an presents earthly life as the arena in which humans voluntarily pursue truth or falsehood:"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"‎ إِنَّا هَدَيْنَاهُ السَّبِيلَ إِمَّا شَاكِرًا وَإِمَّا كَفُورًا “Indeed, We guided him to the way, whether he be grateful or ungrateful.” (Qur’an 76:3) Scholars explained that Allah “left freedom of choice for people, …","more":{"h":"Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","p":["‎","إِنَّا هَدَيْنَاهُ السَّبِيلَ إِمَّا شَاكِرًا وَإِمَّا كَفُورًا","“Indeed, We guided him to the way, whether he be grateful or ungrateful.” (Qur’an 76:3)","Scholars explained that Allah “left freedom of choice for people, so the effect of choice would appear.”","The Salaf al-Ṣāliḥīn and later scholars therefore held a balanced position between two extremes: they rejected the idea that human beings are forced like machines or puppets, and they also rejected the idea that humans act independently of Allah. As stated in works of creed such as Sharḥ al-ʿAqīdah al-Ṭaḥāwiyyah: “The servant is not compelled; rather, he has will and choice, but his will is subordinate to the will of Allah.”","The Islamic conclusion is coherent and internally consistent:","Allah eternally knows and decrees all things.\n,\nHuman beings still possess real will and choice within what Allah has created for them.\n,\nThe worldly test exists not because Allah lacks knowledge, but because divine justice and wisdom require deeds to be manifested.\n,\nAccountability applies where there is capacity and choice.\n,\nMercy is not negated by testing; rather, the test is the path through which eternal mercy, forgiveness, reward, and moral excellence become meaningful realities.\n,"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #atheist-arguments 1 › Why Does Allah Test Humanity?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1549150963980304414"},"next":[]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#atheist-arguments 1)."}}}});
topic(["other","hinduism","d-ia-karma-vs-qadar"],{"title":"Karma vs qadar","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"2 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Karma vs qadar","tree":{"they":"Karma vs qadar","we":"Like many Muslims, I used to think karma was basically the same as qadr (Allah’s decree).","more":{"h":"Like many Muslims, I used to think karma was basically the same as qadr (Allah’s decree).","p":["Like many Muslims, I used to think karma was basically the same as qadr (Allah’s decree).","My thinking was simple: if you do good, good will come back to you. If you do bad, bad will come back to you. Since Islam teaches reward and punishment, I thought karma was just another word for the same idea.","As I learned more about Islam, I realized I was wrong.","I wasn’t learning an Islamic version of karma. I was changing the meaning of karma until it matched Islam. At that point, it wasn’t really karma anymore.","Yes, there are some similarities. Both teach that our actions matter and that we are responsible for what we do. But once you look deeper, the differences are huge.","A common way people describe karma is:","“Do good, and good will happen to you. Do bad, and bad will happen to you.”","Islam doesn’t teach that life works like this.","The Qur’an teaches that this life is a test, not a system where every good deed brings an immediate reward or every sin brings an immediate punishment.","“We will surely test you with fear, hunger, loss of wealth, lives, and crops. But give good news to those who are patient.” (Qur’an 2:155)"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #karma-vs-qadar","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1521773507376054352"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Allah SWT also tells us: “No disaster happens on earth or to yourselves except that it was written before We made it happen.” (Qur’an 57:22) This changes how Muslims see hardship.","more":{"h":"Allah SWT also tells us:","p":["Allah SWT also tells us:","“No disaster happens on earth or to yourselves except that it was written before We made it happen.” (Qur’an 57:22)","This changes how Muslims see hardship.","For example, if a baby dies shortly after birth, we do not ask, “Whose karma was it?” We believe it happened because Allah decreed it, and His wisdom is perfect even if we do not understand it.","The same is true for wealth and poverty.","A rich person is not automatically good.","A poor person is not automatically bad.","Both wealth and poverty can be tests from Allah.","Another big difference is forgiveness.","Karma is usually understood as an impersonal law of cause and effect. Islam teaches that Allah is the One who judges, and He can forgive those who sincerely repent.","Allah SWT says:","“O My servants who have sinned against themselves, do not lose hope in Allah’s mercy. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. He is the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful.” (Qur’an 39:53)","Finally, Islam does not teach that every evil person will be punished in this life. Allah may punish them now, He may forgive them if they sincerely repent, or He may delay their punishment until the Day of Judgment.","https://islamicdiscourse.substack.com/p/reincarnation-an-islamic-critique\nReincarnation: An Islamic Critique\nReincarnation: An Islamic Critique\nReincarnation is the belief that after death a person returns to earthly life in another body, usually as part of an ongoing process of moral development, purification, punishment, reward, or spiritual evolution."],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #karma-vs-qadar","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1521773507376054352"},"next":[]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#karma-vs-qadar)."}});
topic(["other","hinduism","d-ia-gods-fighting-each-other"],{"title":"Gods fighting each other","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"6 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Gods fighting each other","tree":{"they":"Gods fighting each other","we":"Brahma Vs Shiva , Varaha Purana 97.1-7 , ”Varaha said: O Earth, now listen to the origin of Rudra Vrata, by knowing which one gets freed from all sins.","more":{"h":"Brahma Vs Shiva","p":["Brahma Vs Shiva\n,\nVaraha Purana 97.1-7\n,\n”Varaha said: O Earth, now listen to the origin of Rudra Vrata, by knowing which one gets freed from all sins. The red-eyed and tawny coloured Rudra who was created by Brahma in his third birth, was borne by him in pleasure on his shoulder. When he was thus on the shoulder, the fifth head of Brahma told Rudra the Atharvan mantra by which release is obtained. ‘O Kapalin, Rudra, Babhru, Bhava, Kairata, Suvrata, my valiant and broad-eyed son, do protect this world’. When Rudra was thus addressed by the names which he would be getting in future he was angry at the word ‘Kapala’ used and clipped off that (fifth) head. The head was clipped off by the nail in the left thumb, but it got to the hand.”","All the Puranas agree that Shiva beheaded Brahma, but they differ on why it happened. In the verses you mentioned, it says Shiva got mad when Brahma called him Kapala. But in Kurma Purana 2.31.1-32, it says Shiva and Brahma were arguing about who’s more powerful, and Shiva, annoyed by Brahma’s arrogance, chopped off his head in anger.","In the Shiva Purana, there’s a story that mentions Shiva’s inclination to confront Brahma. This stems from an incident where Brahma, having cast a lustful gaze upon Shiva’s wife, faced consequences resulting from an inappropriate discharge of semen. Shiva Purana 2.2.19.43-45\nThe Varaha Purana, Part 1 : J. L. Shastri, G. P. Bhatt, S. Venkatas...\nThe Varaha Purana, Part 1 : J. L. Shastri, G. P. Bhatt, S. Venkatas...\nThis book was published by Motilal Banarsidass, the oldest publisher in India. For more information on this and other books please...\nKurma Purana Full (Parts 1 and 2) : Motilal Banarsidass Publishers ...\nKurma Purana Full (Parts 1 and 2) : Motilal Banarsidass Publishers ...\nDownloaded from West Bengal Public Library...\nDescription of Śiva’s sports [Chapter 19]\nDescription of Śiva’s sports [Chapter 19]\nBrahmā said:— 1. After giving his daughter in marriage, Dakṣa gave her different articles in the form of dowry. Many gifts were given to Śiva. Dakṣa g..."],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #gods-fighting-each-other","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1530161197452628039"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Shiva Purana 7.1.30.19 , ”The lord cut off the fifth head of Brahmā who stubbornly and repeatedly censured Śiva calling him “O son.” The principle of Śiva [Chapter 30] The principle of Śiva [Chapter 30] The sages said:— 1.","more":{"h":"Shiva Purana 7.1.30.19","p":["Shiva Purana 7.1.30.19\n,\n”The lord cut off the fifth head of Brahmā who stubbornly and repeatedly censured Śiva calling him “O son.”\nThe principle of Śiva [Chapter 30]\nThe principle of Śiva [Chapter 30]\nThe sages said:— 1. The activities of deities of domestic nature are curious, dense and inscrutable, even to the gods. They delude our minds. 2. In th...","Vishnu Vs Shiva\n,\nIn another notable encounter between Shiva and Krishna, Shiva aligns himself with Kasiraja and faces defeat at the hands of Krishna. However, in the Skanda Purana, the narrative takes a different turn, portraying a battle between Shiva and Vishnu. The account unfolds with a king named Paundraka claiming to be Vasudeva, infuriating Krishna and prompting him to prepare for a confrontation against the imposter Vasudeva (Paundraka). King Paundraka finds support from his ally, the King of Kasi named Kasiraja, who, being a devotee of Shiva, seeks Shiva’s assistance in the battle against Krishna. Shiva agrees to help Kasiraja in this conflict.","Skanda Purana 2.2.12.17-18\n,\n”Nila mountain is in the third Yojana (i.e. 3X12 Kms.). This is the holy spot of the Lord of Gauri named Ekamrakavana. Not far off, O king, is the place where, being afraid, he sought refuge. Indradyumna said: Why was the Lord of Gauri (Siva) frightened? With whom did he seek refuge"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #gods-fighting-each-other","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1530161197452628039"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Vishnu Vs Shiva , In another notable encounter between Shiva and Krishna, Shiva aligns himself with Kasiraja and faces defeat at the hands of Krishna.","more":{"h":"Vishnu Vs Shiva","p":["Vishnu Vs Shiva\n,\nIn another notable encounter between Shiva and Krishna, Shiva aligns himself with Kasiraja and faces defeat at the hands of Krishna. However, in the Skanda Purana, the narrative takes a different turn, portraying a battle between Shiva and Vishnu. The account unfolds with a king named Paundraka claiming to be Vasudeva, infuriating Krishna and prompting him to prepare for a confrontation against the imposter Vasudeva (Paundraka). King Paundraka finds support from his ally, the King of Kasi named Kasiraja, who, being a devotee of Shiva, seeks Shiva’s assistance in the battle against Krishna. Shiva agrees to help Kasiraja in this conflict. Skanda Purana 2.2.12.17-18\n,\n”Nila mountain is in the third Yojana (i.e. 3X12 Kms.). This is the holy spot of the Lord of Gauri named Ekamrakavana. Not far off, O king, is the place where, being afraid, he sought refuge. Indradyumna said: Why was the Lord of Gauri (Siva) frightened? With whom did he seek refuge\nSkanda Purana 2.2.12.45-57\n,\n”O king, many king ruled over that city. Formerly in Dvapara Yuga, there was a king there (commonly) called Kasiraja. By means of severe penance he propitiated Lord Sambhu with this aim in his mind: ‘I will excel in war Acyuta (Krsna), the conquerer of kings, the chief of whom is Jaraasandha.’ The Pinaka-bearing Lord (Siva) who was propitiated, granted him that boon: ‘O suppressor of enemies, you will conquer the Slayer of Kamsa in battle. For your sake I shall fight seated on my Bull, along with (my attendants) Pramathas…That Lord (Krsna) who is the immanent soul (of all), knew the incident of that sort, and sent his Discus for killing Kasiraja. The infuriated Discus that was very fierce in appearance, had the refulgence of a thousand suns. It knew the power of the mind of Visnu. It cut off the head of Kasiraja and burned to ash his army as well as that city. On seeing that extremely violent action Pasupati (Siva) became furious. Surrounded by his Ganas and seated on his Bull, the Pinaka-bearing Lord rushed at it. Then Sambhu looked at the Sudarsana Discus at the outset and discharged his Pasupata missile in front of it, like an ominous calamity. Formerly Sambhu had secured a boon from Visnu who had been pleased by his devotion: ‘On being remembered by you I shall invigorate your missile. But if you go against me, it will become lustreless (and ineffective.’ When this Pasupata missile which was (usually) terrible, became futile and when Varanis was burned, the Bull-bannered Lord became afraid. Then he eulogized the Primordial Purusottama, the cause of all the worlds.”"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #gods-fighting-each-other","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1530161197452628039"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Shiva Purana 3.23.3-12 , ”Then the bull attacked Visnu’s sons wielding their bows for fighting, deluded by Siva’s Mäyä and proud of their great strength and exploit.","more":{"h":"Shiva Purana 3.23.3-12","p":["Shiva Purana 3.23.3-12\n,\n”Then the bull attacked Visnu’s sons wielding their bows for fighting, deluded by Siva’s Mäyä and proud of their great strength and exploit. O excellent sage, the sons of Visnu became furious. Those heroes roared loudly and rushed against Siva. Rudra in that form of a bull (Vrsabha) was furious at those sons of Visnu who rushed at him. He kicked them with his hoof’s and tore them with his horns. When their limbs were split by Rudra, they swooned and lost their lives. They were immediately destroyed. When they were killed Visnu the foremost of the strons came our spousns ouary and hastened towards Siva. On seeing Siva in the form of the bull going along after killing his sons, Visnu hit him with divine arrows and missiles. Then the infuriated Siva, the highly powerful one in the form of a bull stood like a mountain and caught hold of all those missiles of Visnu. O sage, shouting furiously, lord Siva in the form of a bin shook the three worlds terribly. The lord leaped up suddenly and kicked the infuriated Visnu who was deluded and could not realise him. The lord then tore him with his horns. Unable to bear the onslaught, Visnu deluded by Maya was exhausted and utterly shattered.”"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #gods-fighting-each-other","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1530161197452628039"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"— Vishnu Vs Other Gods , the gods, either accidentally or deliberately, severed the head of Vishnu.","more":{"h":"Gods fighting each other","p":["—","Vishnu Vs Other Gods\n,\nthe gods, either accidentally or deliberately, severed the head of Vishnu. The incident unfolded as Vishnu slumbered with his head resting at the end of a bow. Seeking a peculiar solution, the gods struck a deal with white ants, convincing them to gnaw at the bowstring. However, the unintended consequence was the severing of Vishnu’s head in the process.","Shatapatha Brahmana 14.1.1.6-9\n,\n”Now he who is this Vishnu is the sacrifice; and he who is this sacrifice is yonder Aditya (the sun). But, indeed, Vishnu was unable to control that (love of) glory of his; and so even now not every one can control that (love of) glory of his. Taking his bow, together with three arrows, he stepped forth. He stood, resting his head on the end of the bow. Not daring to attack him, the gods sat themselves down all around him. Then the ants said-these ants (vamri), doubtless, were that (kind called) ‘upadikä ‘-‘What would ye give to him who should gnaw the bowstring?’-‘We would give him the (constant) enjoyment of food, and he would find water even in the desert: so we would give him every enjoyment of food. ‘So be it, they said. Having gone nigh unto him, they gnawed his bowstring. When it was cut, the ends of the bow, springing asunder, cut off Vishnu’s head.” \nSatapatha Brahmana Part V (SBE44): Fourteenth Kâ&lt... | Internet ...\nSatapatha Brahmana Part V (SBE44): Fourteenth Kâ&lt... | Internet ...\nHinduism: most excellent of the gods; whence people say, 'Vish"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #gods-fighting-each-other","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1530161197452628039"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Devi Bhagavatam Purana 1.5.23-36 , ”Brahmā said :– We will give you, too, share in this our Yajña (sacrifice); so hear me; do our work and rouse Viṣṇu from His sleep.","more":{"h":"Devi Bhagavatam Purana 1.5.23-36","p":["Devi Bhagavatam Purana 1.5.23-36\n,\n”Brahmā said :– We will give you, too, share in this our Yajña (sacrifice); so hear me; do our work and rouse Viṣṇu from His sleep. During the time of performing Homa whatever ghee will fall outside the Homa-Kund (the sacrificial pit) will fall to your share; so be quick and do this. Sūta said :– Thus ordered by Brahmā, the Vamrī insect soon ate away the fore end of the bow that rested on the ground. Immediately the string gave way and the bow went up; the other end became free and a terrible sound took place. The Devas bcame afraid; the whole universe got agitated; the earth trembled. The sea became swollen; the aquatic animals became startled; violent wind blew; the mountains shook; ominous meteors fell. The quarters assumed a terrific aspect; the Sun went down the horizon. In that time of distress the Devas became anxious what evil might come down. O ascetics! while the Devas were thus cogitating, the head with crown on it of the Devadeva Viṣṇu vanished away ; no body knew where it fell. When the awful darkness disappeared, Brahmā and Mahādeva saw the disfigured body of Viṣṇu with its head off. Seeing that headless figure of Viṣṇu they were greatly surprised; they were drowned in the ocean of cares and, overwhelmed with grief, began to weep aloud.”"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #gods-fighting-each-other","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1530161197452628039"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#gods-fighting-each-other)."}});
topic(["other","hinduism","d-ia-caste-system-vs-islamic-governance"],{"title":"Caste system vs islamic governance","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"Caste system vs islamic governance","tree":{"they":"Caste system vs islamic governance","we":"The presence of the caste system in Hindu texts is not unknown.","more":{"h":"Caste system vs islamic governance","p":["The presence of the caste system in Hindu texts is not unknown. There are many references to it, as you can see on this website: https://hinduscript.com/caste-system-in-hinduism/#41_Punishment_for_a_Shudra_who_Teaches_Dharma_to_the_Upper_Castes","You see Hindus nowadays use various ways to defend the caste system. One of them is saying that it is based on varna, which, according to this argument, would mean it is based on your qualities or occupation. So, for example, if you wished to be a businessman or merchant, you would belong to the Vaishya varna. Some of them argue that the birth-based caste system was never part of Hinduism.","But again, as you can see from verses like Chandogya Upanishad 5.10.7, there are clearly texts that connect social status and caste with birth:","\"Those whose conduct has been good, will quickly attain some good birth, the birth of a Brahmana, or a Kshatriya, or a Vaisya. But those whose conduct has been evil, will quickly attain an evil birth, the birth of a dog, or a hog, or a Kandala.\"","You will often see Hindus avoid addressing verses related to a birth-based system and instead point to other verses to argue that the system was not based on birth. However, they do not always provide an explanation for the verses that appear to support a birth-based system.","This is one of the major issues that needs to be addressed when discussing the caste system in Hinduism. It is not enough to point to passages that support a qualities-based interpretation while ignoring passages that connect social status with birth. Once again it shows contradiction in hindu text which happens a lot.","Of course, when they cannot defend the issue as easily, some Hindus will bring up criticisms of Islam, sometimes using anti-Muslim websites or sources such as Sunnah.com to find hadiths that they can use to create anti-Islamic arguments.","Once they realize that the caste system cannot be defended that easily, some will turn the argument toward the Islamic Caliphate and try to argue that Islam promotes a caste system. One reference they may use is a hadith about leadership being among Quraysh or about the leadership of Quraysh. Sahih Muslim 1818a and Sahih Muslim 1820","However, these arguments ignore the broader context of the hadiths, including other narrations concerning the Caliphate and Quraysh.","This is not a problem for us because the Caliphate is a political institution involving the position of the ruler. It is not a complete social system in which only Quraysh can hold high positions in society. Comparing this to the caste system is therefore a false comparison.","The caste system involves social divisions that can affect a person's status, occupation, marriage, social treatment, and other aspects of life, with birth playing a major role in determining a person's caste.","The Caliphate, on the other hand, is primarily a form of political leadership. A ruler being from Quraysh does not mean that every Muslim is assigned a social class at birth with different rights, occupations, and social status.","Hindus may go further and argue about the status of dhimmis in Islamic societies, claiming that they were treated differently from Muslims. You can read more about this here: https://www.call-to-monotheism.com/the_status_of_non_muslims_in_the_islamic_state","However, none of this makes it equivalent to the caste system.","The caste system is fundamentally a system of hereditary social divisions and inequality that can affect people not only through certain laws, but also through occupations, social status, marriage, and many other aspects of life.","InshaAllah, I will add more to this. \nCaste System In Hinduism\nCaste System In Hinduism\nCaste System In Hinduism List Of Articles 1. Introduction Caste system is one of the evils of Hindu religion that still exists in society. It serves to isolate the low castes, creating divisions within the Hindu community. The condition of low caste people has been unfortunate, as they faced Brahminical oppression throughout history. The Untouch...\nThe Status of Non-Muslims In the Islamic State\nThe Status of Non-Muslims In the Islamic State\nIt is about Islamic apologetics and refuting Christianity and deviant Muslim sects. It is also about learning Islam."],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #caste-system-vs-islamic-governance","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1546832223188033537"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#caste-system-vs-islamic-governance)."}});
topic(["islam","sects","d-ia-mirza-ghulam-ahmad"],{"title":"Mirza ghulam ahmad","k":"Islamic Apologetics","blurb":"2 threads","children":{"t-when-did-the-worship-of-jesus-begin":{"title":"When did the worship of Jesus begin?","k":"IA","blurb":"1 post from Discord","article":{"claim":"When did the worship of Jesus begin?","tree":{"they":"When did the worship of Jesus begin?","we":"The only response to this is that since jesus traveled to kashmir, he was \"no longer with them to correct them\" But the problem is that the verse is pretty clear \"When i was among them\" indexes back to \"when you caused m…","more":{"h":"When did the worship of Jesus begin?","p":["The only response to this is that since jesus traveled to kashmir, he was \"no longer with them to correct them\"","But the problem is that the verse is pretty clear","\"When i was among them\" indexes back to \"when you caused me to die\"","The plain reading is with us","If \"tawaffi\" can mean \"traveled\" instead of \"death\", then why can't it mean \"traveled upwards\" like us sunnis claim?","some guy tried to refute me, check this thread of mine for the answer: https://x.com/misbah_bangee/status/2118303985170001921 \n@SpreadHaqq Nice tactic to portray me in bad light.","Its not my problem that u guys (minority) counts bismillah as a verse too","Leave that","Appart from the fact that the verse is pretty clear","I agree with Mirza ghulam ahmad","And you don't","U cooked urself"],"imgs":1,"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #mirza-ghulam-ahmad › When did the worship of Jesus begin?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1562354756331110490"},"next":[]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#mirza-ghulam-ahmad)."}},"t-mirza-ghulam-ahamad-a-prophet":{"title":"Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","k":"IA","blurb":"5 posts from Discord","article":{"claim":"Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","tree":{"they":"Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","we":"Founder : Mirza Ghulam Ahmad Qadiani, born in 1265 AH in Qadian.","more":{"h":"founder : Mirza Ghulam Ahmad Qadiani, born in 1265 AH in Qadian.","p":["founder : Mirza Ghulam Ahmad Qadiani, born in 1265 AH in Qadian.\nMirza began his activity as an Islamic preacher, then claimed to be a reformer and inspired by God, then he progressed to another level and claimed to be the awaited Mahdi and the promised Messiah. He says in this regard: “Muslims and Christians believe, with slight differences, that Jesus, son of Mary, was raised to heaven in his physical body, and that he will descend from heaven in some era. I have proven in my book that this is a false belief, and I have explained that what is meant by the descent is not the descent of the Messiah, but rather it is a metaphorical announcement of the coming of someone like the Messiah, and that this incapable one - meaning himself - is the confirmation of this news according to the announcement and inspiration”!!","Then he moved from claiming to be the likeness and similarity of Christ, peace be upon him, to claiming that he is Christ himself, saying: “This is the awaited Jesus, and what is meant by Mary and Jesus in the inspired phrases is none other than me.” Since Christ was a prophet to whom revelation was sent, Mirza claimed that revelation was sent to him, and he wrote a Qur’an for himself which he called “The Clear Book,” saying: “I am on clear guidance from a generous Lord. God sent me at the beginning of the century to renew the religion, illuminate the face of the nation, break the cross, extinguish the fire of Christianity, establish the Sunnah of the best of creation, fix what has been corrupted, and promote what has been stagnant. I am the promised Messiah and the promised Mahdi. God has bestowed upon me revelation and inspiration, and He spoke to me as He spoke to the noble messengers"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #mirza-ghulam-ahmad › Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1562354756331110490"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"It seems that the claim that he was the Messiah did not receive the desired acceptance, nor did it achieve the hoped-for purpose.","more":{"h":"Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","p":["It seems that the claim that he was the Messiah did not receive the desired acceptance, nor did it achieve the hoped-for purpose. So he moved from the claim that he was the Messiah the Prophet to the claim that he was Muhammad the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and that the Muhammadan reality had been embodied in him, and that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had been sent again in the person of Mirza Ghulam. Mirza says: “God sent Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, again in Qadian to fulfill His promise.” He said: “The Promised Messiah is Muhammad, the Messenger of God, and he has come to the world again to spread Islam.” Then he claimed that his prophethood was higher and more sublime than the prophethood of our master Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was followed by those who followed him from among the rabble, the mob, the ignorant, and the worldly interests"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #mirza-ghulam-ahmad › Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1562354756331110490"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Examples of his confusion : Despite those broad claims that Mirza made for himself, he was naive, obscene, and foul-mouthed, hurling the most vile insults and curses at his opponents!","more":{"h":"Examples of his confusion :","p":["Examples of his confusion :\nDespite those broad claims that Mirza made for himself, he was naive, obscene, and foul-mouthed, hurling the most vile insults and curses at his opponents!","As for the revelation he claimed for himself, it was a mixture of scattered verses that he collected into inconsistent passages, indicating his lack of understanding and comprehension of the Qur'an. Here are some examples of his alleged revelation: He said, \"I was inspired just now, while commenting on this marginal note, in March 1882, with the following exact words: 'O Ahmad, may God bless you, and you did not throw when you threw, but it was God who threw. The Most Merciful taught the Qur'an, that you may warn a people whose forefathers were not warned, and that the way of the criminals may become clear. Say, \"I have been commanded, and I am the first of the believers.\" Say, \"The truth has come, and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is ever bound to vanish.\"' etc.\" He also says, \"And by God, it is the essence of the eloquence of the Qur'an, to be a sign for a people who ponder. Do you say I am a thief? Then bring forth stolen pages like it in adherence to truth and wisdom, if you are truthful!\"","As for his prophecies, they are numerous and quick to come true, but contrary to what he foretold and informed. Among them is that he debated a Christian, and the Christian refuted him. When Mirza could not answer him, he became angry with the Christian and wanted to erase the shame of his defeat. So he claimed that the Christian would die - if he did not repent - after fifteen months, according to what God had revealed to him. The appointed time came, and the Christian did not die. So the Qadianis claimed that the Christian had repented and turned back to God. However, when the Christian heard that claim, he wrote to refute them and boast of his Christianity"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #mirza-ghulam-ahmad › Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1562354756331110490"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"Among his claims was that the plague would not enter his town of Qadian as long as he was there, even if the plague lasted for seventy years.","more":{"h":"Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","p":["Among his claims was that the plague would not enter his town of Qadian as long as he was there, even if the plague lasted for seventy years. God proved him wrong, and the plague entered Qadian and killed its people, and he died from it. He is the one who said, “And a sign for him is that God gave him glad tidings that the plague would not enter his house, and that earthquakes would not destroy him and his supporters, and God would ward off their evil from his house.”","Qadiani beliefs :","Qadianism believes in the transmigration of souls: Mirza claimed that Abraham, peace be upon him, was born two thousand and fifty years later in the house of Abdullah bin Abdul-Muttalib, embodied in the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was sent twice more, one of which was when the Muhammadan reality came into being in the perfect follower, meaning himself.\n,","They believe that God fasts, prays, sleeps, and makes mistakes. God is far above what they say. Mirza says: “God said to me: I pray, fast, wake up, and sleep.” He also said: “God said: I am with the Messenger, I answer, I make mistakes, and I am right. I am with the Messenger, encompassing\n,"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #mirza-ghulam-ahmad › Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1562354756331110490"},"next":[{"they":null,"we":"They believe that prophethood was not sealed with Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, but is ongoing, and that God sends messengers as needed, and that Ghulam Ahmad is the best of all the prophets!!","more":{"h":"Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","p":["They believe that prophethood was not sealed with Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, but is ongoing, and that God sends messengers as needed, and that Ghulam Ahmad is the best of all the prophets!! And that Gabriel, peace be upon him, used to descend upon Ghulam Ahmad with revelation, and that his inspirations are like the Qur’an.\n,","They say: There is no Qur’an except that which was presented by the Promised Messiah (Ghulam), and no Hadith except that which is in light of his teachings, and no Prophet except under the authority of “Ghulam Ahmad”, and they believe that their book is revealed and its name is the Clear Book, and it is other than the Holy Qur’an!!\n,","They believe that they are the followers of a new, independent religion and an independent law, and that the companions of the boy are like the companions, as stated in their newspaper “Al-Fadl, Issue 92”: “There was no difference between the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the disciples of Mirza Ghulam Ahmad. Those were the men of the first mission and these are the men of the second mission.”\n,","They believe that the greatest pilgrimage is the pilgrimage to Qadian and visiting the grave of the Qadiani. They stated that there are three holy places: Mecca, Medina, and Qadian. It was stated in their newspaper: “The pilgrimage to Mecca without the pilgrimage to Qadian is a dry and barren pilgrimage, because the pilgrimage to Mecca does not fulfill its mission or achieve its purpose.”\n,","They permit alcohol, opium, and drugs!!\n,","Every Muslim is considered an infidel by them until he enters the Qadiani faith: Likewise, whoever marries or gives in marriage to someone other than the Qadianis is an infidel!!\n,","They call for the abolition of jihad and the obligation of blind obedience to the English government that was occupying India at that time, because - according to their claim - it is the guardian of the Muslims\n,"],"credit":"Islamic Apologetics · #mirza-ghulam-ahmad › Mirza ghulam ahamad a prophet?","link":"https://discord.com/channels/1514269918978248796/1562354756331110490"},"next":[]}]}]}]}]},"sum":"Notes from Islamic Apologetics (#mirza-ghulam-ahmad)."}}}});
